(1265, 13, 'Hanka', 'hanaevans@yahoo.co.uk', 'Ceska konverzace 26.-27.1.', 'Mili krajane,\r\ndovolim si sem vloudit se s nadeji, ze se mi postesti si po dlouhe dobe popovidat nazivo cesky.\r\nZiji 10 let v Cornwallu, (Penzance), kde by Cecha hledal jak jehlu v kupce sena. Ted jsem ale zacala pravidelne navstevovat pritele v Glasgove a s nadsenim jsem objevila the Czech bunch na vasi universite.\r\nMel by nekdo zajem se se mnou sejit u kavy a pomoci mi roztocit ceske rezavejici mozkove zavity, prosim? Moc bych to ocenila. Priste jsem v Glasgowe 27.a 28.ledna.\r\nJe mi 33, pracuji jako pecovatelka a vytvarnice.\r\nTake by me do budoucna zajimalo, jestli existuje (v Glasgowe) moznost zamestnani v ceske konverzaci - ne vyuky, protoze nejsem kvalifikovana ucitelka.\r\n\r\nMoc vam dekuji, budu se tesit na odpoved.\r\nHana Evansova', '2004-01-14 23:13:34', 0, 1),
(1266, 14, 'Paul Coupland', 'listopad21uk@yahoo.co.uk', 'Pomoc!', 'I\'m currently looking for employment in the Czech Republic, in particular Prague. This is proving difficult (as I thought it would be!)unless you want to teach English on a low wage. I\'ve sent my CV to various British companies based in the Czech Republic on an \'ad-hoc\' basis but haven\'t had much response.\r\n\r\nDoes anyone know of any good web-sites where I can search for work?\r\n\r\nMaybe you know someone who is looking for an English speaking employee (I do speak a little Czech and I\'m working hard to get fluent!). I have various skills mainly clerical/ retail/ customer service. For the last 7 years I\'ve worked for a major British airline. \r\n\r\nThankyou in advance to anyone who replies to this request!\r\n\r\nPaul ', '2004-01-16 19:34:00', 0, 1),
