(57, '', '<h3>Odpovězte na tyto otázky:</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Máte hodně nebo málo volného času?\r\n<li>Napite aspoň deset věcí, které děláte kadý týden, protoe musíte.\r\n<li>Co děláte, kdy se nudíte?\r\n<li>Jak vypadá vá týden dnes a jak by vypadal před sto lety? (Přečtěte si text písně <i>Těínská</i>)\r\n<li>Je pravda, e čas jsou peníze?\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\nNapite seznam slovíček a frází o volném čase.\r\n\r\n', 129, 0, 100),
(59, '', '<hr><i>Tato sekce obsahuje některé důleité materiály a odkazy (linky) na relevantní webové adresy.</i>\r\n<hr>', 142, 0, 9),
(56, '', '1.	Klady a zápory středního kolství ve Velké Británii a v České republice  <br>\r\n2.	Kulturní vývoj v České republice po roce 1989<br>\r\n3.	Václav Havel - dramatik vs. politik<br>\r\n4.	Internet jako prostředek globalizace<br>\r\n5.	Je Evropská unie nástrojem homogenizace kultur a etnik?<br>\r\n6.	Kniha vs. televize, kino a video<br>\r\n7.	\"Miluj pravdu, haj pravdu, prav pravdu a do smrti.\" (Jan Hus) - česká společnost ve 21. století a její morální a etická měřítka.<br>\r\n8.		\"Pouhá 4% z bohatství shromáděného 225 nejmovitějími osobami planety by údajně stačila k zajitění základních existenčních a sociálních poadavků (základní výiva, přístup ke vzdělání, zdravotní péče) pro vekerou populaci.\"<br>Celosvětová zpráva OSN o rozvoji lidstva 1998<br>\r\n9.	\"Úskalím fungování justice a státní správy v České republice byla a je korupce. Zprávy EU to setrvale konstatují. V nedávném hodnocení auditorské firmy PriceWaterhouse-Coopers se z 35 evropských zemí Česká republika ocitla na třetím místě od konce!\" <br>\r\n	(Václav ák, Britské listy 7. 6. 2002)<br>\r\n10.	Historie národa jako prostředek pochopení jeho vývoje.\r\n', 140, 0, 100),
(61, '', '<hr>\r\n<i><center>Zde je několik relevantních linků na jiných webech. Bohuel jsou větinou v angličtině.</center></i>\r\n<hr>\r\n', 142, 0, 50);
 identity over the personal one (p. 63)? In what sense can the little Czech still be said to lack individuation (p. 62)?<o:p></o:p></SPAN></LI>\r\n<LI class=MsoNormal style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt; mso-list: l5 level1 lfo18; tab-stops: list 36.0pt\"><SPAN style=\"mso-ansi-language: EN-US\">Hol</SPAN><SPAN lang=CS>ý </SPAN><SPAN style=\"mso-ansi-language: EN-US\">repeatedly mentions collectivism as an implicitly explanatory term. How would his definition of collectivism compare with that described by Ward at al. for the Collectivism-Individualism continuum (Ward at al., The Psychology of Culture Shock, 2001, pp. 11  17). How can these theories account for such phenomena as the collectivist Czechs reluctance to engage in teamwork as reported by many Western managers, on one hand, and the individualist Americans slogan There is no I in team, on the other?<o:p></o:p></SPAN></LI>\r\n<LI class=MsoNormal style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt; mso-list: l5 level1 lfo18; tab-stops: list 36.0pt\"><SPAN style=\"mso-ansi-language: EN-US\">As an ideology, nationalism is totalizing in stressing the collectivity united in a common purpose; democratic ideology is pluralistic. (p. 70) Is Hol</SPAN><SPAN lang=CS>ý </SPAN><SPAN style=\"mso-ansi-language: EN-US\">making living up to his original commitment not to engage in the interpretation of history in this statement? <o:p></o:p></SPAN></LI>\r\n<LI class=MsoNormal style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt; mso-list: l5 level1 lfo18; tab-stops: list 36.0pt\"><SPAN style=\"mso-ansi-language: EN-US\">Compare this statement: Democracy (in CEE after 1989) was not understood as a political system, or a political and social arrangement or process, or as a political culture. Rather the concept was employed rhetorically, its definition gaining meaning only in relation to what is perceived as its opposite, or negation, that is, totalitarianism. </SPAN><SPAN lang=CS>(<SPAN class=articletitle>Little Czechs, Big Europe, </SPAN><SPAN class=articletopauthor>Jiří Brodský, 1999 at <A href=\"http://www.ce-review.org/00/20/brodsky20.html\">http://www.ce-review.org/00/20/brodsky20.html</A>) with Holýs </SPAN></SPAN><SPAN class=articletopauthor><SPAN style=\"mso-ansi-language: EN-US\">description of the nation-state: The freedom of the nation and the freedom of individuals become synonymous. A nation-state cannot be repressive and still serve the nations interest. (p. 71) How does the Czech concept of democracy identified by Hol</SPAN><SPAN lang=CS>ý </SPAN></SPAN><SPAN class=articletopauthor><SPAN style=\"mso-ansi-language: EN-US\">as coterminous with freedom (p. 70) fit into this picture?</SPAN></SPAN><SPAN style=\"mso-ansi-language: EN-US\"><o:p></o:p></SPAN></LI>\r\n<LI class=MsoNormal style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt; mso-list: l5 level1 lfo18; tab-stops: list 36.0pt\"><SPAN style=\"mso-ansi-language: EN-US\"><A href=\"http://www.new-presence.cz/98/04/czech.htm\">Read</A> (<A href=\"http://www.new-presence.cz/98/04/czech.htm\">http://www.new-presence.cz/98/04/czech.htm</A>) the views of Czech students on the issue of Czechness and identify elements of Czech national identity described by Hol</SPAN><SPAN lang=CS>ý </SPAN><SPAN style=\"mso-ansi-language: EN-US\">thus far. Compare this with views <A href=\"http://www.pcv.cz/home/adamec/czech/balances.html\">expressed by Benjamin Kuras</A>. (<A href=\"http://www.pcv.cz/home/adamec/czech/balances.html\">http://www.pcv.cz/home/adamec/czech/balances.html</A>)<o:p></o:p></SPAN></LI>\r\n<LI class=MsoNormal style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt; mso-list: l5 level1 lfo18; tab-stops: list 36.0pt\"><SPAN style=\"mso-ansi-language: EN-US\">Create a question the answer to which will best summarize your understanding of the texts.<o:p></o:p></SPAN></LI></OL>', 189, 0, 100),
(88, '', '<h3>Monday</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Review of verb conjugation (workbook p. 10-11)\r\n<li>Review of nationalities (pictures of world leaders)\r\n<li>Introducing direct object (Textbook p. 32-33)\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3>Tuesday</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Review of verbs with accusative\r\n<li>Arrangin sentences\r\n<li>Listening (p. 37)\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3>Wednesday</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>First progress test (all done so far up  to accusative)\r\n<li>Review of spelling rules, capitalization\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3>Thursday</h3>\r\nLecture via videoconference from Prague. Prof. Karel Kučera of Charles University gave a presentation on some of the differences between Czech and English from the grammatical, cultural and historical perspectives.\r\n\r\n<font color=white> <li>Doing things at the moment\r\n<li>Verbs <i>znát, vědět, umět</i> - states and repetitions</font>\r\n', 177, 0, 100),
(155, '', '<h2>Pondělí</h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Reviewing apartment (p. 121)\r\n<li>Introducing locative 139-140\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h2>Úterý</h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Review of locative - find locative in text\r\n<li>Introducing future tense and aspect\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h2>Středa</h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Progress test\r\n<li>Aspect verb pairs (three types of pairs and prefixes) Textbook pp. 144-150.\r\n</ul>', 242, 0, 100),
(27, '', '<b>Note:</b> No additional fonts are necessary for Windows 98 and later (ME, 2000, XP). ', 46, 0, 1),
(29, '', 'Many of the portals and search engines <a href=?m=catalog&s=50>listed separately</a> also contain news headlines.', 57, 0, 1),
(92, '', '<h3>Fráze a gramatika k tématu <i>čas</i></h3>\r\n<P>\r\n<H4>Idiomy k času</H4>\r\n<P></P>\r\n<TABLE align=default border=0 cellPadding=0 cellSpacing=0 width=\"100%\">\r\n<TBODY>\r\n<TR>\r\n<TD>\r\n<P> </P></TD>\r\n<TD><EM>pro</EM></TD>\r\n<TD>kamaráda, tebe</TD></TR>\r\n<TR>\r\n<TD><STRONG>mít čas</STRONG></TD>\r\n<TD><EM>na</EM></TD>\r\n<TD>kamarády, procházky, čte<STRONG>ní</STRONG>, psa<STRONG>ní, </STRONG>vaře<STRONG>ní</STRONG></TD></TR>\r\n<TR>\r\n<TD></TD>\r\n<TD><EM>, aby</EM></TD>\r\n<TD>mohl kadý den něco dělat</TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE>\r\n<P></P>\r\n<P><STRONG>trvat </STRONG>- <EM>Cesta do Londýna trvá dvě hodiny.</EM></P>\r\n<P><STRONG>trávit/strávit </STRONG>- <EM>V Praze jsme strávili celý týden. / Dovolenou obvykle trávíme ve panělsku.</EM></P>\r\n<P><STRONG>trávit čas </STRONG>- <EM>Trávím moc času v hospodě.</EM></P>\r\n<P><STRONG>zabírat čas</STRONG> - <EM>Vaření zabírá moc času.</EM></P>\r\n<P><STRONG>udělat si čas na </STRONG>- <EM>Na kamarády si vdycky udělám čas.</EM></P>\r\n<P><STRONG>čas chybí na </STRONG>- <EM>Chybí mi čas na domácí úkoly.</EM></P>\r\n<P><strong>najít si čas </strong>- <em>Na dobrou knihu si rád trochu času najdu.</em></p>\r\n<H4>Adverbia k času</H4>\r\n<P>zřídka, zřídkakdy, málokdy, kadý druhý den, nejvíc, nejčastěji, moc času, obvykle, někdy, výjimečně</P>\r\n<P>\r\n<H4>Aktivity</H4>\r\n<P></P>\r\n<P>uklízet, chodit na procházku, číst si, nudit se, scházet se s přáteli, chodit na kurz tanců, telefonovat s rodinou, jezdit na výlety do přírody (na venkov)</P>', 129, 0, 100),
(93, '', '<hr>\r\nInformace pro zpracování otázek k tomuto tématu větinou najdete na internetu. Nejdůleitějí odkazy jsou níe. Dalí můete najít v sekci <a href=http://www.bohemica.com/links>Links na Bohemica.com</a>. A budete hledat informace o jednotlivých politicích, podívejte se také do novin. Lidové Noviny, Mladá Fronta Dnes i Respekt mají na internetu volně přístupné archívy zpráv za posledních 10 let.\r\n<hr>', 178, 0, 100),
(167, '', '\r\nThis is an aligned corpus of translations between Czech and English. The total is just under 100,000 words. It consists of 24 samples between 1000 and 4000 words. The texts are equally from two broad genres: fiction and not-fiction.\r\n\r\n<p>The corpus is aligned by paragraph &lt; p &gt; and sentences are marked by &lt; s &gt;. The texts are separated using the COCOA format. The files have been tested to work with <a href=\"http://www.athel.com/para.html\">Paraconc</a> (Version 1 BETA build 233).\r\n\r\n</p><p>\r\n<b>Corpus for download:</b> <a href=\"corpus/corpus.zip\">Corpus.zip</a><br />\r\n<i>Right-click and use Save as.</i></p><p>\r\n\r\nFeel free to use this for research purposes but be aware that it is a compromise of time and availability. <b>Anybody wishing to contribute texts (samples of up to 4000 words, preferably aligned) to make the corpus more balanced will be welcome with open arms.</b> A great free tool for aligning and tagging parallel texts is PlusTools, a companion application to <a href=\"http://www.wordfast.net\">WordFast</a>. The commercial version of <a href=\"http://www.athel.com\">Paraconc</a> also comes with a tool for aligning texts.\r\n\r\n</p><p>\r\nThe work started with a pilot corpus of 8000 words (8 texts at 500 words of source language). This is still useful for those who need to go through texts in more detail rather than searching for set expressions. Both text files aligned for Paraconc and a paragraph aligned Word file are available. I used this pilot corpus in writing parts of <a href=\"/index.php?m=catalog&s=14&a=132\">a chapter comparing cohesion in Czech and English</a>.\r\n</p><p>\r\n<b>Pilot corpus for download:</b> <a href=\"corpus/pilotcorpus.zip\">Pilotcorpus.zip</a><br />\r\n\r\n\r\n</p><p>\r\nMore information on the main corpus including detailed info on text samples forthcoming. Here are the basic numbers:\r\n\r\n</p><p>\r\n\r\n<table width=\"578\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" border=\"1\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; table-layout: fixed; width: 434pt;\">\r\n <col width=\"137\" style=\"width: 103pt;\" />\r\n <col width=\"64\" span=\"3\" style=\"width: 48pt;\" />\r\n <col width=\"88\" span=\"2\" style=\"width: 66pt;\" />\r\n <col width=\"73\" style=\"width: 55pt;\" />\r\n <tbody><tr height=\"18\" style=\"height: 13.2pt;\">\r\n  <td width=\"137\" height=\"18\" class=\"xl2414272\" style=\"height: 13.2pt; width: 103pt;\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n  <td width=\"64\" class=\"xl2414272\" style=\"border-left: medium none; width: 48pt;\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n  <td width=\"64\" class=\"xl2414272\" style=\"border-left: medium none; width: 48pt;\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n  <td width=\"64\" class=\"xl2414272\" style=\"border-left: medium none; width: 48pt;\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n  <td width=\"88\" class=\"xl2414272\" style=\"border-left: medium none; width: 66pt;\">Czech Words</td>\r\n  <td width=\"88\" class=\"xl2414272\" style=\"border-left: medium none; width: 66pt;\">English\r\n  Words</td>\r\n  <td width=\"73\" class=\"xl2414272\" style=\"border-left: medium none; width: 55pt;\">Total words</td>\r\n </tr>\r\n <tr height=\"18\" style=\"height: 13.2pt;\">\r\n  <td height=\"18\" class=\"xl2514272\" style=\"border-top: medium none; height: 13.2pt;\">Total\r\n  texts</td>\r\n  <td class=\"xl2414272\" style=\"border-top: medium none; border-left: medium none;\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\" class=\"xl2414272\" style=\"border-top: medium none; border-left: medium none;\" x:fmla=\"=C7+C11\">24</td>\r\n  <td class=\"xl2414272\" style=\"border-top: medium none; border-left: medium none;\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\" class=\"xl2414272\" style=\"border-top: medium none; border-left: medium none;\" x:fmla=\"=E7+E11\">46079</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\" class=\"xl2414272\" style=\"border-top: medium none; border-left: medium none;\" x:fmla=\"=F11+F7\">53826</td>\r\n  <td align=\"right\" class=\"xl2514272\" style=\"border-top: medium none; border-left: medium none;\" x:fmla=\"=SUM(E2:F2