(119, '', '<P class=MsoTitle style=\"BORDER-RIGHT: medium none; PADDING-RIGHT: 0cm; BORDER-TOP: maroon; PADDING-LEFT: 0cm; PADDING-BOTTOM: 0cm; MARGIN: 12pt 0cm 3pt; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; PADDING-TOP: 0cm; BORDER-BOTTOM: maroon; mso-border-top-alt: thin-thick-small-gap maroon 4.5pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid maroon .5pt; mso-padding-alt: 5.0pt 0cm 3.0pt 0cm\" align=center><SPAN lang=EN-GB style=\"FONT-SIZE: 20pt; COLOR: navy; mso-ansi-language: EN-GB; mso-bidi-font-size: 16.0pt\"><STRONG><FONT face=Arial>Attention all students!!!<?xml:namespace prefix = o ns = \"urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office\" /><o:p></o:p></FONT></STRONG></SPAN></P>\r\n<P class=MsoNormal style=\"MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: center\" align=center><SPAN lang=EN-GB style=\"FONT-SIZE: 14pt; TEXT-TRANSFORM: uppercase; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-ansi-language: EN-GB; mso-bidi-font-size: 10.0pt\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></SPAN></P>\r\n<P class=MsoNormal style=\"MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: center\" align=center><B><SPAN lang=EN-GB style=\"FONT-SIZE: 14pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-ansi-language: EN-GB; mso-bidi-font-size: 10.0pt\">Department Of Slavonic Studies<o:p></o:p></SPAN></B></P>\r\n<P class=MsoNormal style=\"MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: center\" align=center><B><SPAN lang=EN-GB style=\"FONT-SIZE: 14pt; TEXT-TRANSFORM: uppercase; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-ansi-language: EN-GB; mso-bidi-font-size: 10.0pt\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></SPAN></B></P>\r\n<P class=MsoNormal style=\"MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: center\" align=center><B><SPAN lang=EN-GB style=\"FONT-SIZE: 14pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-ansi-language: EN-GB; mso-bidi-font-size: 10.0pt\">Proudly presents<o:p></o:p></SPAN></B></P>\r\n<P class=MsoNormal style=\"MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: center\" align=center><SPAN lang=EN-GB style=\"FONT-SIZE: 11pt; TEXT-TRANSFORM: uppercase; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-ansi-language: EN-GB; mso-bidi-font-size: 10.0pt\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></SPAN></P>\r\n<H1 style=\"MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt\" align=center><FONT face=Arial><B><SPAN lang=EN-GB style=\"FONT-SIZE: 36pt; TEXT-TRANSFORM: none; COLOR: maroon; mso-bidi-font-size: 14.0pt\">Poetry Contest 2002</SPAN></B><B><SPAN lang=EN-GB style=\"FONT-SIZE: 36pt; COLOR: maroon; mso-bidi-font-size: 14.0pt\"><o:p></o:p></SPAN></B></FONT></H1>\r\n<P class=MsoNormal style=\"MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt\"><SPAN lang=EN-GB style=\"mso-ansi-language: EN-GB\"><o:p><FONT size=2>&nbsp;</FONT></o:p></SPAN></P>\r\n<DIV style=\"BORDER-RIGHT: windowtext 1pt solid; PADDING-RIGHT: 4pt; BORDER-TOP: windowtext 1pt solid; PADDING-LEFT: 4pt; PADDING-BOTTOM: 1pt; BORDER-LEFT: windowtext 1pt solid; PADDING-TOP: 1pt; BORDER-BOTTOM: windowtext 1pt solid; mso-border-alt: solid windowtext .5pt\">\r\n<P class=MsoNormal style=\"BORDER-RIGHT: medium none; PADDING-RIGHT: 0cm; BORDER-TOP: medium none; PADDING-LEFT: 0cm; PADDING-BOTTOM: 0cm; MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; PADDING-TOP: 0cm; BORDER-BOTTOM: medium none; mso-padding-alt: 1.0pt 4.0pt 1.0pt 4.0pt; mso-border-alt: solid windowtext .5pt\"><SPAN style=\"FONT-FAMILY: Arial\"><o:p><FONT size=2>&nbsp;</FONT></o:p></SPAN></P>\r\n<P class=MsoNormal style=\"BORDER-RIGHT: medium none; PADDING-RIGHT: 0cm; BORDER-TOP: medium none; PADDING-LEFT: 0cm; PADDING-BOTTOM: 0cm; MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt 18pt; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; TEXT-INDENT: -18pt; PADDING-TOP: 0cm; BORDER-BOTTOM: medium none; TEXT-ALIGN: justify; tab-stops: list 18.0pt; mso-padding-alt: 1.0pt 4.0pt 1.0pt 4.0pt; mso-border-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1\"><SPAN style=\"FONT-SIZE: 14pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-fareast-font-family: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 10.0pt\"><SPAN style=\"mso-list: Ignore\">1.<SPAN style=\"FONT: 7pt \'Times New Roman\'\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </SPAN></SPAN></SPAN><SPAN dir=ltr><SPAN style=\"FONT-SIZE: 14pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 10.0pt\">Choose any poem from the </SPAN></SPAN><SPAN lang=EN-GB style=\"FONT-SIZE: 14pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-ansi-language: EN-GB; mso-bidi-font-size: 10.0pt\">nine</SPAN><SPAN lang=EN-GB style=\"FONT-SIZE: 14pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 10.0pt\"> </SPAN><SPAN style=\"FONT-SIZE: 14pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 10.0pt\">presented (in Czech, Polish, Russian). One of the poems in each language was chosen specifically for Level 1 students.<o:p></o:p></SPAN></P>\r\n<P class=MsoNormal style=\"BORDER-RIGHT: medium none; PADDING-RIGHT: 0cm; BORDER-TOP: medium none; PADDING-LEFT: 0cm; PADDING-BOTTOM: 0cm; MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt 18pt; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; TEXT-INDENT: -18pt; PADDING-TOP: 0cm; BORDER-BOTTOM: medium none; TEXT-ALIGN: justify; tab-stops: list 18.0pt; mso-padding-alt: 1.0pt 4.0pt 1.0pt 4.0pt; mso-border-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1\"><SPAN style=\"FONT-SIZE: 14pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-fareast-font-family: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 10.0pt\"><SPAN style=\"mso-list: Ignore\">2.<SPAN style=\"FONT: 7pt \'Times New Roman\'\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </SPAN></SPAN></SPAN><SPAN dir=ltr><SPAN style=\"FONT-SIZE: 14pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 10.0pt\">Translate it into English.<o:p></o:p></SPAN></SPAN></P>\r\n<P class=MsoNormal style=\"BORDER-RIGHT: medium none; PADDING-RIGHT: 0cm; BORDER-TOP: medium none; PADDING-LEFT: 0cm; PADDING-BOTTOM: 0cm; MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt 18pt; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; TEXT-INDENT: -18pt; PADDING-TOP: 0cm; BORDER-BOTTOM: medium none; TEXT-ALIGN: justify; tab-stops: list 18.0pt; mso-padding-alt: 1.0pt 4.0pt 1.0pt 4.0pt; mso-border-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1\"><SPAN style=\"FONT-SIZE: 14pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-fareast-font-family: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 10.0pt\"><SPAN style=\"mso-list: Ignore\">3.<SPAN style=\"FONT: 7pt \'Times New Roman\'\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </SPAN></SPAN></SPAN><SPAN dir=ltr><SPAN style=\"FONT-SIZE: 14pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 10.0pt\">Submit your entry to the Departmental Office <B style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal\"><SPAN style=\"COLOR: #333399\">by </SPAN></B></SPAN></SPAN><?xml:namespace prefix = st1 ns = \"urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:smarttags\" /><st1:time Hour=\"17\" Minute=\"0\"><B style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal\"><SPAN style=\"FONT-SIZE: 14pt; COLOR: #333399; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 10.0pt\">5 p.m.</SPAN></B></st1:time><B style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal\"><SPAN style=\"FONT-SIZE: 14pt; COLOR: #333399; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 10.0pt\"> on</SPAN></B><SPAN style=\"FONT-SIZE: 14pt; COLOR: #333399; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 10.0pt\"> <B style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal\">Thursday 12 December</B></SPAN><SPAN style=\"FONT-SIZE: 14pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 10.0pt\">.<o:p></o:p></SPAN></P>\r\n<P class=MsoNormal style=\"BORDER-RIGHT: medium none; PADDING-RIGHT: 0cm; BORDER-TOP: medium none; PADDING-LEFT: 0cm; PADDING-BOTTOM: 0cm; MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt 18pt; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; TEXT-INDENT: -18pt; PADDING-TOP: 0cm; BORDER-BOTTOM: medium none; TEXT-ALIGN: justify; tab-stops: list 18.0pt; mso-padding-alt: 1.0pt 4.0pt 1.0pt 4.0pt; mso-border-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1\"><SPAN style=\"FONT-SIZE: 14pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-fareast-font-family: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 10.0pt\"><SPAN style=\"mso-list: Ignore\">4.<SPAN style=\"FONT: 7pt \'Times New Roman\'\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </SPAN></SPAN></SPAN><SPAN dir=ltr><SPAN style=\"FONT-SIZE: 14pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 10.0pt\">A jury will assess all the entries (anonymously) and nominate a winner for each of the languages.<o:p></o:p></SPAN></SPAN></P>\r\n<P class=MsoNormal style=\"BORDER-RIGHT: medium none; PADDING-RIGHT: 0cm; BORDER-TOP: medium none; PADDING-LEFT: 0cm; PADDING-BOTTOM: 0cm; MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt 18pt; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; TEXT-INDENT: -18pt; PADDING-TOP: 0cm; BORDER-BOTTOM: medium none; TEXT-ALIGN: justify; tab-stops: list 18.0pt; mso-padding-alt: 1.0pt 4.0pt 1.0pt 4.0pt; mso-border-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1\"><SPAN style=\"FONT-SIZE: 14pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-fareast-font-family: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 10.0pt\"><SPAN style=\"mso-list: Ignore\">5.<SPAN style=\"FONT: 7pt \'Times New Roman\'\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </SPAN></SPAN></SPAN><SPAN dir=ltr><SPAN style=\"FONT-SIZE: 14pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 10.0pt\">The best poems will be read out at the official ceremony.<o:p></o:p></SPAN></SPAN></P>\r\n<P class=MsoNormal style=\"BORDER-RIGHT: medium none; PADDING-RIGHT: 0cm; BORDER-TOP: medium none; PADDING-LEFT: 0cm; PADDING-BOTTOM: 0cm; MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; PADDING-TOP: 0cm; BORDER-BOTTOM: medium none; mso-padding-alt: 1.0pt 4.0pt 1.0pt 4.0pt; mso-border-alt: solid windowtext .5pt\"><o:p><FONT size=2>&nbsp;</FONT></o:p></P></DIV>\r\n<P class=MsoNormal style=\"MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt; TEXT-ALIGN: justify\"><SPAN style=\"FONT-SIZE: 14pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 10.0pt\"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></SPAN></P>\r\n<P class=MsoBodyText style=\"MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt\" align=center><FONT size=5><FONT face=Arial></FONT></FONT>&nbsp;</P>\r\n<P class=MsoBodyText style=\"MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt\" align=center><FONT size=5><FONT face=Arial></FONT></FONT>&nbsp;</P>\r\n<P class=MsoBodyText style=\"MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt\" align=center><FONT size=5><FONT face=Arial>The <B><SPAN style=\"COLOR: #333399\">official prize-giving ceremony</SPAN></B> will take place on <BR><B><SPAN style=\"COLOR: #333399\">18 December</SPAN></B><SPAN style=\"COLOR: #333399\">, </SPAN><st1:time Hour=\"14\" Minute=\"30\"><B><SPAN style=\"COLOR: #333399\">2.30 p.m.</SPAN></B></st1:time> <BR>all students, staff and friends are welcome.<o:p></o:p></FONT></FONT></P>\r\n<P class=MsoBodyText style=\"MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt\" align=center><o:p><FONT face=Arial size=5>&nbsp;</FONT></o:p></P>\r\n<P class=MsoBodyText style=\"MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt\" align=center><FONT size=5><FONT face=Arial>All the information on the contest including, <BR>the text of the poems for translation, is available on-line at <SPAN style=\"COLOR: #333399\"><A href=\"http://www.bohemica.com/poetrycontest\"><SPAN style=\"COLOR: #333399\">http://www.bohemica.com/poetrycontest</SPAN></A></SPAN></FONT></FONT><o:p></o:p></P>', 208, 0, 100),
(120, '', '<h3>Monday</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Review of půjdu, pojedu, chci jet (dělat): Create a story about Petr and his future weekend activities\r\n<li>Indefinite and negative pronouns, adjectives, adverbs (něco, nic,...) (2 translations of what and no)\r\n<li>Double negatives (\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3>Tuesday</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Review of vocabulary\r\n<li>Watching first unit of Mluvte s námi česky (Video course available at the Language Centre Library) See below for worksheet.\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>Wednesday</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Writing Czech address (textbook p. 57): <br>Titul, Jméno a přímení, <br>jméno ulice, číslo domu<br>PSČ, město\r\n<li>Looking up people\'s addresses on the internet using <a href=http://www.telefonnicislo.cz>Telefonní seznam</a> to find street name and <a href=http://www.cpost.cz>Česká pota</a> to find PSČ (Potovní směrovací číslo)\r\n<li><i>Jetě, jetě ne, u, u ne</i> - Textbook 62: 2, 64:3<br>\r\nVčera: Lenka jetě není studentka.<br>\r\nDnes: Lenka u je studentka.<br>\r\nZa 1 rok: Lenka je jetě studentka.<br>\r\nZa 4 roky: Lenka u není studentka.<br>\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>Thursday</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Review of past homework in Lekce 4\r\n<li>Answer questions about text: Koho má Petr v Olomouci?, Koho zná Petr na univerzitě? Koho má Petr ve Stránici?\r\n<li>Accusative plural of animate masculines (Textbook p. 58-59)\r\n</ul>', 209, 0, 100),
(121, '', '<h3>Monday</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Workbook: p. 24, ex. 5, 6\r\n<li>Textbook: finish exercises 1, 2 on page 63\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>Tuesday</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Catch up on exercises\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>Wednesday</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Workbook 25: 9 - focus on word order\r\n<li>Workbook 25: 10 - match nouns with appropriate adjectives (and the correct form)\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>Thursday</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Finish exercises in Workbook Lekce 4; Particularly 25-26: 11, 12\r\n<li>Finish exercises in Textbook Lekce 4\r\n</ul>', 210, 0, 100),
(122, '', 'Přečtěte si první dvě kapitoly <i>Nemocnice na kraji města</i> a zodpovězte tyto otázky:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Jaký obraz společnosti vykresluje Dietl\r\n<li>Jaké hodnoty vyvolávají pro Čechy pojmy: primář Sova, Cvach, trosmajer, Blaej, Alběta Čeňková\r\n<li>Jak si myslíte, e se příběh bude vyvíjet dál?\r\n<li>Česká televize připravuje pokračování seriálu v moderní době (<a href=http://www.lidovky.cz/claneknejlepsi.asp?r=nejlepsi&c=A020314_133534_nejlepsi_ttt>zde o tom píí Lidové Noviny</a>). Vyberte si jednu postavu a napite, jak si představujete její příběh v současné době (po 20ti letech).\r\n</ul>\r\nZamyslete se také nad tím:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Jakou roli hrály seriály v ivotě Čechů před rokem 1989?\r\n<li>Změnilo se od té doby jejich místo ve společnosti?\r\n<li>Jak je moné toto srovnat se situací v Británii?\r\n</ul>\r\nK tomu si přečtěte <a href=http://www.lidovky.cz/archiv.asp?r=ahorizont&c=L231A11D&d=04.10.2002>diskusi čtenářů v Lidových Novinách</a> a <a href=http://www.lidovky.cz/clanekrozhovory.asp?r=rozhovory&c=A020713_145048_rozhovory_pol>rozhovor s manelkou autora seriálu</a>.\r\n', 212, 0, 100),
(156, '', '<h2>Pondělí</h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Workbook 61: 1, 62: 2-3\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h2>Úterý</h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Complete tense/aspect chart in textbook on p. 145 - 146\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h2>Středa</h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Textbook 145-7: Complete chart\r\n<li>Textbook 148:2, 150-1: 6-7\r\n<li>Workbook 62: 4, 63: 5-6\r\n</ul>', 243, 0, 100),
(123, '', '<hr>\r\n<center><b>Further links are below</b></center>\r\n<hr>', 32, 0, 100),
(125, '', '<h3>Monday</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Listen to dialog on p. 68 and answer these questions:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Kdo volá?\r\n<li>Do jakého hotelu volá?\r\n<li>Na kdy si chce rezervovat pokoj?\r\n<li>Chce jednolůkový nebo dvoulůkový pokoj?\r\n<li>Má ten pokoj koupelnu?\r\n<li>Kolik stojí jedna noc?\r\n<li>Jaké číslo má jeho pokoj?\r\n<li>Musí platit hned?\r\n<li>Co jetě chce?\r\n</ul>\r\n<li>Modal verbs (p. 71)\r\n<li>Exercises (p. 73: 7 - 10)\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3>Tuesday</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Review of modal verbs (Textbook 72: 1)\r\n<li>Addressing people and the vocative (Textbook 71:2, 74:12) \r\n</ul>\r\n<h3>Wednesday</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Review of rules for addressing people (using business cards)\r\n<li>Listen to dialogue in the restaurant (3), read and answer questions about the text\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>Thursday</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Reading dialog\r\n<li>Mít rád(a, i); rád(a,i) dělat Textbook p. 74: 1 75: 1\r\n<li>Adverbs of quantity (moc, hodně, málo, trochu, dost) Textbook p. 75: 2\r\n</ul>', 214, 0, 100),
(126, '', '<h3>Monday</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Workbook 27: 1 - 3\r\n<li>Textbook 74: 11\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>Tuesday</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Workbook 28: 4, 5, 29: 8\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>Wednesday</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Read and translate the text\r\n<li>Workbook 32: 16\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>Thursday</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Finish all exercises on modal verbs assigned so far\r\n<li>Workbook 29: 9\r\n<li>Write in complete sentences 10 things you like and 10 things you like to do (and why)\r\n</ul>', 215, 0, 100),
(127, '', 'Připravte si odpovědi na tyto otázky. Jednu otázku zpracujte písemně:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Jak často se díváte ne televizi teď a jak často jste se na ni dívali dříve? Jak jste na tom ve srovnání s ostatními?\r\n<li>Jakou roli hraje televize v ivotě dnení společnosti?\r\n<li>Které význačné osobnosti dneka proslavila televize?\r\n<li>Jakou má podle vás televize souvislost s hlavními problémy dnení společnosti, jako jsou například <i>vzdělanost, kriminalita, soudrnost společenství, mezilidské vztahy, zájem občanů o politiku a věci veřejné</i>\r\n<li>Měla televize očekávaný negativní dopad na divadlo, film a umění veobecně?\r\n<li>Jak byste srovnali vliv televize s vlivem počítačů?\r\n<li>Přečtěte si rady Společnosti pro ochranu před televizí na <a href=http://www.joukl.cz/sot.htm>http://www.joukl.cz/sot.htm</a>. Souhlasíte s nimi?\r\n</ul>', 216, 0, 100),
(128, '', '<B>Questions to guide the reading and discussion of Holý, Chapters 5 and 6: National traditions and the political process and Nation and state in the context of Czech culture</B>\r\n<P>\r\n<OL style=\"MARGIN-TOP: 0cm\" type=1>\r\n<LI class=MsoNormal style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list 36.0pt\"><SPAN lang=CS>Holý</SPAN><SPAN style=\"mso-ansi-language: EN-US\"> suggests that once we begin to see politics as an aspect of the cultural system the paradox between standard preconditions for a successful revolution and the speed and thoroughness of the 1989 revolution disappears. Are the aspects of the cultural system he provides as an explanation sufficient to explain the difference? Compare this view with. <A href=\"http://www.ce-review.org/00/20/interview20_belohradsky.html\">B</A></SPAN><SPAN lang=CS><A href=\"http://www.ce-review.org/00/20/interview20_belohradsky.html\">ělohradský</A></SPAN><SPAN style=\"mso-ansi-language: EN-US\"><A href=\"http://www.ce-review.org/00/20/interview20_belohradsky.html\">s description</A> of what he calls the Czech inability to integrate the relative and contradictory nature of values into our national life as the key dimension of modernity. (p. 4 of printout)<?xml:namespace prefix = o ns = \"urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office\" /><o:p></o:p></SPAN></LI>\r\n<LI class=MsoNormal style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list 36.0pt\"><SPAN style=\"mso-ansi-language: EN-US\">What does </SPAN><SPAN lang=CS>Holý</SPAN><SPAN lang=CS style=\"mso-ansi-language: EN-US\"> </SPAN><SPAN style=\"mso-ansi-language: EN-US\">identify as typical of Czechs for the following discourses (both in chapters 5 and 6)? What sort of evidence does he need to justify his assertions? Does he present such evidence, if not, where could it be found? <o:p></o:p></SPAN></LI>\r\n<OL style=\"MARGIN-TOP: 0cm\" type=a>\r\n<LI class=MsoNormal style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt; mso-list: l0 level2 lfo1; tab-stops: list 72.0pt\"><SPAN style=\"mso-ansi-language: EN-US\">politics and economy<o:p></o:p></SPAN></LI>\r\n<LI class=MsoNormal style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt; mso-list: l0 level2 lfo1; tab-stops: list 72.0pt\"><SPAN style=\"mso-ansi-language: EN-US\">heroism vs. martyrdom<o:p></o:p></SPAN></LI>\r\n<LI class=MsoNormal style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt; mso-list: l0 level2 lfo1; tab-stops: list 72.0pt\"><SPAN style=\"mso-ansi-language: EN-US\">environment<o:p></o:p></SPAN></LI>\r\n<LI class=MsoNormal style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt; mso-list: l0 level2 lfo1; tab-stops: list 72.0pt\"><SPAN style=\"mso-ansi-language: EN-US\">gender<o:p></o:p></SPAN></LI>\r\n<LI class=MsoNormal style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt; mso-list: l0 level2 lfo1; tab-stops: list 72.0pt\"><SPAN style=\"mso-ansi-language: EN-US\">homeland and nation<o:p></o:p></SPAN></LI></OL>\r\n<LI class=MsoNormal style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list 36.0pt\"><SPAN style=\"mso-ansi-language: EN-US\">What is the role of key symbols and metaphors through which Czechs make sense of the world in which they live (p. 200)? How successful is </SPAN><SPAN lang=CS>Holý</SPAN><SPAN lang=CS style=\"mso-ansi-language: EN-US\"> </SPAN><SPAN style=\"mso-ansi-language: EN-US\">at using them to define the Czech national identity as a phenomenon on its own and how successful is he at pinpointing what sets the Czech national identity apart from others? Compare this approach with that of a metaphor as a projection between domains.<o:p></o:p></SPAN></LI>\r\n<LI class=MsoNormal style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list 36.0pt\"><SPAN style=\"mso-ansi-language: EN-US\">Compare the Czech view of a difference between patriotism (</SPAN><SPAN lang=CS>vlastenectví) </SPAN><SPAN style=\"mso-ansi-language: EN-US\">vs. nationalism (</SPAN><SPAN lang=CS>nacionalismus</SPAN><SPAN style=\"mso-ansi-language: EN-US\">) as described by Hol</SPAN><SPAN lang=CS>ý </SPAN><SPAN style=\"mso-ansi-language: EN-US\">(p. 189) with other conceptions of nationalism examined so far (Isaacs, Geertz, Hobsbawn).<o:p></o:p></SPAN></LI>\r\n<LI class=MsoNormal style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list 36.0pt\"><SPAN style=\"mso-ansi-language: EN-US\">[Only discussed if cross-cultural simulation is conducted.] Hol</SPAN><SPAN lang=CS>ý </SPAN><SPAN style=\"mso-ansi-language: EN-US\">reports Czech as saying that homeland is a country in which one knows the rules of appropriate behavior Reflect on the personal experience of the X-ians simulation and discuss the different dimensions of the importance of rules of behavior and their potential link to values and the construction of values.<o:p></o:p></SPAN></LI>\r\n<LI class=MsoNormal style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list 36.0pt\"><SPAN lang=CS>Holý </SPAN><SPAN style=\"mso-ansi-language: EN-US\">describes a more-European-than-though vision of European nationalism as an attitude, in which particular nationalistic ambitions are couched in terms what are ostensibly European values. Compare your personal view of the benefits and dangers of European integration with this description.<o:p></o:p></SPAN></LI>\r\n<LI class=MsoNormal style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list 36.0pt\"><SPAN style=\"mso-ansi-language: EN-US\">What in the readings was new, what was surprising and what provoked disagreement? What was not clear? What could be said to be the common theme of all this weeks readings?<o:p></o:p></SPAN></LI></OL>', 218, 0, 100),
(129, '', '<h3>Monday</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Review of mít rád\r\n<li>Different ways of saying to like, Textbook: 74-77, mít rád (generic liking, liking for substane), chutnat (liking the taste of a specific thing), líbit se (liking the surface appearance, liking a specific object)\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>Tuesday</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Practicing different ways of saying \'to like\'\r\n<li>Asking questions about like (survey activity)\r\n<li>Use of the modal verb: \'mít\' + infinitiv (should)\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>Wednesday</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Reading text in Unit 6, describing pictures on p. 83\r\n<li>Past tense, p. 86, 88: 2, 3\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>Thursday</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Review past tense rules p. 83, 87-88:1 a,b\r\n<li>Practice past tense p. 85: 4, 89:4 \r\n</ul>\r\n', 219, 0, 100),
(130, '', '<h3>Monday</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Complete exercises 4, 5, 6, 7 on p. 76 of the Textbook\r\n<li>Workbook 28: 6, 7\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3>Tuesday</h3>\r\nIdentify weak areas and over the next week, select exercises from the workbook between pages 30 and 41, that will help you to practice these elements. Turn in your workbook on Monday for correction before the test on Wednesday.\r\n\r\n<h3>Wednesday</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Answer questions on p. 82\r\n<li>Describe pictures on p. 83\r\n<li>Exercise 1 a) and b) on pp. 87-88\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>Homework</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Textbook 89: 5, 90: 6\r\n<li>Worbook 44: 6, 7, 8\r\n</ul>', 220, 0, 100),
(131, '', '<h2>Diskuze 1</h2>\r\nPřipravte si odpovědi na tyto otázky. Jednu otázku zpracujte písemně: \r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Jaké jsou mytické počátky českého národa?\r\n<li>Je současná situace Čechů výsledkem jejich dějin?\r\n<li>Jaký je význam čísla 8 v českých dějinách? Popite alespoň jedno datum končící na 8.\r\n<li>Jakou si myslíte, e má český národ budoucnost?\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2>Diskuze 2</h2>\r\nPřečtěte si text v učebnici na straně 106. Odpovězte na otázky a napite krátký text o českých dějnách.\r\n\r\n<h2>Diskuze 3</h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Přečtěte si text o Libui na s. 85 a odpovězte na otázky cvičení 3, 4 na s. 86\r\n<li>Vyberte si patnáct dvojic z těchto cvičení, a napite krátké věty.<uL>\r\n<li>Cvičení 1, strana 106\r\n<li>Cvičení 2, strana 86\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n</ul>\r\n', 221, 0, 100);
 one might say that the Czech martyr complex itself represents an expression of that collectivism the Revivalists saw in the Slavs. The national martyr obliterates his personal identity for the sake of the nations identity. (p. 210) Compare this with the cultural-pattern approach to collectivism (Ward at al., The Psychology of Culture Shock, 2001, pp. 11  17) and with Isaacs notion of basic group identity.<o:p></o:p></SPAN></LI>\r\n<LI class=MsoNormal style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list 36.0pt\"><SPAN style=\"mso-ansi-language: EN-US\">What cultural universals and national specifics can be identified in the Czech national myths described by Pynsent? (e.g. Great Moravia, Otokar II P</SPAN><SPAN lang=CS>řemysl, </SPAN><SPAN style=\"mso-ansi-language: EN-US\">St. Wenceslas, Charles IV., Hussite movement, George of Pod</SPAN><SPAN lang=CS>ěbrady, </SPAN><SPAN style=\"mso-ansi-language: EN-US\">Battle of White Mountain, National Revival, the First Republic, Masaryk when compared to other nations myths)<o:p></o:p></SPAN></LI>\r\n<LI class=MsoNormal style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list 36.0pt\"><SPAN style=\"mso-ansi-language: EN-US\">What in the readings was new, what was surprising and what provoked disagreement? What was not clear? What could be said to be the common theme of all this weeks readings?<o:p></o:p></SPAN></LI></OL>', 222, 0, 100),
(133, '', '<h3>Monday</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Review of past tense\r\n<li>Asking questions about past schedule (days of the week)\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>Tuesday</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Text on p. 82 - identify underlined expressions and deduce the rules for forming genitive\r\n<li>Prepositions with genitive: Space: od, do, u, vedle, z; Other: bez, kromě\r\n<li>Textbook p. 91, 92: 3, 4, 93: 5\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3>Wednesday</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Progress test 3\r\n<li>Practicing genitive: Use <a href=http://mapy.atlas.cz>http://mapy.atlas.cz</a> to find 5 streets beginning with U (such as U poliklinky, and decide what are they near (use <a href=http://www.wordbook.cz>Wordbook.cz</a> to help with the translations).\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>Thursday</h3>\r\nDifferent uses of genitive\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>After prepositions 92: 3, 4 (space), 93: 5 (time), 6, 7, 95: 14\r\n<li>As the object case of verbs 92: 1, 2\r\n<li>Expressing quantity 94: 9\r\n<li>Expressing kind, belonging 94: 10\r\n<li>Possession and ownership 94: 11, 95: 12\r\n<li>After <i>co, něco, nic</i> 95: 13\r\n</ul>\r\n', 223, 0, 100),
(134, '', '<h3>Monday and Tuesday</h3>\r\nReview for progress test.\r\n\r\n<h3>Wednesday</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Find an interesting restaurant name such as U bílé paní (use <a href=http://mapy.atlas.cz>http://mapy.atlas.cz</a>\r\n<li>Exercises to practice genitive: Workbook 42: 1, 2; 43: 4\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\n<h3>Thursday</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Complete exercises in textbook and workbook on genitive and past tense\r\n<li><i>Co jste dělali o prázdninách?</i> Write 150 words using all the grammar and vocabulary covered so far. Use words such as:\r\n<uL>\r\n<li>vánoce (Christmas)\r\n<li>tědrý večer (Christmas Eve)\r\n<li>Nový rok (New Year)\r\n<li>Sylvestr (New Year\'s Eve)\r\n<li>dát/dostat dárek\r\n<li>Dates format: 24. 12.\r\n</uL>\r\n<uL>', 224, 0, 100),
(135, '', 'Postavení eny ve společnosti. Politická korektnost, pozitivní diskriminace a lidská práva. \r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Jaké je postavení eny v dnení společnosti v porovnání s rokem 1950?\r\n<li>Jaký je rozdíl mezi enami v Británii a v České republice.\r\n<li>O čem mluví české feministiky?\r\n<li>Proč není feminismus populární v České republice?\r\n</ul>\r\n\r\nPřečtěte si článek o enách v České republice a najděte alespoň dva relevantní texty na serveru feminismus.cz.<p>\r\nNapite sto slov o tom, jaký je vá vlastní postoj k feminismu.', 226, 0, 10),
