owtext 2.25pt solid; PADDING-RIGHT: 5.35pt; BORDER-TOP: medium none; PADDING-LEFT: 5.35pt; PADDING-BOTTOM: 0cm; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; WIDTH: 59.4pt; BORDER-BOTTOM: windowtext 2.25pt solid\" width=79>\r\n<P><A href=\"tuit/sound/grammar/pronexamples/vowels/mu1ze.rm\">mue</A> </P></TD>\r\n<TD style=\"BORDER-RIGHT: medium none; PADDING-RIGHT: 0cm; BORDER-TOP: medium none; PADDING-LEFT: 0cm; PADDING-BOTTOM: 0cm; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; BORDER-BOTTOM: medium none; mso-cell-special: placeholder\" width=0>\r\n<P class=MsoNormal> </P></TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE>', 3, NULL);
INSERT INTO `exercises` (`ex_id`, `ex_type`, `ex_name`, `ex_description`, `ex_creator`, `ex_task`, `ex_story`, `ex_difficulty`, `ex_options`) VALUES
(1947, 6, 'Consonant Clusters', 'Consonant Clusters', 49, 'Consonant Clusters', '<P><SPAN lang=CS>Another trick of Czech pronunciation is its tendency to cluster consonants. As many as 4 consonants can be in one syllable without any vowels. Thus, <i><a href=/tuit/sound/grammar/consonantclusters/zmrzlina.rm>zmrzlina</a></i> (icecream) is in fact a two-syllable word. Examples of monosyllabic words without any vowels are <I><a href=/tuit/sound/grammar/consonantclusters/smrt.rm>smrt</a></I>, <I><a href=/tuit/sound/grammar/consonantclusters/krk.rm>krk</a>, <a href=/tuit/sound/grammar/consonantclusters/vlk.rm>vlk</a>, <a href=/tuit/sound/grammar/consonantclusters/smrk.rm>smrk</a>, <a href=/tuit/sound/grammar/consonantclusters/pstros.rm>ptros</a>, <a href=/tuit/sound/grammar/consonantclusters/strom.rm>strom</a>, <a href=/tuit/sound/grammar/consonantclusters/stvol.rm>stvol</a></I>. </P>\r\n<P>6 consonants in a row can be found in verbs in the past tense such as <I><a href=/tuit/sound/grammar/consonantclusters/scvrkl.rm>scvrkl</a> </I>(shrank) forming two syllables and even a 7 consonant rarity could be contemplated in the verb <I><a href=/tuit/sound/grammar/consonantclusters/scvrnkl.rm>scvrnkl</a> </I>(pinged off a surface).</P>\r\n<P>Indeed, there is a famous Czech sentence <I><a href=/tuit/sound/grammar/consonantclusters/strcprstskrzkrk.rm>Strč prst skrz krk</a></I> which seemingly lacks vowels completely. <I>Notice</I>, however, that whenever there are no vowels in the word either <I>r</I> or <I>l</I> is present to play the role of a vowel. </P></SPAN>', 3, NULL),
(1948, 6, 'Contrasts', 'Contrasts in pronunciation', 49, 'Pronunciation Contrasts', '<P><SPAN lang=CS>There are several groups of sounds which have something in common one way or another. <I>Vowels</I> and <I>consonants</I> are one example. Vowels are <I>long</I> and <I>short</I>. Consonants are <I>soft </I>and <I>hard</I>, or<I> voiced </I>and <I>unvoiced</I>. It is important to be aware of this opposition since very often when the form of a word changes the ending consonant changes from hard to soft. See the <I>how to</I> spell it charts below for examples.</SPAN></P>\r\n<P class=MsoHeading7 style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt 49.6pt\"><A name=_Toc18756028><STRONG><EM>Short and long vowels</EM></STRONG></A><?xml:namespace prefix = o ns = \"urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office\" /></P>\r\n<P>There are many pairs of Czech words which are distinguished only by the length of the vowels.</P>\r\n<P class=MsoHeading7 style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt 49.6pt\"><A name=_Toc18756029><STRONG><EM>Soft and Hard</EM></STRONG></A><SPAN style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc18756029\"></SPAN><STRONG><EM><SPAN style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc18756029\"><SPAN style=\"mso-spacerun: yes\"> </SPAN>and Both</SPAN></EM></STRONG></P>\r\n<TABLE style=\"BORDER-COLLAPSE: collapse; mso-padding-alt: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt; mso-table-layout-alt: fixed\" cellSpacing=0 cellPadding=0 border=0>\r\n<TBODY>\r\n<TR>\r\n<TD style=\"BORDER-RIGHT: #c0c0c0; PADDING-RIGHT: 5.4pt; BORDER-TOP: #c0c0c0; PADDING-LEFT: 5.4pt; PADDING-BOTTOM: 0cm; BORDER-LEFT: #c0c0c0; WIDTH: 55.05pt; PADDING-TOP: 0cm; BORDER-BOTTOM: #c0c0c0; BACKGROUND-COLOR: transparent\" vAlign=top width=73>\r\n<P><STRONG>HARD</STRONG></P></TD>\r\n<TD style=\"BORDER-RIGHT: #c0c0c0; PADDING-RIGHT: 5.4pt; BORDER-TOP: #c0c0c0; PADDING-LEFT: 5.4pt; PADDING-BOTTOM: 0cm; BORDER-LEFT: #c0c0c0; WIDTH: 33.45pt; PADDING-TOP: 0cm; BORDER-BOTTOM: #c0c0c0; BACKGROUND-COLOR: transparent\" vAlign=top width=45>\r\n<P><B>d</B></P></TD>\r\n<TD style=\"BORDER-RIGHT: #c0c0c0; PADDING-RIGHT: 5.4pt; BORDER-TOP: #c0c0c0; PADDING-LEFT: 5.4pt; PADDING-BOTTOM: 0cm; BORDER-LEFT: #c0c0c0; WIDTH: 44.25pt; PADDING-TOP: 0cm; BORDER-BOTTOM: #c0c0c0; BACKGROUND-COLOR: transparent\" vAlign=top width=59>\r\n<P><B>t</B></P></TD>\r\n<TD style=\"BORDER-RIGHT: #c0c0c0; PADDING-RIGHT: 5.4pt; BORDER-TOP: #c0c0c0; PADDING-LEFT: 5.4pt; PADDING-BOTTOM: 0cm; BORDER-LEFT: #c0c0c0; WIDTH: 44.25pt; PADDING-TOP: 0cm; BORDER-BOTTOM: #c0c0c0; BACKGROUND-COLOR: transparent\" vAlign=top width=59>\r\n<P><B>n</B></P></TD>\r\n<TD style=\"BORDER-RIGHT: #c0c0c0; PADDING-RIGHT: 5.4pt; BORDER-TOP: #c0c0c0; PADDING-LEFT: 5.4pt; PADDING-BOTTOM: 0cm; BORDER-LEFT: #c0c0c0; WIDTH: 44.25pt; PADDING-TOP: 0cm; BORDER-BOTTOM: #c0c0c0; BACKGROUND-COLOR: transparent\" vAlign=top width=59>\r\n<P><B>ch</B></P></TD>\r\n<TD style=\"BORDER-RIGHT: #c0c0c0; PADDING-RIGHT: 5.4pt; BORDER-TOP: #c0c0c0; PADDING-LEFT: 5.4pt; PADDING-BOTTOM: 0cm; BORDER-LEFT: #c0c0c0; WIDTH: 44.25pt; PADDING-TOP: 0cm; BORDER-BOTTOM: #c0c0c0; BACKGROUND-COLOR: transparent\" vAlign=top width=59>\r\n<P><B>k</B></P></TD>\r\n<TD style=\"BORDER-RIGHT: #c0c0c0; PADDING-RIGHT: 5.4pt; BORDER-TOP: #c0c0c0; PADDING-LEFT: 5.4pt; PADDING-BOTTOM: 0cm; BORDER-LEFT: #c0c0c0; WIDTH: 44.25pt; PADDING-TOP: 0cm; BORDER-BOTTOM: #c0c0c0; BACKGROUND-COLOR: transparent\" vAlign=top width=59>\r\n<P><B>h</B></P></TD>\r\n<TD style=\"BORDER-RIGHT: #c0c0c0; PADDING-RIGHT: 5.4pt; BORDER-TOP: #c0c0c0; PADDING-LEFT: 5.4pt; PADDING-BOTTOM: 0cm; BORDER-LEFT: #c0c0c0; WIDTH: 44.25pt; PADDING-TOP: 0cm; BORDER-BOTTOM: #c0c0c0; BACKGROUND-COLOR: transparent\" vAlign=top width=59>\r\n<P><B>g</B></P></TD>\r\n<TD style=\"BORDER-RIGHT: #c0c0c0; PADDING-RIGHT: 5.4pt; BORDER-TOP: #c0c0c0; PADDING-LEFT: 5.4pt; PADDING-BOTTOM: 0cm; BORDER-LEFT: #c0c0c0; WIDTH: 44.25pt; PADDING-TOP: 0cm; BORDER-BOTTOM: #c0c0c0; BACKGROUND-COLOR: transparent\" vAlign=top width=59>\r\n<P><B>r</B></P></TD>\r\n<TD style=\"BORDER-RIGHT: #c0c0c0; PADDING-RIGHT: 5.4pt; BORDER-TOP: #c0c0c0; PADDING-LEFT