\n<P class=TableSmall><SPAN lang=EN-US>used to soften consonants <I>c, d, n, r, s, t, z <BR></I></SPAN><SPAN lang=EN-US>if <EM>ď, , ň</EM> is followed by <I>e</I> the Ą is placed over the <I>e</I>, <BR>if they are followed by <I>i/í</I> the ° is dropped (see below)</SPAN></P>\r\n<P class=TableSmall><SPAN lang=EN-US>(<STRONG>Note: </STRONG>In print, háček Ą over <EM>d</EM> and <EM>t </EM>is displayed as an apostrophe \': <EM>, ď</EM>.)<BR> </P></SPAN></TD></TR>\r\n<TR>\r\n<TD style=\"PADDING-RIGHT: 5.4pt; PADDING-LEFT: 5.4pt; PADDING-BOTTOM: 0cm; WIDTH: 83.4pt; PADDING-TOP: 0cm\" vAlign=top width=111>\r\n<P class=NormalNoIndent><B><SPAN lang=EN-US style=\"FONT-SIZE: 14pt; FONT-FAMILY: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-size: 10.0pt; mso-ascii-font-family: Times New Roman; mso-hansi-font-family: Times New Roman; mso-char-type: symbol; mso-symbol-font-family: Symbol\">°</SPAN><SPAN lang=EN-US> </SPAN></B></P></TD>\r\n<TD style=\"PADDING-RIGHT: 5.4pt; PADDING-LEFT: 5.4pt; PADDING-BOTTOM: 0cm; WIDTH: 49.6pt; PADDING-TOP: 0cm\" vAlign=top width=66>\r\n<P class=MsoNormal><A href=\"tuit/sound/grammar/diacritics/krouzek.rm\"><SPAN lang=EN-US>krouek</SPAN></A></P></TD>\r\n<TD style=\"PADDING-RIGHT: 5.4pt; PADDING-LEFT: 5.4pt; PADDING-BOTTOM: 0cm; WIDTH: 11cm; PADDING-TOP: 0cm\" vAlign=top width=416>\r\n<P class=TableSmall><SPAN lang=EN-US>only used with <I>ů </I>if it is not the first letter in the word; otherwise ´ is used</SPAN></P></TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE>', 3, NULL),
