(1794, 13, 'magda', 'alcor69_69@yahoo.com', 'I found a great way to call home to Ostrava', 'I have been using www.callingforcheap.com\r\n\r\nThought you all might like to know and they have a very good speed dial option.', '2005-10-20 06:25:54', 0, 0),
(1795, 13, 'Erik Piper', '', 'Re: what does this mean?', 'I\'m sitting around in Brno and I\'m very [ends here].\r\n\r\nLooks like it got cut off.\r\n\r\ne.', '2005-10-20 14:42:36', 1793, 0),
(1796, 13, 'steve', 'stelingouk@aol.com', 'accusative or locative?', 'How would I translate the following sentence? Children start school at 5 years old.\r\nDeti zacinaji skolu v pet let (acc) or v peti letech (loc)\r\n\r\nDekuji za pomoc.\r\n\r\nSteve', '2005-10-23 02:20:28', 0, 1),
(1797, 13, 'Quinn', 'quinn_romance@yahoo.com', 'Proud of Czech Heritage', 'I just learned from some distant relatives about my Czech heritage, and I\'m so proud of what I am. It\'s really cool to have people ask you, \'Can you tell me more about the Czech people and your heritage?\'. I\'ve only been asked a few times, but each time I explained it, a wash of pride swept over me. I love the Czech people. (Super random? Of course.)', '2005-10-24 06:40:45', 0, 1),
(1798, 13, 'bunny', 'tibunny3@yahoo.com', 'Re: milenka - milenec', 'Ahoj Evo,\r\n\r\n:) Sorry for the late reply, I rarely check that email...\r\n\r\nThank you for your explanation, although it still is not clear to me.\r\n\r\nDo you agree with:\r\n\r\nlaska: big love & sex\r\nmilacek: maybe love & sex\r\nmilenec: no love & sex\r\n\r\n:)\r\n', '2005-10-27 04:34:40', 1791, 1),
(1799, 13, 'Jakub', '', 'Re: accusative or locative?', 'These two variants are both possible: \"v peti letech\" or \"ve stari peti let\".\r\nIs that the answer you want or is it even more confusing?\r\nJakub', '2005-10-31 02:57:41', 1796, 0),
(1800, 13, 'steve', 'stelingouk@aol.com', 'acc or loc?', 'These two variants are both possible: \"v peti letech\" or \"ve stari peti let\". \r\nIs that the answer you want or is it even more confusing? \r\nJakub \r\n\r\nI\'ve had to start this as a new topic as my reply doesn\'t seem to appear. What case is \'peti let\' in the phrase \"ve stari peti let\"?\r\n', '2005-10-31 03:35:35', 0, 1),
(1801, 17, 'Val', 'valkovalenko@hotmail.com', 'Books in Chech', 'Kde muzu koupit czeski knihi v Londyne?\r\nWhere could purchase books in Czech in London?\r\n', '2005-10-31 03:56:32', 0, 1),
(1802, 13, 'Jakub', '', 'Re: acc or loc?', '\"ve stari\" - loc\r\n\"peti let\" - gen\r\n\r\nLit. \'at the age of five years\'\r\n\r\n\"v peti letech\" - loc\r\n\r\nLit. \'at five years\'\r\n\r\n', '2005-10-31 17:18:06', 1800, 0),
(1803, 14, 'Jakub', '', 'Re: looking for a Bohemian pen pal', 'Sorry, can\'t help you. I\'am from Silesia and live in Moravia :(', '2005-11-01 20:40:53', 1792, 0),
(1804, 13, 'Vladimír', '', 'Re: acc or loc?', 'The preposition \"v\" is rarely used with the accusative case.\r\n\r\nvěřit, doufat v někoho, v něco (acc.)\r\n\r\ne.g. Věříme v Boha (acc.). We trust in God.\r\n', '2005-11-03 12:59:25', 1800, 0),
(1805, 17, 'Tomá Řáda', 't.rada@centrum.cz', 'Jen tak', 'Dobrý den.\r\n\r\n         Pocházím z České Republiky a narazil jsem na vá web.Moc se my líbil,a tak jsem se rozhodl,e vám napíu.Já bydlím kousek od Prahy v Kralupech nad Vltavou.A odkud jste vy ???Učím se Angličtinu.Zdraví vás Tomá.', '2005-11-07 00:03:28', 0, 0),
(1806, 17, 'sifak', 't.rada@centrum.cz', 'Re: :o)', 'Já pocházím z České Republiky,jestli si se mnou chce česky psát,napi mi na email t.rad@centrum.cz.Čus\r\n', '2005-11-07 00:08:37', 1120, 0),
(1807, 13, 'Kristina', '', 'Re: milenka - milenec', 'I know when my boyfriend stopped referring to me as milenka, when he said ty jsi moje mila, then I knew we had progressed.  He has subsequently said to me in conversation, that to a czech man - Milenka je jenom na sex, Kristino.', '2005-11-15 11:00:33', 1791, 0),
(1808, 13, 'Pete', 'peter.dain@tesco.net', 'Jen & Pouze', 'Which ones of these fits which senses of \"only\".\r\n\r\nIs it \"pouze\" is a bit like \"exclusive for...\" as in \"only for adults\" whereas \"jen\" covers the other senses eg. \"I have only five carrots left?\"\r\n\r\n', '2005-11-17 04:59:27', 0, 1),
(1809, 13, 'J', '', 'Re: Jen & Pouze', 'Hi!\r\nIn my opinion \"jen\" and \"pouze\" are completely interchangeable. I can\'t realize any case where one of them can go and the other cannot.\r\nJakub', '2005-11-17 19:03:51', 1808, 0),
(1810, 13, 'Vladimír', '', 'Re: Jen & Pouze', 'I can:\r\n\r\n- Smím si vzít?\r\n- Jen si dej!\r\n', '2005-11-18 22:32:01', 1809, 0),
(1811, 13, 'Erik Piper', '', 'Re: Jen & Pouze', 'Výjimka potvrzuje pravidlo. :-) That\'s a sense where jen isn\'t being used to mean \"only.\" No fair!\r\n\r\nAs regards the original question: pouze is seems rarer than jen to me. It also seems stronger. But I\'m not Czech (though I\'ve lived here for about a decade).\r\n\r\ne.', '2005-11-21 18:20:17', 1810, 0),
(1812, 13, 'Vlk', '', 'Re: Jen & Pouze', 'Jen počkej!', '2005-11-21 22:28:33', 1811, 0),
(1813, 13, 'Erik Piper', '', 'Re: Jen & Pouze', 'In short, jen can be an equivalent for the English word \"just\", whereas pouze cannot.\r\n\r\ne.', '2005-11-22 16:44:27', 1812, 0),
(1814, 13, 'Erik Piper', '', 'Re: Jen & Pouze', 'In short, jen can be an equivalent for the English word \"just\", whereas pouze cannot.\r\n\r\ne.', '2005-11-22 18:03:03', 1812, 0),
(1815, 13, 'marta', 'ljubkova@hotmail.com', 'Re: acc or loc?', 'It is genitive (while \"ve stari\" is Locative).', '2005-11-29 14:20:58', 1800, 1),
(1816, 15, 'Christine Davis', 'crdavis+cz@gmail.com', '', 'I\'ve studied Czech off and on for several years.  I would like to use Michael Heim\'s _Contemporary Czech_, but I\'m frustrated by the lack of an answer key, as I\'m studying by myself.  Has anyone used this book?  (Do you have the answers to the exercises?)  Or would someone be willing to puzzle through the exercises with me?\r\n\r\nThanks,\r\nChristine', '2005-12-07 17:34:18', 0, 1),
(1817, 17, 'Jose', 'trigos@gmail.com', 'Re: :o)', 'Your email address  t.rad@centrum.cz is wrong \r\n(failure message: permanent failure) ', '2005-12-08 22:14:43', 1806, 0),
(1818, 17, 'Jose', 'trigos@gmail.com', 'Re: :o)', 'Your email address  t.rad@centrum.cz is wrong \r\n(failure message: permanent failure) ', '2005-12-08 22:15:34', 1806, 1),
(1819, 13, 'mike sumerlin', 'msumerlin@houston.rr.com', 'what is czech for \"Cheers\" or \"Down the Hatch\"', 'What is popular czech term for Cheers or Down the Hatch or Salute?\r\n\r\nThanks much.  For older, well-to-do worldly man.\r\nMS', '2005-12-22 08:38:44', 0, 0),
(1820, 13, 'kevin', 'handleyf@tesco.net', 'Re: what is czech for', 'Nazdravi is the word you are looking for, I think. Though I am neither well to do or worldy but I am a man and the other thing. (pronounced naz-drav-ee)', '2005-12-31 05:17:10', 1819, 0),
(1821, 15, 'kevin', 'handleyf@tesco.net', 'Re:', 'As no-one seems to have replied, I\'ll go for puzzling through with you if you like Christine. I don\'t have this Michael Heims but have a few other textbooks for reference. I too have studied on and off for last few years, not much recently though so could do with something to kickstart me again. Email if you want to take me up on this', '2005-12-31 05:25:39', 1816, 0),
(1822, 13, 'paola', 'pajpa21@yahoo.it', 't\'astný Nový Rok', 'Hi and a very happy new year to everybody....could any of you please translate this message \"Děkuju za přání. I já Ti přeju Veselé vánoce!! Moc příjemné svátky a astný nový rok Do noveho roku hodne ohody, uspechu lasky a zdravi ti take preje\r\nPřeji slunečné dny\" that I received from my loved czech  friend? As I can imagine it\'s a very good wishes-message but I\'m STILL attempting to learn Cech language....many thanks and nicest regards, a Nashledanou\r\nPaola ', '2006-01-03 15:04:36', 0, 0),
(1823, 13, 'KAKATAL', 'elois_norl@hotmail.com', 'Translation', 'Hello,\r\n\r\nCould a good soul translate the following sentence for me plz ?\r\n\r\nTeím se a t&#236; zase znovu uvidim, ale netuím kdy to bude m&#249;j milovaný p&#248;íteli.\r\n\r\nThx.', '2006-01-03 17:13:34', 0, 1),
(1824, 13, 'Sylva', 'rainebowsnake@gmail.com', 'sounds like \'taya\'?', 'hi, is there a word in czech that sounds like \'taya\' i\'m having problems translating this, what do you think?', '2006-01-09 00:54:45', 0, 1),
(1825, 13, 'Frank', 'FCernik@yahoo.com', 'Re: what is czech for', '\"Na zdravi\" it is and for Down the Hatch you can use \"Do dna\" (to the bottom) or \"Na ex\".', '2006-01-11 18:32:29', 1820, 1),
(1826, 13, 'Pavla', '', 'Kdyby chyby in English', 'Hi all :-))\r\n\r\nI wanted to use something like Czech saying \"kdyby chyby\" in English, but did not found eny equivalent yet. The nearest was something like \"when fishes were horses beggarts would ride\" but this doesn\'t fit at all to my essay. I want to use it in the sentence where I write that someone would usually be able to do something but \"kbydy chyby\" - he is not because of some circunstances ...\r\n\r\nAny ideas how kdyby chyby may be in English ?\r\n\r\n                 Many greetings\r\n\r\n                              Pavla', '2006-01-21 12:11:41', 0, 0),
(1827, 13, 'paola', 'pajpa21@yahoo.it', 'translation', 'could any of you please translate this message \"Děkuju za přání. I já Ti přeju Veselé vánoce!! Moc příjemné svátky a astný nový rok Do noveho roku hodne ohody, uspechu lasky a zdravi ti take preje \r\nPřeji slunečné dny\" that I received from my loved czech friend? As I can imagine it\'s a very good wishes-message but I\'m STILL attempting to learn Cech language....many thanks and nicest regards, a Nashledanou \r\nPaola  \r\n   \r\n', '2006-02-03 18:27:18', 0, 1),
(1828, 13, 'Kevin', 'handleyf@tesco.net', 'Re: translation', 'Paola, roughly as follows\r\n\r\nThanks for your wishes\r\nI also wish you a happy Christmas\r\nPleasant holy time (maybe even holidays) and a happy New Year\r\nTo a new year of much contentment, succesful love and health to/for you also (I wish?) \r\nI wish you sunny days\r\n\r\nI am not certain of any nuances there might or might not be but that is hopefully the gist of it.', '2006-02-06 19:04:58', 1827, 0),
(1829, 13, 'A Charles', 'anjistar@charles21784.ndo.co.uk', 'Difficulties with English', 'Is there anywhere on the internet where I can find out about common problems for Czech speakers in learning English?\r\nI have the Learner English book by Smith and Swann. It puts Czech under the heading for Polish speakers, but are the problems exactly the same? Or are there any specific problems for Czech learners of English?\r\nMany thanks\r\nAnji', '2006-02-13 16:25:31', 0, 1),
(1830, 13, 'Lisa', 'lisa_watt@hotmail.com', 'HELP!', 'I just got a text message in what i think is czech and as i only speak english and german i have no idea what it says and REALLY want to know! If anyone could help me that\'d be great!! ok the message reads\r\n\r\n\"pomoc ja uz nemuzu ale kazdopadne bych ti dal rad pusa(or maybe pusu)  kote\"\r\n\r\nAny ideas? Thanks so much!\r\nLisa', '2006-02-14 13:44:39', 0, 0),
(1831, 13, 'Dave C.', 'Eveninthedark73@aol.com', 'Pronouncing a Czech name', 'I will be hosting an exchange student from the Czech Republic starting from June 2006-2007. His name is Josef Ví&#232;kosky. From the best I can figure out his name is pronoused YAH-sef VEE-ay-kah-skee.', '2006-02-14 14:55:37', 0, 1),
(1832, 13, 'V.', '', 'Re: Difficulties with English', 'The problems concerning the English grammar must be exactly the same as the Czech and Polish languages are very similar (West Slavic):\r\n\r\n- articles ( /the?/ transformer is /a?/ device ..., we use no articles in such cases)\r\n- verbal system of tenses (I have written vs. I wrote, I am writing vs. I write)\r\n- phrasal verbs (get /on, off, in, out, .../, put, go, give, break, and many others), that hardly correspond with the Czech/Polish ones\r\n\r\nAbout pronuntiation:\r\n\r\nhttp://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Non-native_pronunciations_of_English#Hungarian\r\n', '2006-02-15 17:20:14', 1829, 0),
(1833, 13, 'V.', '', 'Re: Difficulties with English', 'http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Non-native_pronunciations_of_English#Czech', '2006-02-15 17:30:39', 1832, 0),
(1834, 13, 'V.', '', 'Re: Pronouncing a Czech name', 'The last name is certaily misspelled.', '2006-02-15 17:33:38', 1831, 0),
(1835, 13, 'V.', '', 'Re: Pronouncing a Czech name', '\"certaily\" is also misspelled', '2006-02-15 17:37:22', 1834, 0),
(1836, 13, 'A Charles', 'anjistar@charles21784.ndo.co.uk', 'Re: Difficulties with English', 'Many thanks. That was very helpful!\r\nRegards,\r\nAngie', '2006-02-15 20:42:09', 1833, 0),
(1837, 13, 'kevin', 'handleyf@tesco.net', 'Re: Pronouncing a Czech name', 'Josef, is pretty much as it looks with Y replacing J with a short o. \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n', '2006-02-17 01:51:20', 1831, 0),
(1838, 13, 'lisa', 'lisa_watt@hotmail.com', 'translation...', 'im still stuck with the translation below, listed at HELP! and would be grateful for any help!! my friend tells me i must find out for myself and he will not tell me!! please help if possible!!xxx', '2006-02-17 11:41:17', 0, 1),
(1839, 13, 'V.', '', 'Re: HELP!', 'My attempt:\r\n\r\nHelp! I cannot go on (I got stuck).\r\nBut in any case I should like to kiss you, chicklet (or babe, kitten, ...).', '2006-02-17 13:56:13', 1830, 0),
