(1863, 16, 'Tereza', 'terezat@gmail.com', 'Czech Conversaton class in Portland, OR', 'I will be teaching a beginning-level Czech conversation class at Portland Community College in Portland, Oregon. This will be a non-credit class which will meet Thursdays from 7 to 9 pm, starting June 29th and ending August 17, 2006. \r\n\r\nHere is the course description: Planning a trip to the Czech Republic? Want to get in touch with your Czech heritage? Learn basic phrases, vocabulary, & grammar for everyday use with a focus on culture & travel. Taught by a native speaker. \r\n\r\nFor more information or to register, go to: http://www.pcc.edu or http://studyczech.blogspot.com.\r\n\r\nPlease spread the word among those who may be interested!', '2006-05-06 18:40:36', 0, 1),
(1864, 13, 'Kevin', 'handleyf@tesco.net', 'Re: Mothers Day', 'Vsechno nejlepsi ke Svatku matek\r\n\r\npronounced something like fsheckno neylepshee ke(h) svatku (this is a long a maybe like svahtku?) matek \r\n\r\nIf you write it the sh s\'s have a hacek over them and the long a has the other whotsit as does the the i at the end of nejlepsi', '2006-05-07 00:05:23', 1860, 0),
(1865, 13, 'kevin', 'handleyf@tesco.net', 'Re: Mothers Day', 'and its tomorrow I think', '2006-05-07 00:08:14', 1859, 0),
(1866, 14, 'Persiancat', 'hasharico@hotmail.com', 'Visitng the Czech Republic', 'I am visitng Prague and Zlin for the month of August. I would like to find a Czech friend to tell me about the culture and the country before I arrive. If possible I would like to then hire that person to be my private tour guide on occasion. I would pay for expenses incurred for travel etc.\r\n\r\nPlease write to me at hasharico@hotmail.com.\r\n\r\nThanks.', '2006-05-12 18:54:05', 0, 1),
(1867, 14, 'janea', 'janicka777@centrum.cz', 'Re: Visitng the Czech Republic', 'Don\'t worry, you don\'t need to know anything special about czech republic. We are usually nice people - not afraid of foreigners and young people DO speak english very well... Perhaps, we aren\'t so open immediately (compare to americans) and we don\'t kiss on face by meeting! :-) It\'s usual to go to pub for a beer... The beer is sometimes being cheaper than mineral water. In August is the weather very nice, but sometimes happens that it is raining all the time. Btw., be careful, taxi drivers in Prague are really expensive!', '2006-05-18 02:48:48', 1866, 1),
(1868, 13, 'Melanie', 'k_sde@hotmail.com', 'simple sentences to survive prague help', 'Hi,\r\nmy husband is a pilot who flys to prague.  \r\nWhile he speaks many languages, the czech language elludes him.  \r\nCan someone translate the following sentences for me, so i can pass them to him.  \r\n\r\n1. Where can i purchase an international phone card?\r\n2.  I want to purchase an international phone card, I will be phoning Canada.  \r\n3.  Can you recommend a jewlery store that sells amber?\r\n\r\nThank you in advance\r\nMelanie', '2006-05-18 22:51:20', 0, 1),
(1869, 14, 'PersianCat', 'hasharico@hotmail.com', 'Re: Visitng the Czech Republic', 'Thanks for the reply. I also replied directly to your email address. Please let me know if you received it.\r\n\r\n', '2006-05-19 03:04:09', 1867, 0),
(1870, 13, 'Milan', 'dotazy@milan-broz.co.uk', 'Re: simple sentences to survive prague help', '1.) Kde si mohu koupit telefonní kartu na mezinárodní volání?\r\n2.)Chci si koupit telefonní kartu na mezinárodní volání, budu volat do Kanady.\r\n3.)Můete mi doporučit klenotnictví, kde prodávají jantar?\r\n\r\nHope it helps. \r\n\r\nRegards\r\nMilan\r\n', '2006-05-19 04:21:45', 1868, 0),
(1871, 14, 'janea', '', 'Re: Visitng the Czech Republic', 'Není zač (=that\'s all right =don\'t mention it). I wish you enjoy your stay here. Jana', '2006-05-19 17:32:07', 1869, 0),
(1872, 14, 'victria', 'yul.rlz@gmail.com', 'Food', 'Hey everybody! I\'m involved in a school project, in which I\'m supposed to launch a new product into the Czech food market. My friends and I have thought of dehydrated packaged soup. What we\'re willing to know is if Czech people would accept this new product, and buy it, how much they\'re going to pay for it (it would be really useful if anyone could give us the cost of living there, the average salary, etc.)\r\nIf the soup industry doesn\'t seem a good idea, we accept suggestions of any food product that you think will succeed.\r\n\r\nThank you very much.\r\nVictria.', '2006-05-24 20:32:55', 0, 1),
(1873, 14, 'Kevin', 'kevsy@tesco.net', 'Re: Food', 'I think the soup idea could work, the Czechs seem to like fairly simple food. Pretty much everything is being thrown at central/eastern europe at the moment so they can enjoy the benefits of our wonderful western ways, dehydrated soup must slot nicely into this. Make sure there\'s some meat and stodge in it. \r\nThe cost of living is rapidly catching up with western europe. It\'s now in many thing\'s almost the same, but food and particularly wages lag behind perhaps no more than 50% of say the UK. There also seems to be a marked difference between Prague amd the rest of the country. Certain things can command a premium, I still pack Heinz baked beans they are cheaper at UK Tesco and of course tea (you just can,t get proper teaq anywhere but here .. the UK, ok maybe India), when we go over. So I suppose overall you will need to pitch your soup maybe a little lower priced than here, market it as French or Swiss but make it in Zlin or somewhere cheap (I don\'t know that Zlin is especially cheap .. but it sounds it). Hope this helps and I look forward to seeing your soup at Kaufland, Carrefour, Tesco, Interspar, Lidl, Ikea etc..', '2006-05-31 04:30:26', 1872, 0),
(1874, 13, 'Spellweaver', 'Spellweaver@seznam.cz', 'Re: vepř, prase', '\"vepř\" is spisovně\r\n\"prase\" nespisovně\r\n(Sorry I can\'t say \"spisovne\" in English)', '2006-06-01 00:27:24', 1844, 0),
(1876, 14, 'Arthur Fowler', 'af3@verizon.net', 'Re: Visitng the Czech Republic', 'Hello, or...nazdar!\r\n  I live in Texas and plan to visit the Czech Republic next month for a couple of weeks.  I speak and read a little Czech (ale moje Cesky neni tak dobry jak byl.....a opravdu nebyl moc).  My grandfather, Frank Matus came to Texas from the village of Horni Lidec in 1905 at the age of fourteen.  His father was killed when he fell from a tree while picking fruit, and his stepfather was named Kurtin.\r\n  How would I go about finding out whether there are any distant relatives still in the Horni Lidec area?  I also have great-grandparents named Bravanec and Surovik from the town of Jasene. (I can\'t locate Jasene, perhaps my documents are misspelled).  I have several photos of the area of Horni Lidec from around 1938 when my grandparents went back for a visit, but none of the photos are marked as to who or where.  \r\n  I gather you live in the Prague area, but perhaps you may be familiar with the Moravian end of the country.  I will probably be in Prague for a few days.\r\n  Any information you can give me will be great.\r\n        Thanks very much...dekuji vam!     Arthur', '2006-06-21 02:30:07', 1867, 1),
(1877, 13, 'mary', 'saunamari@hotmail.com', 'translation help - hurry', 'Please translate it to english, very important\r\n\r\nTak ja letim za vama! Tata me pustil!\r\n\r\nDosla ti ta smska? Jedu za vama!\r\n\r\nJo a nechces mi rict, ze si budu muset platit hotel. ze ne?\r\n\r\nAhoooj, sorry za neodpis, ale vcera starsna kalba. Neboj, zjadny hotel', '2006-06-24 23:38:53', 0, 0),
(1878, 22, 'musavir ahmed', 'musavirjan@yahoo.com', 'relation between language and culture', '\r\n\r\n    hello sir\r\n     i am writing my Ph.D thesis on the topic \"LANGUAGE_CULTURE RELATIONSHIP-A CASE STUDY OF KASHMII\". i have been looking for the last two years some serious work on language-culture relationship,especially how metaphor(either as a linguistic phenomenon or a conceptual phenomenon)reflects culture.i will b highly thankful to u if u guide me in this regard.\r\n\r\n                                                    yours faithfully\r\n\r\n                                                    musavir ahmed\r\n                                            teaching assistant\\research scholar\r\n                                                  deptt. of linguistics\r\n                                                  university of kashmir\r\n                                         srinagar,kashmir j&k india-190009', '2006-07-12 13:32:46', 0, 0),
(1879, 15, 'milosz', 'milosz@uni.opole.pl', 'science-camp', 'I would like to invite all students living in Czech Republic to international, Polish-Czech science-camp in the Opawskie Mountains. \r\n	Camp will last ten days (7  17 August 2006) and it is a part of the project to create Center of Biodiversity Studies at Opole University within Interreg III A Czech  Poland. Maintenance costs are refunded by ERDF - European Regional Development Fund. Participant pay for transport and partially for food only. Aims of the camp are students integrations and join to begin cooperation on the Opawskie Mountains. Together with students will be working scientists from Opole University. The scopes of the research are assumed vertebrates, invertebrates and plants.\r\n	All informations: milosz@uni.opole.pl. \r\n\r\n	The deadline of registration expires 27 July 2006.\r\n\r\n	The numbers of places are limited. \r\n	  \r\n', '2006-07-13 17:38:14', 0, 1);
INSERT INTO `messages` (`id`, `board_id`, `author`, `email`, `subject`, `text`, `sent`, `following`, `send_note`) VALUES
(1880, 14, 'victria', '', 'Re: Food', 'hey... thanks for your reply!The info u gave me was really very usefull! by any chance, do u know any price of advertising on tv, newspapapers or magazines? we\'re now in the second part of our work, and we\'ve gotta plan the marketing strategies... can u give me your mail? cause it was hard for me to realize were i had post a comment.. thank you very much! hope to hear from you soon. ', '2006-07-17 20:17:15', 1873, 1),
(1883, 13, 'jared', 'punkman87@gmail.com', 'help me with something (may be offensive)', 'My friend Christi has a frined visiting from Czech. Her name is Petra. They just sent me a text message saying:\r\n\r\n\"No jasne, dame nejakou poradnou kalbicku!: )P\"\r\n\r\nso can anyone help me out with what that means??', '2006-07-25 11:58:55', 0, 1),
(1884, 13, 'nyoghta', '', 'Re: help me with something (may be offensive)', 'Hi jared,\r\nthe Czech sentence is not offensive at all. Is says: \"Sure, we\'re gonna have a great (probably rather drunken) party!\"', '2006-07-30 03:48:02', 1883, 0),
(1885, 14, 'Kevin', 'kevsy@tesco.net', 'Re: Food', 'Sorry Victria if this is a little behind the times. I have no idea of cost of advertising in CR, but will happily find out for you when we do summer visit to Czech half of the family (later this month). I have no problem with you having my mail address it\'s kevsy@tesco.net, hopefully this won\'t land me with a load of junk mail. Let me know if you want me to find out about costs\r\nGood luck with the project', '2006-08-03 01:16:52', 1880, 1),
(1886, 15, 'Kevin', 'kevsy@tesco.net', '', 'One of the unexpected things out of learning Czech (and I guess any other language) for me is the realisation of the complexities and unthought of differences with your own native tongue. As this sites forum seems in near terminal decline I thought I might offer up something that may get other people working on similar lines. \r\nIt interests me that Czech does not differentiate between leg and foot and to a degree between hand and arm and best of all between fingers and toes. This then makes you go on to what are equivalents to \"lend a hand\", \"put your foot down\", \"toe the line\" etc.. It would be good to get to know some of the equivalent phrases in Czech.\r\nIs the apparent lessening of interest in this forum, due to the widespread use of foreign language (english mainly) in CR, or have we all just given up on this difficult jazyk. \r\nFinally Erik where are you, you always came along with great translations and stuff, which always lifted me, even if I was to think there he goes again, the smartarse(maybe you would say smartass). It worries me that I have not seen your name for at least six months, I do hope nothing bad has happened, reassure me. \r\nThere were a few other regulars, who never now send anything, Vlad, Gloria, Jana etc., etc.. Surely some of you are still keen, or do I need to learn the Czech for I\'m a sad git.\r\n', '2006-08-05 00:44:46', 0, 0),
(1887, 13, 'Antani', 'anteo@antani.it', 'Translation', 'My girlfriend, which now is very angry with me, sent me this message: \r\n\"Ty postevaku skurveni!\"\r\nPlease post the translation urgently. Thank you!', '2006-08-22 16:04:40', 0, 0),
(1888, 13, 'aswler', '', 'Re: Translation', 'It is quite rude including some sexually explicit and offensive words! I tell you to leave her! :-(', '2006-08-23 02:36:31', 1887, 0),
(1889, 13, 'aswler', '', 'Re: translation help - hurry', 'I guess it is probably too late for the translation. Anyway:\r\n\r\nI am hurrying to come to you. Dad let me go!\r\n\r\nDid you get that sms? I am coming to you!\r\n\r\nAnd I suppose I won´t need to pay a stay in the hotel, will I?\r\n\r\nHi, sorry for not writing back, we had a great party yesterday. Don´t worry, no hotel', '2006-08-23 02:42:28', 1877, 0),
(1890, 13, 'Dominik Lukes', '', 'Re: Translation', 'You have done something really unpleasant to that woman. Nevertheless, it is fairly amusing. \"potěvák\" is a dedeminutivized version of \"poteváček\" meaning \'clitoris\'. And \"skurveni\" is a misspelling of \"zkurvený\" a word derrived from \"kurva\" (whore) - it is commonly used as an adjective roughly in the sense of the English \"fucking\". You can see that a literal translation doesn\'t really work. The closest I can think of is \"You fucking moron\". But I\'m sure more inventive invectives are available.', '2006-08-23 15:56:20', 1887, 0),
(1892, 13, 'Anna', 'annakerr@hotmail.com', 'Re: Translation', 'Hi,\r\n\r\nhttp://www.translationbooth.com have a free translation tool that I use all the time. You just put in a word or phrase or even a document and it can translate it into over 800 language pairs. Have a look bookmark it and then if you ever have a word you don\'t understand you\'ll be able to find out in minutes.\r\n\r\nHope this helps!\r\n', '2006-08-24 10:09:48', 1887, 0),
(1893, 13, 'Perica Baća (Baa)', 'bacciap4@kulawireless.ent', '\"Řka\"', 'I couldn\'t translate the word \"Řka\" (Z knihy Vladislava Vančury Rozmarné léto)\r\n\r\nsentence:  \"Řka to ujal se mistr řemene,...\"\r\n\r\nCould somebody help me?\r\n\r\n', '2006-09-03 23:40:43', 0, 1),
(1894, 13, 'J', '', 'Re:  Řka', 'Řka to... = Saying this...\r\nřka je tvar slovesa říkat (to say) - přechodník přítomný, rod muský. Přechodníky se v moderní četině moc nepouívají a jsou nahrazovány minulým časem; na rozdíl třeba od poltiny, kde jsou součástí moderního jazyka.', '2006-09-05 14:52:24', 1893, 0),
(1895, 13, 'Perica Baća (Baa)', 'bacciap4@kulawireless.net', 'Re:  Řka', 'Děkuju mockrat!', '2006-09-05 19:26:10', 1894, 1),
(1896, 13, 'Shark', 'zidk.s@seznam.cz', 'Re:', 'its meand said its old czech rkouc rekl rika rici', '2006-09-10 22:09:24', 1893, 0),
(1897, 13, 'V.', '', 'Re:  Řka', 'Je to tvar slovesa říci.\r\n\r\nříci -> řka, řkouc, řkouce (oni řkou)\r\n\r\nříkati -> říkaje, říkajíc, říkajíce (oni říkají)', '2006-09-11 15:47:39', 1894, 0),
(1898, 13, 'Perica Baća (Baa)', 'bacciap4@kulawireless.net', 'Czech Course (Serbian) D. Berg', 'Czech Course (Serbian) - D.Berg \r\nDigitalized\r\n\r\nhttp://www.kulawireless.net/bacciap4/czech/index.html\r\n\r\nFill in the form. I\'ll sent you download link', '2006-09-17 03:48:06', 0, 1),
(1899, 13, 'Henri Ahrends', '', 'Translation af birthformular', 'Anyone who can translate SUBJ ?\r\n\r\nI can send it by e-mail\r\n\r\nHenri / Denmark', '2006-09-20 21:09:21', 0, 0),
(1900, 13, 'Henri Ahrends', '', 'Re: Translation af birthformular', 'I\'m trying to find my family who was living in Czech under the 2.WW\r\nthey escaped to Germany in 1945.\r\n\r\nThe name of my father was Frantisek Weis and maybe Reznik,\r\nwe don\'t know what Reznik means, maybe it\'s a surname ?\r\nmy mothers name was Inger Irene Weisova Rodem S&#248;nders&#248;wa ...\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n', '2006-09-20 21:20:42', 1899, 0),
(1901, 13, 'V', '', 'Re: Translation af birthformular', 'Řezník means Butcher, it is a common Czech surname.\r\n\"rodem\" means something like née (maiden surname)', '2006-09-25 15:29:34', 1900, 0);
