bsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n          </span>Main courses</span></p>\r\n        </div>\r\n        <p class=\"Menuitems\"><span lang=\"CS\">Ku&#345;e, brambor, salát<span style=\"mso-tab-count:\r\n  1 dotted\">................................ </span>45.00<span style=\"mso-tab-count:1 dotted\">..........................\r\n        </span>Chicken, potatoes, salad</span></p>\r\n        <p class=\"Menuitems\"><span lang=\"CS\">Vep&#345;ové maso, zelí, knedlík<span style=\"mso-tab-count:1 dotted\">......................\r\n        </span>75.00<span style=\"mso-tab-count:1 dotted\">..................... </span>Pork,\r\n        sour kraut,dumplings</span></p>\r\n        <p class=\"Menuitems\"><span lang=\"CS\">Rybí filé, hranolky, obloha<span style=\"mso-tab-count:1 dotted\">.......................\r\n        </span>38.00<span style=\"mso-tab-count:1 dotted\">................. </span>Fish\r\n        filet, french fries, garnish</span></p>\r\n        <p class=\"Menuitems\"><span lang=\"CS\">Hov&#283;zí gulá, rýe<span style=\"mso-tab-count:\r\n  1 dotted\">..................................... </span>49.00<span style=\"mso-tab-count:1 dotted\">.....................................\r\n        </span>Beef goulash, rice</span></p>\r\n        <div style=\"border:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext .75pt;padding:0cm 0cm 1.0pt 0cm\">\r\n          <p class=\"MenuHeading\"><span lang=\"CS\">Bezmasá jídla<span style=\"mso-tab-count:\r\n  1\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n          </span>Meatless dishes</span></p>\r\n        </div>\r\n        <p class=\"Menuitems\"><span lang=\"CS\">Smaený sýr, tatarská omá&#269;ka<span style=\"mso-tab-count:1 dotted\">.................\r\n        </span>39.00<span style=\"mso-tab-count:1 dotted\">........................\r\n        </span>Fried cheese, tartar sauce</span></p>\r\n        <p class=\"Menuitems\"><span lang=\"CS\">Pala&#269;inka se leha&#269;kou<span style=\"mso-tab-count:1 dotted\">............................\r\n        </span>25.00<span style=\"mso-tab-count:1 dotted\">................ </span>Pancake\r\n        with whipped creeam</span></p>\r\n        <p class=\"Menuitems\"><span lang=\"CS\">pagety se sýrem<span style=\"mso-tab-count:\r\n  1 dotted\">...................................... </span>32.00<span style=\"mso-tab-count:1 dotted\">.................................\r\n        </span>Spagetti with cheese</span></p>\r\n        <div style=\"border:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext .75pt;padding:0cm 0cm 1.0pt 0cm\">\r\n          <p class=\"MenuHeading\"><span lang=\"CS\">Nápoje<span style=\"mso-tab-count:1\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;\r\n          </span>Drinks</span></p>\r\n        </div>\r\n        <p class=\"Menuitems\"><span lang=\"CS\">Káva<span style=\"mso-tab-count:1 dotted\">.........................................................\r\n        </span>18.00<span style=\"mso-tab-count:1 dotted\">.......................................................\r\n        </span>Coffee</span></p>\r\n        <p class=\"Menuitems\"><span lang=\"CS\">Dus<span style=\"mso-tab-count:1 dotted\">..........................................................\r\n        </span>20.00<span style=\"mso-tab-count:1 dotted\">.........................................................\r\n        </span>Juice</span></p>\r\n        <p class=\"Menuitems\"><span lang=\"CS\">Víno<span style=\"mso-tab-count:1 dotted\">..........................................................\r\n        </span>25.00<span style=\"mso-tab-count:1 dotted\">.........................................................\r\n        </span>Wine</span></p>\r\n        <p class=\"Menuitems\"><span lang=\"CS\">Pivo<span style=\"mso-tab-count:1 dotted\">..........................................................\r\n        </span>17.80<span style=\"mso-tab-count:1 dotted\">..........................................................\r\n        </span>Beer</span></p>\r\n        <p class=\"Menuitems\"><span lang=\"CS\">Minerálka<span style=\"mso-tab-count:1 dotted\">.................................................\r\n        </span>15.00<span style=\"mso-tab-count:1 dotted\">...........................................\r\n        </span>Mineral water</span></p>\r\n        <p class=\"TableFirstColumn\" align=\"right\" style=\"text-align:right;tab-stops:right 439.45pt\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n      </td>\r\n    </tr>\r\n  </table>\r\n  </center>\r\n', '2002-10-12 21:53:39', 10066, 31, 70),
(56, 'Current Czech Celebrities', 'Dominik Luke', '\r\n<p class=\"NormalFirst\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">There are two types of items listed\r\nhere. Those that give you insight into Czech culture and Czech people and the\r\nones that are of international value, or are simply the current rave.</span></p>', '\r\nhe Globe or Big Ben will carry many of the books and the Prague Post gives a weekly listing of other cultural events. For CDs and videos go to Bonton Megastore on Wenceslas sq. or POPRON on Jungamanova str. <p>\r\n\r\n<table cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" border=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse;\">\r\n  <tbody><tr>\r\n    <td width=\"99\" valign=\"top\" style=\"padding: 0cm 3.5pt; width: 74.4pt;\">\r\n      <p class=\"TableHeading2\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><b>Fiction</b></span></p>\r\n    </td>\r\n    <td width=\"515\" valign=\"top\" style=\"padding: 0cm 3.5pt; width: 386.2pt;\">\r\n      <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Anything by the following current\r\n      authors: <i>Ivan Klíma, Ludvík Vaculík,\r\n      Milan Kundera, Josef kvorecký, Bohumil Hrabal, Luká Tomin.</i></span></p>\r\n      <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Or by one of these pre-war\r\n      writers: <i>Karel Čapek, Jaroslav\r\n      Haek, Alois Jirásek.</i></span></p>\r\n    </td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td width=\"99\" valign=\"top\" style=\"padding: 0cm 3.5pt; width: 74.4pt;\">\r\n      <p class=\"TableHeading2\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><b>Poetry</b></span></p>\r\n    </td>\r\n    <td width=\"515\" valign=\"top\" style=\"padding: 0cm 3.5pt; width: 386.2pt;\">\r\n      <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Dont miss the Nobel Prize\r\n      winner <i>Jaroslav Seifert</i>. Some\r\n      other notable poets are </span><i><span lang=\"CS\">Vítězslav\r\n      Nezval, Vladimír Holan, </span><span lang=\"EN-US\">Frantiek Halas</span></i><span lang=\"EN-US\">,\r\n      <i>Jan Holub</i> and many others.</span></p>\r\n    </td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td width=\"99\" valign=\"top\" style=\"padding: 0cm 3.5pt; width: 74.4pt;\">\r\n      <p class=\"TableHeading2\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><b>Non-Fiction</b></span></p>\r\n    </td>\r\n    <td width=\"515\" valign=\"top\" style=\"padding: 0cm 3.5pt; width: 386.2pt;\">\r\n      <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><i><span lang=\"EN-US\">Jan\r\n      Patočka</span></i><span lang=\"EN-US\"> is the most prominent Czech\r\n      philosopher of this century.</span></p>\r\n    </td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td width=\"99\" valign=\"top\" style=\"padding: 0cm 3.5pt; width: 74.4pt;\">\r\n      <p class=\"TableHeading2\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><b>Classical Music-Opera</b></span></p>\r\n    </td>\r\n    <td width=\"515\" valign=\"top\" style=\"padding: 0cm 3.5pt; width: 386.2pt;\">\r\n      <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">There are basically five names in\r\n      classical music:</span></p>\r\n      <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><i><span lang=\"EN-US\">Bedřich\r\n      </span><span lang=\"CS\">Smetana, Antonín Dvořák,\r\n      Josef Suk, Leo Janáček </span></i><span lang=\"EN-US\">and <i>Bohuslav\r\n      Martinů</i>. Another popular work is Christmas Mass by <i>Jakub Ryba</i>.</span></p>\r\n    </td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td width=\"99\" valign=\"top\" style=\"padding: 0cm 3.5pt; width: 74.4pt;\">\r\n      <p class=\"TableHeading2\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><b>Folk</b></span></p>\r\n    </td>\r\n    <td width=\"515\" valign=\"top\" style=\"padding: 0cm 3.5pt; width: 386.2pt;\">\r\n      <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Folk singers are extremely popular\r\n      from the times of communism when they were considered a voice of freedom.\r\n      Here are the most well known names:</span></p>\r\n      <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><i><span lang=\"EN-US\">Jaromír\r\n      Nohavica, Karel Plíhal, Wabi Daněk, Jan Nedvěd, Jiří Dědeček</span></i></p>\r\n    </td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td width=\"99\" valign=\"top\" style=\"padding: 0cm 3.5pt; width: 74.4pt;\">\r\n      <p class=\"TableHeading2\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><b>Jazz</b></span></p>\r\n    </td>\r\n    <td width=\"515\" valign=\"top\" style=\"padding: 0cm 3.5pt; width: 386.2pt;\">\r\n      <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Czech jazz is typically very good.\r\n      It is little known fact that Jan Hammer is Czech.</span></p>\r\n      <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><i><span lang=\"CS\">Jiří\r\n      Stivín, Emil Viklický, Jan Kratochvíl, Jana Koubková, Martin Svoboda</span></i></p>\r\n    </td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td width=\"99\" valign=\"top\" style=\"padding: 0cm 3.5pt; width: 74.4pt;\">\r\n      <p class=\"TableHeading2\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><b>Rock/Pop</b></span></p>\r\n    </td>\r\n    <td width=\"515\" valign=\"top\" style=\"padding: 0cm 3.5pt; width: 386.2pt;\">\r\n      <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Here are some of the most popular\r\n      names from the 60s-80s still active today.</span></p>\r\n      <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><i><span lang=\"EN-US\">Olympic,\r\n      Katapult, Karel Gott, Praský Výběr, Hudba Praha, Laura a její\r\n      tygři</span></i></p>\r\n      <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">These are the most popular new\r\n      names.</span></p>\r\n      <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><i><span lang=\"EN-US\">Lucie,\r\n      Wanastowy věci, Daniel Hůlka, Lucie Bílá, Bára Basiková,\r\n      BUTY</span></i></p>\r\n    </td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td width=\"99\" valign=\"top\" style=\"padding: 0cm 3.5pt; width: 74.4pt;\">\r\n      <p class=\"TableHeading2\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><b>Movies</b></span></p>\r\n    </td>\r\n    <td width=\"515\" valign=\"top\" style=\"padding: 0cm 3.5pt; width: 386.2pt;\">\r\n      <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Oscar films: <i>Kolja, Closely Watched Trains</i></span></p>\r\n      <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Older films available with English\r\n      subtitles: <i>Larks on a String, Vesničko\r\n      má středisková, Limonádový Joe</i></span></p>\r\n      <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Post-communist films: <i>Obecná\r\n      kola, Akumulátor I., Je třeba zabít Sekala, </i>etc.</span></p>\r\n    </td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td width=\"99\" valign=\"top\" style=\"padding: 0cm 3.5pt; width: 74.4pt;\">\r\n      <p class=\"TableHeading2\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><b>Musicals</b></span></p>\r\n    </td>\r\n    <td width=\"515\" valign=\"top\" style=\"padding: 0cm 3.5pt; width: 386.2pt;\">\r\n      <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">There are many musicals currently\r\n      playing in Prague. The original Czech works of the 90s are <i>Dracula </i>and <i>Rusalka </i>(musical\r\n      inspired by Dvořáks famous opera).</span></p>\r\n    </td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td width=\"99\" valign=\"top\" style=\"padding: 0cm 3.5pt; width: 74.4pt;\">\r\n      <p class=\"TableHeading2\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><b>Drama</b></span></p>\r\n    </td>\r\n    <td width=\"515\" valign=\"top\" style=\"padding: 0cm 3.5pt; width: 386.2pt;\">\r\n      <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Drama requires the most language\r\n      knowledge and is often least accessible to a foreigner. For those with\r\n      good Czech ability, these theaters can be recommended:</span></p>\r\n      <p align=\"left\" style=\"text-align: left;\" class=\"MsoNormal\"><i><span lang=\"EN-US\">Divadlo Na Zábradlí, SEMAFOR, Divadlo Járy\r\n      Cimrmana, Národní Divadlo, Stavovské Divadlo, Divadlo Labyrint, </span></i><i><span lang=\"CS\">Činoherní klub</span></i></p>\r\n      <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Some Czech popular playwrights\r\n      are: <i>Václav Havel, Filip Topol,\r\n      Karel Čapek</i></span></p>\r\n    </td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n  <tr>\r\n    <td width=\"99\" valign=\"top\" style=\"padding: 0cm 3.5pt; width: 74.4pt;\">\r\n      <p class=\"TableHeading2\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><b>Sports</b></span></p>\r\n    </td>\r\n    <td width=\"515\" valign=\"top\" style=\"padding: 0cm 3.5pt; width: 386.2pt;\">\r\n      <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Some sports celebrities are still\r\n      famous, even though they have retired, and Czech Republic has had little\r\n      success in their particular field.</span></p>\r\n      <p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Ice-Hockey: <i>Jaromír Jágr</i>, <i>Dominik Haek</i>;\r\n      Football (soccer):<i> Antonín Panenka,\r\n      Jaroslav Chovanec</i>; Athletics: Emil Zátopek, Jarmila Kratochvílová;\r\n      Tennis: <i>Ivan Lendl, Jana Novotná,\r\n      Martina Navrátilová, Petr Korda</i></span></p>\r\n    </td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n</tbody></table>\r\n</p>', '2002-10-12 21:55:35', 5732, 31, 80),
(57, 'Czech Republic in Print', 'Dominik Luke', '<p class=\"NormalFirst\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">There are many books where you can\r\nread about the Czech Republic. Heres a short annotated list of some of the\r\nmore interesting books about life in the Czech Republic.', 'Many of these books are available from the <a href=\"bookstore/index.php\">Bohemica.com Bookstore</a>.<p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:6.0pt;margin-right:14.05pt;margin-bottom:\r\n0cm;margin-left:35.45pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><b style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight:\r\nnormal\"><i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style:normal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Czechs and\r\nBalances: Nations Survival Kit </span></i><span lang=\"EN-US\">by John Kuras<o:p>\r\n</o:p>\r\n</span></b></p>\r\n<p class=\"NormalFirst\" style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:14.05pt;margin-bottom:\r\n0cm;margin-left:35.45pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Witty and\r\nwell-informed if somewhat insensitive account of Czech character from a\r\nhistorical perspective. Written by a British journalist living and writing in\r\nthe Czech Republic.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:6.0pt;margin-right:14.05pt;margin-bottom:\r\n0cm;margin-left:35.45pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><b style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight:\r\nnormal\"><i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style:normal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Everything You\r\nAlways Wanted to Know About Czech </span></i><span lang=\"EN-US\">by Karen Kunes<o:p>\r\n</o:p>\r\n</span></b></p>\r\n<p class=\"NormalFirst\" style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:14.05pt;margin-bottom:\r\n0cm;margin-left:35.45pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Collection of\r\nshort essays about the Czech language published in the Prague Post. Cannot be\r\nused as a textbook but has much interesting information.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:6.0pt;margin-right:14.05pt;margin-bottom:\r\n0cm;margin-left:35.45pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><b style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight:\r\nnormal\"><i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style:normal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Bridging the\r\nGap </span></i><span lang=\"EN-US\">by Grace Hammot and Anna Nováková<o:p>\r\n</o:p>\r\n</span></b></p>\r\n<p class=\"NormalFirst\" style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:14.05pt;margin-bottom:\r\n0cm;margin-left:35.45pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">One of the\r\nfirst, if not the first, books on Czech culture and life from an expatriate\r\nperspective. It is out of print but well worth reading if you can find it.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:6.0pt;margin-right:14.05pt;margin-bottom:\r\n0cm;margin-left:35.45pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><b style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight:\r\nnormal\"><i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style:normal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">For the Love of\r\nPrague </span></i><span lang=\"EN-US\">by Gene Deitch<o:p>\r\n</o:p>\r\n</span></b></p>\r\n<p class=\"NormalFirst\" style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:14.05pt;margin-bottom:\r\n0cm;margin-left:35.45pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Written by an\r\nAmerican cartoon film director whos lived in the Czech Republic for forty\r\nyears. Describes his personal relationships and impressions.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:6.0pt;margin-right:14.05pt;margin-bottom:\r\n0cm;margin-left:35.45pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><b style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight:\r\nnormal\"><i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style:normal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">An Outline of\r\nCzech History</span></i><span lang=\"EN-US\"> by Petr Čornej<o:p>\r\n</o:p>\r\n</span></b></p>\r\n<p class=\"NormalFirst\" style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:14.05pt;margin-bottom:\r\n0cm;margin-left:35.45pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Brief,\r\nobjective and fairly comprehensive booklet written by a leading Czech historian.\r\nAvailable also in other languages.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:6.0pt;margin-right:14.05pt;margin-bottom:\r\n0cm;margin-left:35.45pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><b style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight:\r\nnormal\"><i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style:normal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Coasts of\r\nBohemia: A Czech History </span></i><span lang=\"EN-US\">by Derek Sayer <o:p>\r\n</o:p>\r\n</span></b></p>\r\n<p class=\"NormalFirst\" style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:14.05pt;margin-bottom:\r\n0cm;margin-left:35.45pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Most recent\r\noriginal account of Czech history in English. Shows Czech history in the context\r\nof cultural events. Title a variation on famous Shakespeares sentence\r\nmistakenly attributing a coast to Bohemia.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:6.0pt;margin-right:14.05pt;margin-bottom:\r\n0cm;margin-left:35.45pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><i><b><span style=\"mso-ansi-language: CS; mso-bidi-font-style: normal; mso-bidi-font-weight: normal\" lang=\"CS\">Customs\r\nand Ettiquette in the Czech Republic</span></b></i><b style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight:\r\nnormal\"><i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style:normal\"><span lang=\"CS\" style=\"mso-ansi-language:\r\nCS\"><i><b>: </b></i> Czech Republic </span></i><span lang=\"CS\" style=\"mso-ansi-language:CS\">by</span><span lang=\"EN-US\">\r\n David\r\n</span></b><span lang=\"EN-US\">\r\n<b style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal\">Short</b>\r\n</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"NormalFirst\" style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:14.05pt;margin-bottom:\r\n0cm;margin-left:35.45pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Excellent\r\nintroduction to Czech manners and habits. Friendly, pocket-sized books to get\r\nyou started. Slightly dated in some practical matters.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:6.0pt;margin-right:14.05pt;margin-bottom:\r\n0cm;margin-left:35.45pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><b style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight:\r\nnormal\"><i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style:normal\"><span lang=\"CS\" style=\"mso-ansi-language:\r\nCS\">Culture Shock: Czech Republic </span></i><span lang=\"CS\" style=\"mso-ansi-language:CS\">by</span><span lang=\"EN-US\">\r\nTim Nollen<o:p>\r\n</o:p>\r\n</span></b></p>\r\n<p class=\"NormalFirst\" style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:14.05pt;margin-bottom:\r\n0cm;margin-left:35.45pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Part of\r\nwell-known series. Provides much useful and accurate information. Sometimes the\r\naccount is a little too one sided. Slightly dated in some practical matters,\r\nmost notably housing.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:6.0pt;margin-right:14.05pt;margin-bottom:\r\n0cm;margin-left:35.45pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><b style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight:\r\nnormal\"><i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style:normal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Czechoslovak\r\nCookbook </span></i><span lang=\"EN-US\">by Jo</span><span lang=\"CS\" style=\"mso-ansi-language:CS\"></span><span lang=\"EN-US\">a\r\nBřízová et al.<o:p>\r\n</o:p>\r\n</span></b></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:14.05pt;margin-bottom:\r\n0cm;margin-left:35.45pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Title says it\r\nall. For those who like Czech food and wish to inflict it upon themselves.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:6.0pt;margin-right:14.05pt;margin-bottom:\r\n0cm;margin-left:35.45pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><b style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight:\r\nnormal\"><i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style:normal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Old Czech\r\nLegends</span></i><span lang=\"EN-US\"> by Alois Jirásek<o:p>\r\n</o:p>\r\n</span></b></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:14.05pt;margin-bottom:\r\n0cm;margin-left:35.45pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Translation of\r\na 19<sup>th</sup> century book of old Czech legends. Patently historically\r\ninaccurate but well known (if not actually read) by most Czechs.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:6.0pt;margin-right:14.05pt;margin-bottom:\r\n0cm;margin-left:35.45pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><b style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight:\r\nnormal\"><i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style:normal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Czech Republic\r\nBusiness Guide<o:p>\r\n</o:p>\r\n</span></i></b></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:14.05pt;margin-bottom:\r\n0cm;margin-left:35.45pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Collection of\r\npractical advise for all expatriates with relevant listings in many categories.\r\nPublished annually.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:6.0pt;margin-right:14.05pt;margin-bottom:\r\n0cm;margin-left:35.45pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><b style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight:\r\nnormal\"><i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style:normal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">EveryDay Prague<o:p>\r\n</o:p>\r\n</span></i></b></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:14.05pt;margin-bottom:\r\n0cm;margin-left:35.45pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Listings of\r\nservices in various categories. Comes with a useful discount card.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:6.0pt;margin-right:14.05pt;margin-bottom:\r\n0cm;margin-left:35.45pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><b style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight:\r\nnormal\"><i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style:normal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Prague\r\nPhoneBook<o:p>\r\n</o:p>\r\n</span></i></b></p>\r\n<p class=\"NormalFirst\" style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:14.05pt;margin-bottom:\r\n0cm;margin-left:35.45pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Expat oriented\r\nphonebook and yellow pages.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-top:6.0pt;margin-right:14.05pt;margin-bottom:\r\n0cm;margin-left:35.45pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><b style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight:\r\nnormal\"><i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style:normal\"><span lang=\"CS\" style=\"mso-ansi-language:\r\nCS\">Lonely Planet Prague<o:p>\r\n</o:p>\r\n</span></i></b></p>\r\n<p class=\"NormalFirst\" style=\"margin-top:0cm;margin-right:14.05pt;margin-bottom:\r\n0cm;margin-left:35.45pt;margin-bottom:.0001pt\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">A very\r\naccurate guide for short stays in Prague. Part of well known series.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"> Many works by Czech writers have\r\nbeen translated into English and other languages.</span></p>\r\n<p align=\"center\"> </p>', '2002-10-12 21:57:35', 3389, 31, 90);
INSERT INTO `xc_articles` (`xca_id`, `xca_name`, `xca_author`, `xca_perex`, `xca_text`, `xca_time`, `xca_readers`, `xca_section`, `xca_priority`) VALUES
(58, 'Czech Republic on the Internet', 'Dominik Luke', 'Basic links for more facts about the Czech Republic. More in the <a href=links/index.php>Links</a> section.', '<p class=\"NormalFirst\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">This list is necessarily incomplete,\r\nand moreover it is constantly changing and expanding. For more information use\r\none of the Czech search engines, although general engines such as Google or\r\nAltavista will have much of the information. A list of links geared towards\r\nlanguage learners can be found in the <a href=\"../../links.htm\">Bohemica.com\r\nLinks</a> section.</span></p>\r\n<div align=\"center\">\r\n  <center>\r\n  <table border=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\r\n mso-table-layout-alt:fixed;mso-padding-alt:0cm 3.5pt 0cm 3.5pt\">\r\n    <tr>\r\n      <td width=\"146\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:109.85pt;padding:0cm 3.5pt 0cm 3.5pt\">\r\n        <p class=\"TableHeading1\"><b><a name=\"_Toc442241313\"></a><a name=\"_Toc442241514\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc442241313\">Country\r\n        Domain</span></a><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:14.0pt;mso-bidi-font-size:10.0pt\">\r\n        \r\n        </span></b></p>\r\n      </td>\r\n      <td width=\"170\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:127.55pt;padding:0cm 3.5pt 0cm 3.5pt\">\r\n        <p class=\"TableNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">.cz</span></p>\r\n      </td>\r\n      <td width=\"297\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:223.1pt;padding:0cm 3.5pt 0cm 3.5pt\">\r\n        <p class=\"TableNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Some businesses use .com,\r\n        however. The domain name for Slovakia is .sk.</span></p>\r\n      </td>\r\n    </tr>\r\n    <tr>\r\n      <td width=\"146\" valign=\"top\" style=\"width:109.85pt;padding:0cm 3.5pt 0cm 3.5pt\">\r\n        <p class=\"TableHeading1\"><b><a name=\"_Toc442241314\"></a><a name=\"_Toc442241515\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc442241314\">Search\r\n        Engines</span></a></b