(189, 'Selected Bibliography of Cognitive Linguistics 1980-2005', 'Dominik Luke', '<p>Cognitive Linguistics has now been around for a quarter of a century (if we take the 1980 publication of Lakoff and Johnson\'s <em>Metaphors we live by</em>\r\n as a sort of a milestone). This \'commemorative\' bibliography contains almost a 100 key publications in the field. Most of the items are monographs but several papers of special importance (or of interest to Slavists) have also been included. Several entries, most notably the <em>Oxford Handbook of Cognitive Linguistics </em>\r\nand <em>The Cognitive Linguistics Reader </em>\r\nand <em>Glossary</em>\r\n, are listed as \'to appear\'. Reminders of omissions and errors are more than welcome.</p>\r\n', '<p>This list as been culled from an overview of cognitive linguistics I wrote in Czech as an afterword to my Czech translation of Lakoff\'s 1987 <em>Women, Fire, and Dangerous Things.</em>\r\n See <a href=\"http://www.bohemica.com/lakoff\">http://www.bohemica.com/lakoff</a>\r\n. <br />\r\n<br />\r\nThe list is unsorted and none of the entries are annotated (hopefully the next step). A much shorter but annotated and categorized bibliography compiled by Richard Hudson can be found on <a href=\"http://cogweb.ucla.edu/CogSci/CogLingLit.html\">http://cogweb.ucla.edu/CogSci/CogLingLit.html</a>\r\n&nbsp;another online bibliography which however takes a broader definition of cognitive linguistics is on <a href=\"http://www.uni-saarland.de/fak4/norrick/down/pastseminars/hscogling_bib.pdf\">http://www.uni-saarland.de/fak4/norrick/down/pastseminars/hscogling_bib.pdf</a>\r\n. Further links to CogLing resources can be found on <a href=\"http://www.cognitivelinguistics.org/research.shtml\">http://www.cognitivelinguistics.org/research.shtml</a>\r\n. </p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt 36pt; TEXT-INDENT: -36pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left\" align=\"left\"><span lang=\"PL\" style=\"mso-ansi-language: PL\">Barcelona, Antonio ed. 2000. </span>\r\n<i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Metaphor and metonymy at the crossroads: a cognitive perspective</span>\r\n </i>\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\">. Berlin: Mouton de Gruyter.</span>\r\n </p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt 36pt; TEXT-INDENT: -36pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left\" align=\"left\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Barnden, John, Mark Lee, and Katja Markert eds. 2001. <i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal\">Proceedings of the workshop on corpus-based and processing approaches to figurative language: held in conjunction with Corpus Linguistics 2001</i>\r\n . <i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal\">University Centre for Computer Corpus Research on Language technical papers; v. 14, special issue</i>\r\n . Lancaster: UCREL.</span>\r\n </p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt 36pt; TEXT-INDENT: -36pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left\" align=\"left\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Barnden, John ed. 2003. <i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal\">Proceedings of the Interdisciplinary Workshop on Corpus-Based Approaches to Figurative Language, 27 March 2003: held in conjunction with the Corpus Linguistics 2003 conference</i>\r\n . <i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal\">Technical papers (University of Lancaster. University Centre for Computer Corpus Research on Language); v. 18, special issue</i>\r\n . Lancaster: UCREL.</span>\r\n </p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt 36pt; TEXT-INDENT: -36pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left\" align=\"left\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Cameron, Lynne, and Graham Low eds. 1999. <i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal\">Researching and applying metaphor</i>\r\n . <i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal\">The Cambridge applied linguistics series</i>\r\n . Cambridge: Cambridge University Press.</span>\r\n </p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt 36pt; TEXT-INDENT: -36pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left\" align=\"left\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Charteris-Black, Jonathan. 2004. <i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal\">Corpus approaches to critical metaphor analysis</i>\r\n . Basingstoke: Palgrave Macmillan.</span>\r\n </p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt 36pt; TEXT-INDENT: -36pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left\" align=\"left\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Chilton, Paul. 1996. <i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal\">Security metaphors: Cold War discourse from containment to common house</i>\r\n : Conflict and consciousness; v.2. New York: Peter Lang.</span>\r\n </p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt 36pt; TEXT-INDENT: -36pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left\" align=\"left\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Coulson, Seana, and Todd Oakley. 2000. Blending basics. <i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal\">Cognitive Linguistics</i>\r\n 11:175-96.</span>\r\n </p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt 36pt; TEXT-INDENT: -36pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left\" align=\"left\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Croft, William. 2001. <i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal\">Radical construction grammar: Syntactic theory in typological perspective</i>\r\n : Oxford Linguistics. Oxford: Oxford University Press.</span>\r\n </p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt 36pt; TEXT-INDENT: -36pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left\" align=\"left\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Croft, William, and D. Alan Cruse. 2004. <i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal\">Cognitive linguistics</i>\r\n : Cambridge textbooks in linguistics. Cambridge: Cambridge University Press.</span>\r\n </p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt 36pt; TEXT-INDENT: -36pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left\" align=\"left\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Cuyckens, H., René Dirven, and John R. Taylor eds. 2003. <i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal\">Cognitive approaches to lexical semantics</i>\r\n . <i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal\">Cognitive linguistics research; 23</i>\r\n . Berlin; New York: Mouton de Gruyter.</span>\r\n </p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt 36pt; TEXT-INDENT: -36pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left\" align=\"left\"><span lang=\"EN-US\