MsoNormal\" style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt 36pt; TEXT-INDENT: -36pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left\" align=\"left\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Rudzka-Ostyn, Brygida ed. 1988. <i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal\">Topics in cognitive linguistics</i>\r\n . <i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal\">Amsterdam studies in the theory and history of linguistic science. Series 4, Current issues in linguistic theory; v.50</i>\r\n . Amsterdam: Benjamins.</span>\r\n </p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt 36pt; TEXT-INDENT: -36pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left\" align=\"left\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Rudzka-Ostyn, Brygida. 2003. <i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal\">Word power: phrasal verbs and compounds; a cognitive approach</i>\r\n : Planet communication. Berlin: Mouton de Gruyter.</span>\r\n </p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt 36pt; TEXT-INDENT: -36pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left\" align=\"left\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Semino, Elena, and Jonathan Culpeper eds. 2002. <i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal\">Cognitive stylistics: language and cognition in text analysis</i>\r\n . <i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal\">Linguistic approaches to literature; v. 1</i>\r\n . Amsterdam: John Benjamins.</span>\r\n </p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt 36pt; TEXT-INDENT: -36pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left\" align=\"left\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Sinha, Chris. to appear. Cognitive linguistics, psychology and cognitive science. In <i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal\">Hanbook of cognitive linguistics</i>\r\n , eds. Geeraerts, Dirk a Hubert Cuyckens. Oxford: Oxford University Press.</span>\r\n </p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt 36pt; TEXT-INDENT: -36pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left\" align=\"left\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Stockwell, Peter. 2002. <i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal\">Cognitive poetics: an introduction</i>\r\n . London; New York: Routledge.</span>\r\n </p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt 36pt; TEXT-INDENT: -36pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left\" align=\"left\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Sweetser, Eve. 1990. <i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal\">From etymology to pragmatics: metaphorical and cultural aspects of semantic structure</i>\r\n : Cambridge studies in linguistics; 54. Cambridge: Cambridge University Press.</span>\r\n </p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt 36pt; TEXT-INDENT: -36pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left\" align=\"left\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Tabakowska, Elzbieta. 1993. <i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal\">Cognitive linguistics and poetics of translation</i>\r\n : Language in performance; 9. Tubingen: G. Narr.</span>\r\n </p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt 36pt; TEXT-INDENT: -36pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left\" align=\"left\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Talmy, Leonard. 2000. <i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal\">Toward a cognitive semantics</i>\r\n . Cambridge, Mass.; London: MIT Press.</span>\r\n </p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt 36pt; TEXT-INDENT: -36pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left\" align=\"left\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Taylor, John R. 1995. <i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal\">Linguistic categorization: prototypes in linguistic theory</i>\r\n . Oxford: Oxford University Press.</span>\r\n </p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt 36pt; TEXT-INDENT: -36pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left\" align=\"left\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Taylor, John R., and Robert E. MacLaury eds. 1995. <i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal\">Language and the cognitive construal of the world</i>\r\n . <i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal\">Trends in linguistics. Studies and monographs; Vol.82</i>\r\n . Berlin: De Gruyter.</span>\r\n </p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt 36pt; TEXT-INDENT: -36pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left\" align=\"left\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Taylor, John R. 2002. <i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal\">Cognitive grammar</i>\r\n : Oxford linguistics. Oxford: Oxford University Press.</span>\r\n </p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt 36pt; TEXT-INDENT: -36pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left\" align=\"left\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Turner, Mark. 1987. <i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal\">Death is the mother of beauty: mind, metaphor, criticism</i>\r\n . Chicago; London: University of Chicago Press.</span>\r\n </p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt 36pt; TEXT-INDENT: -36pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left\" align=\"left\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Turner, Mark. 1996. <i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal\">The literary mind</i>\r\n . New York; Oxford: Oxford University Press.</span>\r\n </p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt 36pt; TEXT-INDENT: -36pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left\" align=\"left\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Turner, Mark. 2001. <i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal\">Cognitive dimensions of social science</i>\r\n . Oxford, UK; New York: Oxford University Press.</span>\r\n </p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt 36pt; TEXT-INDENT: -36pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left\" align=\"left\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Ungerer, Friedrich, and Hans-Jörg Schmid. 1996. <i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal\">An introduction to cognitive linguistics</i>\r\n : Learning about language. London; New York: Longman.</span>\r\n </p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0cm 0pt 36pt; TEXT-INDENT: -36pt; TEXT-ALIGN: left\" align=\"left\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">van Hoek, Karen. 1997. <i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal\">Anaphora and conceptual structure</i>\r\n : Cognitive theory of language and culture. Chicago: University of Chicago Press.</span>\r\n </p>\r\n', '2005-06-14 20:12:42', 4224, 14, 10);
INSERT INTO `xc_articles` (`xca_id`, `xca_name`, `xca_author`, `xca_perex`, `xca_text`, `xca_time`, `xca_readers`, `xca_section`, `xca_priority`) VALUES
(193, '', '', '\r\n<br />\r\n', '\r\n<center><h2>TRANSLATOR DATABASE</h2>\r\n</center>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p><hr />\r\n<p><b>Petr Adámek </b>\r\n<br />\r\nPřesličková 2679, 106 00 Praha 10<br />\r\n<a href=\"mailto:padamek@chello.cz\">padamek@chello.cz</a><br />\r\n606 226 316 <br />\r\nGeneral science and technology, chemistry, nuclear, environmental</p>\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><b>Zdeněk Bobek</b>\r\n <br />\r\nFibichova 39, Adamov, PSČ 679 04, Czech Republic <br />\r\nMobile: +420 603 844 754 <br />\r\nCompany ID No.: 462 48 927 <br />\r\n<a href=\"mailto:zdenek.bobek@tiscali.cz\">zdenek.bobek@tiscali.cz</a>\r\n <br />\r\n<a href=\"http://clix.to/anglos\">http://clix.to/anglos</a>\r\n <br />\r\nor <br />\r\n<a href=\"http://sweb.cz/zdenek24\">http://sweb.cz/zdenek24</a>\r\n <br />\r\nFreelance translator, interpreter and tutor since 1993. <br />\r\nActivities: <br />\r\nEnglish lessons <br />\r\nCzech for foreigners <br />\r\nEnglish-Czech and Czech-English translation services <br />\r\nInterpreting <br />\r\nI am experienced in the following fields: <br />\r\nmechanical engineering, civil engineering, information technologies, computer graphic, business correspondence, trade negotiations, geology, brick and tile industry, linguistics. </p>\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><b>Jirka Bolech</b>\r\n <br />\r\nFranklinova 729, Liberec, 46005, Czech Republic <br />\r\n<a href=\"http://www.bangl.cz\">http://www.bangl.cz</a>\r\n , <br />\r\n<a href=\"mailto:jirka@bangl.cz\">jirka@bangl.cz</a>\r\n <br />\r\n+420-724240580 <br />\r\nEnglish to Czech: electronics, computers, business and much more... </p>\r\n<hr />\r\n<a name=\"mbc\"></a><p><a name=\"mbc\"><b>Melvyn Clarke</b>\r\n <br />Skype: zehrovak2<br /></a><a href=\"mailto:zehrovak@gmail.com\">zehrovak@gmail.com</a> <br /><br />Legal, commercial, journalism, advertising and marketing, librarianship, archive work, literature, non-fiction, accounting, meteorology, town planning, linguistics, banking, construction,  education, entertainment, theatre, video, cinema, food and drink (menus), hotels and catering, human resources, IT, insurance, publishing, water management, tourism, sports. <br />\r\n <br />\r\nLiving and working in CZ since 1990. BA Czech and Slovak  School of Slavonic and East European Studies in London. My work is reviewed by Hana Jirkalová, my Czech partner, who for over 25 years has been Editor-in-Chief of Ctenář, a professional magazine for librarians. Together we translated Who Invented, Discovered, Made the First... (<a href=\"http://katalog.kjm.cz/eng/l.dll?cll~10001468\">Kdo první vynalezl, objevil, vyrobil</a>) by Kenneth Ireland (the first draft into Czech was mine) and other non-fiction. I also work together with Stanislava Kellnerová (below) and occasionally consult other translators on this list regarding specialist terminology problems and nuance issues. <br />\r\n<br />\r\n\r\nClients include the Office of the President, the Senate of the Czech Parliament, the Academy of Sciences Archive, Institute of Czech Literature, Institute of Slavonic Studies, Czech TV, Czech Radio, Patria Finance and Sitel.<br />\r\n<br />\r\nReferences available upon request. Annotated samples of my translation work can be found at: <a href=\" http://www.bohemica.com/czechparallel\">http://www.bohemica.com/czechparallel</a>\r\n</p>\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><strong>Michal Činčiala</strong>\r\n <br />\r\nN. Frýda 6, 700 30 Ostrava<br />\r\nTel./fax: 596-721-061<br />\r\nMobil: 603-410-754<br />\r\nURL: <a href=\"http://www.cinciala.cz\">http://www.cinciala.cz</a>\r\n <br />\r\nICQ: 299498940<br />\r\nFreelance translator since 1994<br />\r\nTechnical translations, contracts, legal translations</p>\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><b>Gabriela Fiserova</b>\r\n <br />\r\n206 South Fifth Ave, Suite 175- Ann Arbor-MI- 48104<br />\r\nMobile: 734.709.3777<br /><a href=\"mailto:gabriela.fisherova@gmail.com\">gabriela.fisherova@gmail.com</a><br />\r\nExport-Import- international contract translations. International business. General. Experience: Tutor for students from Slavic Department @University of Michigan. Translated during Science Fair in Detroit 2000. </p>\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><b>Alexej Havlíček</b>\r\n <br />\r\nNad pilou 49, 273 51 Kyice <br />\r\ntel: +420 602 219 029 <br />\r\nfax: +420 602 682 411 <br />\r\n<a href=\"mailto:ahavlicek@volny.cz\">ahavlicek@volny.cz</a>\r\n <br />\r\nFreelance translator since 1972 with experience in the following fields: financial, general economics, legal, mechanical engineering, IT, EU legislation. Over 10 years experience as investment banker and IT manager with Credit Suisse First Boston. </p>\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><b>Alena Jetelinová</b>\r\n <br />\r\nLipovec 128, CZ-679 15; 405 N. Wabash #1104, Chicago,IL <br />\r\n<a href=\"mailto:czech@translator.zzn.com\">czech@translator.zzn.com</a>\r\n <br />\r\n<a href=\"mailto:a_jetelinova@yahoo.com\">a_jetelinova@yahoo.com</a>\r\n <br />\r\n604/ 131 139, (+1) 312- 282- 1420 <br />\r\nCommercial, legal, general, food &amp; menu, correspondence </p>\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><b>Stanislava Kellnerová</b>\r\n <br />\r\nHackerova 3, 181 00 Praha 8 <br />\r\n<a href=\"mailto:skellnerova@volny.cz\">skellnerova@volny.cz</a>\r\n <br />\r\n604 30 11 95 <br />\r\nCopyright law, general legal, commercial and technical. <br />\r\nI have translated several plays including Master Class by Terrence McNally (performed at Viola, Praha), Key for Two by John Chapman and David Freeman (performed at Skelet, Praha) and Murder by Sex by Joan Shirley (performed at U hasičů, Praha). </p>\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><b>Liba Khan</b>\r\n <br />\r\nChuderov 121, Usti nad Labem/ West Lodge, Sunningdale, UK <br />\r\n<a href=\"mailto:Jetlk@aol.com\">Jetlk@aol.com</a>\r\n <br />\r\n603 140525 <br />\r\nMedical, legal and general. </p>\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><b>Zuzana Kočičková</b>\r\n <br />\r\nStřelniční 518 <br />\r\n793 26 Vrbno pod Pradědem <br />\r\nLegal, commercial, general technical, chemistry. I have worked as a translator since 1993. </p>\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><b>Robert Morrison</b>\r\n <br />\r\nPohořelec 3, 118 00 Praha <br />\r\n<a href=\"mailto:robert_s_morrison@yahoo.com\">robert_s_morrison@yahoo.com</a>\r\n <br />\r\nMobile: +420 602 357 673<br />\r\nFax: +420 233 353 991<br />\r\nCzech Commercial Registry ID: 7105 0523<br />\r\nCzech to English Translations <br />\r\nExperience: translator for marketing presentations, technology, real estate, culture, business correspondence, and contracts <br />\r\nBackground: more than 11 years of business and living experience in the Czech Republic, native English speaker with fluent Czech, references availableCAT Tools: TRADOS 6 Freelance and Multiterm 5.5 with an extensive Czech to English translation memory and termbase.</p>\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><b>Radovan Pletka</b>\r\n <br />\r\nCzech and Slovak Services, 180 Crestwood East, Prescott, AZ 86303, USA <br />\r\n<a href=\"mailto:pletka@czechtranslation.com\">pletka@czechtranslation.com</a>\r\n <br />\r\n<a href=\"mailto:RPletka@aol.com\">RPletka@aol.com</a>\r\n <br />\r\n928 445 3259, E- fax 561 423 8233, Mobile phone 703 980 8554 <br />\r\n<a href=\"http://www.czechtranslation.com\">http://www.czechtranslation.com</a>\r\n <br />\r\nContracts, business documents, letters and other materials for American companies doing business in Czech and Slovak Republics, technical translation, including nuclear powerplant contracts, textile patents and agricultural, medical, banking and computer materials. Translations of manuals and other materials for government agencies and U.S. companies, Translation and revision of Czechoslovak statutes and agreements for the U.S. Department of State and several D.C. law firms. Freelance conference interpreter for Department of State, including interpreting for President Clinton during his visit to the Czech Republic in January 1994. Consecutive or simultaneous interpreter for a number of Czech and Slovak delegations - journalists, supreme court judges, mayors, university deans, health care professionals, etc. - in the U.S. for USIA and other agency programs. Publisher of the famous weekly job list for translators/interpreters For more info see <a title=\"Linkification: http://www.jobsfortranslators.com\" href=\"http://www.jobsfortranslators.com\" class=\"linkification-ext\">www.jobsfortranslators.com</a> Feel free to request a sample (-: </p>\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><b>Ondřej Roldan</b>\r\n <br />\r\nVlastislavova 22, Praha 4, 140 00 <br />\r\n<a href=\"mailto:roldan@seznam.cz\">roldan@seznam.cz</a>\r\n<br />\r\n<a href=\"mailto:diplodok@seznam.cz\">diplodok@seznam.cz</a>\r\n <br />\r\n777 242 674 <br />\r\n241 740 706 <br />\r\nBusiness, banking&amp;finance, contracts&amp;law, advertising, technical (esp. aerospace industry), historical science, librarianship, general <br />\r\nTranslating and interpreting since 1993. Just for the record, my second B/C language is Spanish. </p>\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><b>árka Rubková</b>\r\n <br />\r\nSibeliova 1001/23, 16200 Praha 6, Czech Republic <br />\r\nPhone: 0420 220518582 <br />\r\nMobile: 0420 605 446504 <br />\r\nFax: 0420 220518581 <br />\r\nFreelance interpreter and translator since 1983. <br />\r\nTranslation of training programmes and hand-outs for various Phare programmes and companies. <br />\r\nLiterary translations (Geoffrey Regan: Guinness Book of Military Blunders (Guinnessova kniha válečných omylů), published by Velryba, Jungmannova ul. 3, Praha; Weather and Climate (Tajemství podnebí), published by Velryba Publishing House, Jungmannova ul. 3, Praha 1 and others). <br />\r\nGeneral and technical translations (architecture, art, civil engineering including all necessary trades, town planning, landscaping, history of art, sports - canoing, quality management, paper industry, wood industry, forestry, telecommunications, mechanical engineering, automotive industry, power plants, computers, software; banking, etc.) <br />\r\nInterpreting both simultaneous and consecutive (courses, conferences, business affairs and negotiations, banking and accountancy, civil engineering, architecture, light engineering, power plants, etc.) </p>\r\n<hr />\r\n<strong>Vít Růička<br /><span style=\"font-weight: normal;\">Prague, Czech Republic</span><br /><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\"></span>+420 731 700054<br /><span style=\"font-weight: normal;\"></span></strong><strong><span style=\"font-weight: normal;\"></span><a href=\"mailto:translations@vegadata.cz\">translations@vegadata.cz</a><br style=\"font-weight: normal;\" /><span style=\"font-weight: normal;\"><a href=\"http://www.vegadata.cz\">http://www.vegadata.cz</a></span><br style=\"font-weight: normal;\" /><span style=\"font-weight: normal;\">Hi-technology, aircraft, nuclear industry, accounting, immunology, miscellaneous</span><br /></strong><hr /><strong><br />Miluse Saskova-Pierce<br />\r\n</strong>\r\n<a href=\" http://www.bohemica.com/index.php?m=catalog&s=258&a=170\">See CV</a>\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><strong>Patrick Seguin</strong>\r\n <br />\r\nBryksova 666/4, 198 00 Prague 9<br />\r\n<a href=\"mailto:transloris@seznam.cz\">transloris@seznam.cz</a>\r\n<br />\r\n(+420) 775 119 995</p>\r\n<p>Freelance translator (Czech to English, English to Czech, French to<br />\r\nEnglish), copywriter and editor specialising in telecommunications and<br />\r\nadvertising and marketing. Also very skilled at translating literature and<br />\r\nnon-fiction, legal documents and business correspondence. </p>\r\n<p>References and samples for translations available on request. Part of my<br />\r\nwriting and editing portfolio can be seen at <a href=\"http://www.prague-spot.com/blog\">www.prague-spot.com/blog</a>\r\n.</p>\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><b>Martina Silpoch</b>\r\n <br />\r\n1512 Grant Rd. St. Louis, MO 63119 <br />\r\n<a href=\"mailto:mmsilpoch@earthlink.net\">mmsilpoch@earthlink.net</a>\r\n <br />\r\nTranslations - general, technical, legal, educational materials, personal and business correspondence, documents, manuals (since 1985) <br />\r\nCourt interpreting in the US (since 1990) <br />\r\nTeaching Czech in St. Louis, MO area - private or through several local agencies (since 1990) </p>\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><b>Tomá Skřont</b>\r\n <br />\r\nKurzova 12/ 2224, 155 00 Prague 5 <br />\r\n<a href=\"mailto:skront@chello.cz\">skront@chello.cz</a>\r\n <br />\r\n<a href=\"mailto:tskront@volny.cz\">tskront@volny.cz</a>\r\n <br />\r\n420 2 56 156 77, 420 602 712 923 <br />\r\nEconomics, management, marketing, law, business contracts, correspondence, general, sports, informatics, communications <br />\r\n<a href=\"http://www.ekonomickepreklady.cz\">http://www.ekonomickepreklady.cz</a><br />\r\n </p>\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><b>Zuzana Slánská</b>\r\n <br />\r\nBelehradská 513/97, 530 09 Pardubice, Czech Republic<br />\r\nTel/Fax: +420 46 641 26 51<br />\r\nMobile phone: +420 603 164 831 <br /><a href=\"mailto:angita@volny.cz\">angita@volny.cz</a>  <a href=\"mailto:angita@seznam.cz\">angita@seznam.cz</a> <br /><a href=\"http://angita.euweb.cz\">http://angita.euweb.cz</a><br />ICQ: 232 286 161<br />\r\nEnglish-Czech, Czech-English, Italian-Czech, Czech-Italian and English-Italian translations, and Italian-Czech and Czech-Italian interpreting, Italian-Czech and Czech-Italian sworn translations and interpreting<br />\r\nTechnical translations, mechanical engineering, contracts, legal translations, commercial and general translations<br />\r\nFreelance translator and interpreter since 1991</p>\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><b>Pavel Storkan</b>\r\n <br />\r\nPod vodojemem 1597, Beroun 2, 266 01 <br />\r\n<a href=\"mailto:Alderan@lycos.com\">Alderan@lycos.com</a>\r\n <br />\r\n603- 262886 <br />\r\n311- 625542 <br />\r\nMechanical and electronic engineering, hardware and software, telecommunications, patent applications <br />\r\n<a href=\"http://Alderan.Tripod.com\">http://Alderan.Tripod.com</a>\r\n </p>\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><b>Jitka Subiková</b>\r\n <br />\r\nZolova 13, 783 01 Olomouc, Czech Republic <br />\r\nMobile: +420-608-123-350 <br />\r\nTel/fax: +420-585-433-148 <br />\r\nBusiness license No.: 733 01 124 <br />\r\n<a href=\"mailto:jitka88@volny.cz\">jitka88@volny.cz</a>\r\n <br />\r\nFreelance Czech/English translator and interpreter, various fields. </p>\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><b>Lenka Suková </b>\r\n<br />\r\nJagellonská 25, 130 00 Praha 3 - ikov <br />\r\n<a href=\"mailto:sukova.lenka@worldonline.cz\">sukova.lenka@worldonline.cz</a>\r\n <br />\r\n602/ 829651 <br />\r\nLaw (contracts), Business, Finance, Telecommunications, Audit <br />\r\nDegree in Hindi </p>\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><b>Martin Tlustý</b>\r\n <br />\r\n<a href=\"mailto:tlustymartin@volny.cz\">tlustymartin@volny.cz</a>\r\n <br />\r\n<a href=\"mailto:tlusty.martin@mbox.dkm.cz\">tlusty.martin@mbox.dkm.cz</a>\r\n <br />\r\nPhone: 272 912 787 (home), 222 510 164 (work) <br />\r\nMobile: 607 883 661 / 601 248 581 (only at home) <br />\r\n<a href=\"http://www.martin-tlusty.euweb.cz\">http://www.martin-tlusty.euweb.cz</a>\r\n <br />\r\n<a href=\"http://www.devitalizace.euweb.cz\">http://www.devitalizace.euweb.cz</a>\r\n <br />\r\nAddress: Michnova 2, Praha 4, 14900, Czech Republic <br />\r\nResume: <a href=\"http://www.martin-tlusty.euweb.cz/CV.htm\">http://www.martin-tlusty.euweb.cz/CV.htm</a>\r\n <br />\r\nTechnical (civil engineering, mechanical engineering etc.), scientific, general, <br />\r\nChristian texts. Eng&gt;Czech: above-average expressive abilities in Czech, <br />\r\nCzech &gt;Eng: adequate for technical texts, Refs available. <br />\r\nKaterina Tlusta, Martin Tlusty\'s wife: <br />\r\nProfessor of Czech &amp; writer, offers proof-reading of Czech texts <br />\r\n<a href=\"http://www.ester.euweb.cz\">http://www.ester.euweb.cz</a>\r\n <br />\r\n<a href=\"http://www.haj-tl.euweb.cz\">http://www.haj-tl.euweb.cz</a>\r\n <br />\r\n<a href=\"mailto:hajtl@volny.cz\">hajtl@volny.cz</a>\r\n <br />\r\n<a href=\"mailto:ktlusta@mbox.dkm.cz\">ktlusta@mbox.dkm.cz</a>\r\n <br />\r\nPhone: 233 325 557 (work), 732 546 618 (mobile) </p>\r\n<hr />\r\n<strong>Pavel Trusina</strong>\r\n <br />\r\nTranslator and interpreter specializing in pharmaceuticals.<br />\r\nFor all details see: <a href=\"http://www.pt.cz\">http://www.pt.cz</a>\r\n <br />\r\n<hr />\r\n<strong>Jaroslav Tupý, RNDr.</strong>\r\n <br />\r\nStonky 630<br />\r\nDům bytové kultury Uherské Hraditě<br />\r\nOtakarova 1253<br />\r\n686 01 Uherské Hraditě, Czech Republic<br />\r\nE-mail: <a href=\"mailto:dbk@dbk.cz\">dbk@dbk.cz</a>\r\n <br />\r\nCellPh: +420 777 340 384<br />\r\nFax: +420 572 555 066<br />\r\nEnglish/Czech translationsand interpreting: general, technical, business, law (contracts), finance, audit, certificates\r\n <hr />\r\n<p><b>Petr Veselý</b>\r\n <br />\r\nPlucárna 16, 695 01 Hodonín, Czech Republic <br />\r\n+420 608 667 188 <br />\r\n<a href=\"mailto:petr.vesely@centrum.cz\">petr.vesely@centrum.cz</a>\r\n <br />\r\nGeneral, technical, law (contracts), IT, business, finance <br />\r\n<br />\r\n</p>\r\n<hr />', '2005-07-02 16:52:39', 60187, 269, 127);
INSERT INTO `xc_linx` (`xcl_id`, `xcl_url`, `xcl_name`, `xcl_description`, `xcl_section`) VALUES
(4, 'http://www.masteringczech.com/czechkeyboard.html', 'http://www.masteringczech.com/czechkeyboard.html <img border=\"0\" src=\"images/excellent.gif\">', 'Instructions on how to install Czech keyboard on Windows 2000 (probably applies to XP as well).', 46),
(5, 'http://www.bohemica.com/czechonline', 'http://www.bohemica.com/czechonline', 'Contains detailed description of installing and using Czech keyboard included with Windows 9x.', 46),
(6, 'http://www.cestina.cz', 'http://www.cestina.cz <img border=0 src=images/excellent.gif>', 'Covering all aspects of encoding Czech on the internet. (In Czech only).', 46),
(7, 'http://clover.slavic.pitt.edu/~aatseel/keyboards.html', 'http://clover.slavic.pitt.edu/~aatseel/keyboards.html', 'Links to Slavonic fonts from American Association of Teachers of Slavic and East European Languages (AATSEEL).', 46),
(8, 'http://www.muselik.com/czech/fonts.html', 'http://www.muselik.com/czech/fonts.html', 'Czech info center points to most important font sources both for Windows and Macintosh.', 46),
(9, 'http://www.sil.org/computing/fonts/rf.htm', 'http://www.sil.org/computing/fonts/rf.htm', 'Many fonts including Czech. Czech fonts listed are only for Macintosh.', 46),
(10, 'http://www.ncsml.org', 'http://www.ncsml.org', 'A web site of the Czech and Slovak museum located in Cedar Rapids, Iowa.', 47),
(11, 'http://www.czechoslovaknews.org', 'http://www.czechoslovaknews.org', 'A clearing house of information for Czech and Slovak expatriates and those with business interests there. Also publishes the newsletter Czech & Slovak Connections. (Used to be czech.com).', 47),
(12, 'http://www.czechland.org', 'http://www.czechland.org', 'A Czech Culture-Heritage Web Site from Nebraska contains many useful links to expatriate sites around the world. Also a good starting place for genealogy.', 47),
(13, 'http://www.muselik.com', 'http://www.muselik.com', 'Provides extensive information about the Czech Republic in English.', 47),
(14, 'http://hurontaria.baf.cz/', 'http://hurontaria.baf.cz/', 'Hurontaria: A Czech expatriate forum in Canada. ', 47),
(15, 'http://www.czech-books.com', 'http://www.czech-books.com', 'Distributor of Czech books, mostly in the original, in the US.', 47),
(16, 'http://www.cesky-dialog.cz', 'http://www.cesky-dialog.cz', 'A magazine in Czech for expatriates around the world as well as patriots\r\nliving in the Czech Republic. ', 47),
(17, 'http://www.czech.cz', 'http://www.czech.cz', 'Czech foreign ministry\'s page contains links to Czech centers around\r\nthe world. ', 47),
(18, 'http://www.czech-republic.org', 'http://www.czech-republic.org', '<a href=\"http://www.kulturklub.cz\">http://www.kulturklub.cz</a>\r\nTwo sites for German-speaking expatriates promoting Czech and Sudeten-German\r\ncultural and heritage societies. Information in German and English. ', 47),
(19, 'http://www.telecom.cz', 'http://www.telecom.cz', 'This is an extremely useful tool for the initial stages of genealogy research. It is nothing else but the Czech Republic phonebook online. You can try searching for your name in different cities to see where it is most common.', 47),
(20, 'http://www.geocities.com/goodolejoe/indexf.html', 'http://www.geocities.com/goodolejoe/indexf.html', 'A great site dealing with Czech Texas heritage. It contains a sample of Texas Czech and lots of lyrics to Czech folklore and polka songs. There are also a few pictures of Czech national costumes as worn in Texas as well as some old Czech records in Real Audio.', 47),
(21, 'http://www.phil.muni.cz/info/courses/czech_for_foreigners.html', 'http://www.phil.muni.cz/info/courses/czech_for_foreigners.html', 'A variety of courses including a summer school at the Faculty of Arts at the Masaryk University of Brno (the second largest city of the Czech Republic and the unofficial capital of Moravia). ', 54),
(22, 'http://lsss.upol.cz', 'http://lsss.upol.cz', 'Summer School of Slavonic Studies organized by Palacký University in Olomouc (Moravia). ', 54),
(26, 'www.lang.uni-linz.ac.at', 'http://www.lang.uni-linz.ac.at', 'Course for German-speaking students held in České Budějovice organized by <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"http://www.uni-linz.ac.at\">Johannes Kepler Universität Linz.<b></b>Wirtschaftsraum Österreich - Tschechien. 7. - 20. 9. 2003</a>', 54),
(27, 'http://www.people.memphis.edu/~cehall/summer.html', 'http://www.people.memphis.edu/~cehall/summer.html', 'International Summer Language School at the University of West Bohemia in Pilsen (Plzeň - the home of the best of Czech beer). ', 54),
(29, 'http://www.jcu.cz/stud/cestina/cestina_en.html', 'http://www.jcu.cz/stud/cestina/cestina_en.html', 'Summer School at the University of South Bohemia in České Budějovice (the home of the original Budweiser near the beautiful UNESCO-protected Český Krumlov). ', 54),
(30, 'http://www.sfservis.com', 'http://www.sfservis.com/', 'Prague Summer University: summer school as well as year-long courses organized by SF Servis of the Student Council of Charles University Faculty of Philosophy. ', 55),
(31, 'http://www.pedf.cuni.cz/~www_kcj/kurz_e.htm', 'http://www.pedf.cuni.cz/~www_kcj/kurz_e.htm', 'A three-week course organized at the Faculty of Pedagogy in July 2001. Mostly for Prague residents but available to anybody. Caters to Russian speakers as well. ', 55),
(32, 'http://praha1.ff.cuni.cz/~holubj/ubs', 'http://praha1.ff.cuni.cz/~holubj/ubs', 'Summer School of Slavonic Studies and other courses organized by the Czech Department of the Charles University Faculty of Philosophy. ', 55),
(33, 'http://www.cuni.cz/cuni/ujop/czech.htm.en', 'http://www.cuni.cz/cuni/ujop/czech.htm.en', 'Also associated with Charles University some courses take place in Poděbrady a lovely spa town not far from Prague. Provides Czech as a foreign language training to prospective students at Czech Universities. ', 55),
(34, 'http://www.chp.cz', 'http://www.chp.cz', 'Jerome of Prague College offers a Summer Program of which Czech for Foreigners if just one part. This is in conjunction with their Semester Abroad for students at selected US universities. Materials from <a href=\"http://bohemica.com/czechonline\">http://www.bohemica.com/czechonline</a> are also used. ', 55),
(35, 'www.praguesummerschool.com', 'www.praguesummerschool.com', 'All sorts of courses organized by \'Prague Institute\'. Not much information about the institute was available and the prices seem slightly high. ', 55),
(36, 'http://www.seznam.cz', 'http://www.seznam.cz', '&quot;Czech Yahoo&quot; this is the most successful Czech web site with over 50000 hits a day (increasing constantly). Offers both full text search and search by category. Also hosts two news services <a href=\"http://dnes.seznam.cz\">http://dnes.seznam.cz</a> which summarizes news and relevant information from other sources and <a href=\"http://www.novinky.cz\">http://www.novinky.cz</a> . Also offers map search for major Czech cities. Offers web mail. ', 50),
(37, 'http://www.atlas.cz', 'http://www.atlas.cz', 'The second most important portal. Offers all that Seznam does and adds further services. Its services include: free web hosting, web mail, online radio, map search, news and video clips. ', 50),
(38, 'http://www.centrum.cz', 'http://www.centrum.cz', 'A thriving new portal with probably the best full-text search results on the Czech web. ', 50),
(39, 'http://www.czlist.com', 'http://www.czlist.com', 'New portal for tourists and expats. One of the few all in English (although it does have a Czech version). ', 50),
(40, 'http://www.expats.cz', 'http://www.expats.cz', 'A website for all foreigners that live - and will be relocating to - the Czech Republic. ', 50),
(41, 'http://www.czechonweb.cz', 'http://www.czechonweb.cz', 'Provides a whole range of information on the Czech Republic in English: geography, cuture, architecture, government, etc. ', 50),
(42, 'http://www.quick.cz', 'http://www.quick.cz', 'One of the newest portals established in September 2000 by Czech Telecom. Provides many resources including the phone book. Also offers free internet connections. ', 50),
(43, 'http://www.zlatestranky.cz', 'http://www.zlatestranky.cz', 'Czech Yellow Pages online. ', 50),
(44, 'http://www.praha.cz', 'http://www.praha.cz', 'Portal to sites and news related to Prague. ', 50),
(45, 'http://www.uzdroje.cz', 'http://www.uzdroje.cz', 'The very first portal, now largely forgotten, although still functional. ', 50),
(46, 'http://www.centraleurope.com', 'http://www.centraleurope.com', 'An English portal and news source for things Central European with an extensive Czech section. ', 50),
(47, 'http://www.slavophilia.com', 'http://www.slavophilia.com', 'A useful by-category search engine of all things Slavonic.  ', 50),
(48, 'http://www.radia.cz', 'http://www.radia.cz <img border=0 src=excellent.gif>', 'Radia (Radios) lists all Czech radios and newly TV stations both online and terrestrial. It contains links to many interesting sites. It\'s a great resource.', 56),
(49, 'http://www.radio.cz', 'http://www.radio.cz', 'Czech Radio broadcasts aimed abroad in several languages including Czech. It also offers daily email with a news summary in several languages. (Notice the URL differs from the above only in the last letter [Radio as opposed to Radio<b>s</b>]). ', 56),
(50, 'http://www.bbc.co.uk/czech', 'http://www.bbc.co.uk/czech', 'Broadcasts of the World Service in Czech. Also offers written news in Czech and English lessons for Czechs. Has some instructions in English. ', 56),
(51, 'http://www.voa.gov/czech', 'http://www.voa.gov/czech', 'Voice of America broadcasts in Czech. No special services available. ', 56),
(52, 'http://www.tv-nova.cz', 'http://www.tv-nova.cz', 'The largest commercial Czech TV station broadcasts selected programs online. ', 56),
(53, 'http://www.ct1.cz', 'http://www.ct1.cz', 'Czech public TV station broadcasts the news and other selected programs online. The site also contains an archive of news broadcasts. ', 56),
(54, 'http://tv.idnes.cz', 'http://tv.idnes.cz', 'An online-only channel of news broadcasts. You can also find clips from film trailers and other archive materials. ', 56),
(55, 'http://live.atlas.cz', 'http://live.atlas.cz', 'Archive of video material. Clips of interviews, sporting events, independent short films and children\'s TV. ', 56),
(56, 'http://www.bohemica.com/czechgrammar', 'http://www.bohemica.com/czechgrammar', 'Complete detailed grammar of Czech (still under development). Also includes a list of idioms, vocabulary tips and Czech trivia.', 12),
(57, 'http://www.seelrc.org/casebooks', 'http://www.seelrc.org/casebooks <img border=\"0\" src=\"images/excellent.gif\">', 'Detailed and erudite grammar of the Czech case system focusing on meaning by Laura Janda. (In PDF). The site also contains additional Czech exercises with more being developed. ', 12),
(58, 'http://mujweb.cz/www/grammarcz', 'http://mujweb.cz/www/grammarcz <img border=\"0\" src=\"images/excellent.gif\">', 'Good overview of Czech declension and conjugation and mentions of other parts of speech. Provided by authors of WinCzEdu CD-ROM at <a href=\"http://mujweb.cz/www/winczeduc\">http://mujweb.cz/www/winczeduc</a>. Also contains Czech history at <a href=\"http://mujweb.cz/www/historycz\">http://mujweb.cz/www/historycz</a>.', 12),
(59, 'http://www.locallingo.com', 'http://www.locallingo.com', ' Contains some language exercises and a brief but useful grammar overview. ', 12),
(60, 'http://czech.ya.cz', 'http://czech.ya.cz', 'An interesting site for Russian speakers. Contains declension and conjugation tables as well as other aspects of Czech grammar explained in Russian. Excerpts from Czech poets are also placed on the site. ', 12),
(61, 'http://cnk.ff.cuni.cz', 'http://ucnk.ff.cuni.cz <img border=\"0\" src=\"images/excellent.gif\">', ' Czech National Corpus with a limited search tool available to the public. ', 12),
(62, 'http://www.allpraha.com', 'http://www.allpraha.com', 'A useful new portal for expats living in Prague listing all sorts of websites with Czech-relevant info.', 48),
(63, 'http://www.prague-hotel.cz', 'http://www.prague-hotel.cz', 'A travel agency which might make it easier to find accommodation in Prague or the Czech Republic.', 48),
(64, 'http://www.slovio.com', 'http://www.slovio.com', 'An interesting project to try and establish a pan-Slavic language which will be intelligible to all Slavs. Its chances of success are slim, but it can give a student a good idea of what is Slavonic in Czech. There is also a related site with a self-explanatory name at <a href=\"http://www.panslavia.com\">http://www.panslavia.com</a>.', 53),
(65, 'http://www.praha.tv', 'http://www.praha.tv', 'A site in English offering all sorts of useful information to Prague\'s English speaking community.', 48),
(66, 'http://www.expats.cz', 'http://www.expats.cz <img border=0 src=images/excellent.gif>', 'A great online community for English speaking expatriates living in Prague. Discussion boards include a lot of information relevant for the short term visitors, as well.', 48),
(67, 'http://www.quick.cz', 'http://www.quick.cz', 'Links to some important news resources. Also includes full text search going back several years. Invaluable to any researchers and all free. (This item supplements listing sites of all the newspapers it services.) ', 57),
(68, 'http://www.ceskenoviny.cz', 'http://www.ceskenoviny.cz', 'Daily online paper published by CTK (Czech Press Agency). ', 57),
(69, 'http://www.lidovky.cz', 'http://www.lidovky.cz', 'Online edition of one of the most respectable Czech dailies. ', 57),
(70, 'http://www.idnes.cz', 'http://www.idnes.cz', 'Online edition of the best selling Czech daily Mladá Fronta Dnes <a href=\"http://www.mfdnes.cz\">http://www.mfdnes.cz</a>, offering up-to-date news and many online only features such as Inet interviews with celebrities and politicians. (Second link goes directly to electronic version of the paper edition). ', 57),
(71, 'http://www.ihned.cz', 'http://www.ihned.cz', 'Leading Czech business daily (equivalent of Financial Times) services this web site which also provides other business services such as tax advice. ', 57),
(72, 'http://www.respekt.cz', 'http://www.respekt.cz', 'Political commentary weekly with an archive going back to 1993. It publishes a week in review on its last page. ', 57),
(73, 'http://www.ringier.cz', 'http://www.ringier.cz', 'Major publisher of magazines and tabloid newspapers such as Reflex and Blesk. This site contains links to full online editions of all of them including the cult youth technology monthly magazine ABC. ', 57),
(74, 'http://www.tyden.cz', 'http://www.tyden.cz', 'A popular weekly magazine. ', 57),
(75, 'http://pes.eunet.cz', 'http://pes.eunet.cz', 'Neviditelný Pes (Invisible Dog) is the first online paper edited by a sci-fi writer Ondřej Neff. Its commentary is often used by mainstream printed media, such as <a href=\"http://www.lidovky.cz\">Lidové Noviny. </a>', 57),
(76, 'http://www.blisty.cz', 'http://www.blisty.cz', 'News and commentary by a Czech journalist, Jan Čulík, living in Glasgow. Summarizes daily news and comments on Czech realities from the UK perspective. ', 57),
(77, 'http://www.zive.cz', 'http://www.zive.cz', 'Source for computer related news in Czech. ', 57),
(78, 'http://www.nova-pritomnost.cz', 'http://www.nova-pritomnost.cz', 'Also <a href=\"http://www.new-presence.cz\">http://www.new-presence.cz</a>. Monthly political review both in Czech and English. Its publication was discontinued in April of 1999 but the web site contains archives of all issues going back through 1997. Issues are also available to be downloaded in PDF (readable by <a href=\"http://www.adobe.com\">Adobe Acrobat</a>). ', 57),
(79, 'http://www.prague.tv', 'http://www.prague.tv', 'New expatriate Prague newspaper. Refers about Czech culture as well as expat happenings. ', 57),
(82, 'http://www.wordbook.cz', 'http://www.wordbook.cz', ' A decent English/Czech - Czech/English dictionary. Contains an ingenious system for typing in letters with accents for those without a Czech keyboard. ', 11),
(83, 'http://www.translator.cz', 'http://www.translator.cz', ' Multilingual Dictionary and Translator also available as a commercial application. It translates between Czech and six other languages: English, German, French, Spanish, Italian and Russian. <b>Note: </b>To reverse the direction of translation click on button <i>Otoč.</i> ', 11),
(84, 'http://www.mtranslations.cz', 'http://www.mtranslations.cz', ' Moravia Translations provide a decent dictionary. It tends to show less frequent equivalents first, however. Also contains a description of the Czech alphabet. The company specializes in software localization. ', 11),
(85, 'http://www.oplatek.cz/0deutsch.htm', 'http://www.oplatek.cz/0deutsch.htm', ' German-Czech Dictionary offered by an electronic dictionary maker. ', 11),
(86, 'http://www.czechprimer.org', 'http://www.czechprimer.org <img border=\"0\" src=\"images/excellent.gif\">', ' A cute picture dictionary offering the most basic vocabulary with hand-drawn illustrations. ', 11),
(87, 'http://www.microton.cz', 'http://www.microton.cz', ' Online automatic translator from English into Czech. Its output is of limited use. ', 11),
(88, 'http://www.travlang.com', 'http://www.travlang.com', ' Basic Czech phrases with sound plus an online dictionary using a peculiar transcription system. (Also available for many other languages.) ', 11),
(89, 'http://www.maxdorf.cz/psm/psm.html', 'http://www.maxdorf.cz/psm/psm.html', ' Czech to Czech dictionary of medicine. ', 11),
(90, 'http://www.notam.uio.no/~hcholm/altlang/ht/Czech.html', 'http://www.notam.uio.no/~hcholm/altlang/ht/Czech.html', ' Alternative Czech Dictionary of about 34 vulgarisms translated into English. Uses peculiar transliteration. Contains vulgarisms in a number of other languages. ', 11),
(91, 'http://www.vegateam.cz/slovnik', 'http://www.vegateam.cz/slovnik', '  A page (including a short dictionary) describing the differences between Prague Czech and various Moravian dialect. ', 11),
(92, 'http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/8085927489/qid=939590039/sr=1-3/026-1201242-6968426', 'Buy the best printed dictionary from Amazon in the UK', ' Release in 1999 written by Josef Fronek, this is the only dictionary worth anything for serious language learning. ', 11),
(93, 'http://www.leda.cz', 'http://www.leda.cz', ' Czech dictionary publisher Leda which offers dictionaries both in print and on CD-ROM. ', 11),
(94, 'http://www.onelist.com/messages/Czechlist', 'http://www.onelist.com/messages/Czechlist', ' A group of Czech/English translators discussing problems with translating from Czech into English. ', 11),
(95, 'http://goethe-verlag.com/tests/', 'http://goethe-verlag.com/tests', '  A number of tests and quizzes for vocabulary and phrase between many languages. Includes correct answers but is not interactive. ', 11),
(96, 'http://www.unforgettablelanguages.com/frames_a10.html', 'http://www.unforgettablelanguages.com/frames_a10.html', 'Although it brands itself a full language course, this is too ambitious. But it can be recommended as an interesting vocabulary building aid which may be very useful to some users. It introduces Czech words through associations with English words and phrases. No grammar is mentioned. Only a sample is free but a full course can be had for relatively little (under US$10). ', 11),
(97, 'http://www.slovnik.cz', 'http://www.slovnik.cz', 'A decent online dictionary which doesn\'t use diacritics, however (could be a plus if you\'re not sure about a particular Czech word). Also contains a German/Czech dictionary.', 11),
(98, 'http://users.ox.ac.uk/~tayl0010', 'http://users.ox.ac.uk/~tayl0010 <img border=0 src=images/excellent.gif>', 'James Naughton\'s page offers a learner\'s dictionary to download and use offline. Also many classical Czech texts with annotations and translations.', 11),
(99, 'http://www.bohemica.com/essays', 'http://www.bohemica.com/essays', 'A number of articles about Czech language and culture. ', 53),
(100, 'http://www.czech-language.cz', 'http://www.czech-language.cz <img border=0 src=images/excellent.gif>', ' Excellent site describing Czech from a linguistic perspective. Contains many useful links. ', 53),
(101, 'http://www.locallingo.com', 'http://www.locallingo.com', ' An impressive site with a lot of information and a few interesting exercises. There are greatly useful lists, for example a list of Czech name days and nicknames. ', 53),
(102, 'http://www.slavic.ohio-state.edu/people/holdeman/czech', 'http://www.slavic.ohio-state.edu/people/holdeman/czech', ' A list of resources for teachers and learners of Czech as a foreign language. Particularly useful to US residents. Also contains database of places where Czech can be learned around the world. Seems defunct now.', 53),
(103, 'http://www.language.brown.edu/CZH', 'http://www.language.brown.edu/CZH <img border=0 src=images/excellent.gif>', ' Excerpts from selected works of Czech literature with exercises for advanced students. ', 53),
(104, 'http://www.language.brown.edu/NAATC', 'http://www.language.brown.edu/NAATC', ' Official website of the North American Association of Teachers of Czech (NAATC) which includes PDF versions of past newsletters. ', 53),
(105, 'http://www.baylanguagebooks.co.uk', 'http://www.baylanguagebooks.co.uk <img border=0 src=images/excellent.gif>', ' Online shopfront of a major distributor of language textbooks with an extensive selection of Czech language materials hard to get elswhere. ', 53),
(106, 'http://www.bama.ua.edu/~adrozd/czech', 'http://www.bama.ua.edu/~adrozd/czech', '  Sundry exercises to practice Czech vocabulary organized by themes. ', 53),
(107, 'http://www.ujc.cas.cz', 'http://www.ujc.cas.cz', 'Ústav pro jazyk český Akademie věd (Czech Language Institute at the Academy of Sciences) is all in Czech but contains an online FAQ about the language from the point of view of native speakers. You can also ask your own questions in Czech. ', 53),
(108, 'http://www.geocities.com/Athens/Forum/7953/Intro.html', 'http://www.geocities.com/Athens/Forum/7953/Intro.html', ' A site dealing with Czech-English translation problems. ', 53),
(109, 'http://www.tsjechisch.nl', 'http://www.tsjechisch.nl', 'A Dutch site about Czech. ', 53),
(110, 'http://www.masteringczech.com', 'http://www.masteringczech.com', '  A small info site run by a Czech expat living in the US as a supplement for her lessons. Includes pronunciation tips, a list of textbooks and a list of Czech authors translated into English. ', 53),
(111, 'http://www.czechstepbystep.cz', 'http://www.czechstepbystep.cz', ' Site connected to a new textbook \'Czech Step by Step\' with a free sample. ', 53),
(112, 'http://www.radio.cz', 'http://www.radio.cz <img border=0 src=images/excellent.gif>', ' Even though these are the pages of a Czech radio. The <b>Living Czech </b>and <b>Czechs in History</b> sections are excellent resources for learners of Czech language and culture. Also see Czech Grammar ', 53),
(113, 'http://www.ceskaliteratura.cz', 'http://www.ceskaliteratura.cz <img border=0 src=images/excellent.gif>', ' Probably the most complete Czech-based resource for Czech literature. Contains many texts and excerpts and links to others. ', 59),
(114, 'http://www.cuni.cz/cte', 'http://www.cuni.cz/cte', ' Czech library of electronic texts. Contains texts and links to texts both Czech originals and Czech translations. ', 59),
(115, 'http://www.language.brown.edu/CZH/', 'http://www.language.brown.edu/CZH/', '\'Brown University Online Czech Anthology\' is an excellent starting place for anyone wanting to read Czech literature in the original. It contains excerpts from Čapek and Haek with voice recordings and vocabulary links.There are also several exercises. ', 59),
(116, 'http://users.ox.ac.uk/~tayl0010', 'http://users.ox.ac.uk/~tayl0010', ' James Naughton\'s page containing many resources for Czech literature hosted by Oxford University as well as links to other sites. Resources include full texts of some Czech classical texts with annotations and translations. A learner\'s dictionary is also available for download. ', 59),
(117, 'http://www.lf1.cuni.cz/~dcasl/litera3.html', 'http://www.lf1.cuni.cz/~dcasl/litera3.html', ' Czech literature page with many excerpts and further links (all in Czech). Mirrored on ', 59),
(118, 'http://www.mujweb.cz/www/literatura', 'http://www.mujweb.cz/www/literatura', '. ', 59),
(119, 'http://www.bohemistika.cz', 'http://www.bohemistika.cz', ' A site of announcements for literary critics interested in Czech studies. All in Czech. ', 59),
(120, 'http://www.twistedspoon.com', 'http://www.twistedspoon.com', ' Prague-based publisher of translated Czech literature in English (specializing in but not limited to books written by Prague Jews at the turn of the last century). Well worth having a look. ', 59),
(121, 'http://www.noveknihy.cz', 'http://www.noveknihy.cz', ' Online version of weekly New Books magazine which containing a searchable database of nearly all books published in Czech since roughly 1990. Over 30,000 titles (including translations from other languages) with brief bibliographical information and a synopsis are listed by the site. ', 59),
(122, 'http://www.lupomesky.cz/maj', 'http://www.lupomesky.cz/maj', ' Complete text and translation of a famous romantic poem by K. H. Mácha <i>Máj</i>. ', 59),
(123, 'http://www.labyrint.cz', 'http://www.labyrint.cz', 'Complete text and translation of <i>Labyrint světa a ráj due</i> by Commenius. Also contains a fascinating 3D presentation. <b>Note: </b><i>All other links to specific works and authors can be found in one of the link collections above.</i> <p>\r\nNow seems defunct but the text can still be found on <a href=http://users.ox.ac.uk/~tayl0010>James Naughton\'s page</a>.', 59),
(124, 'http://www.locallingo.com', 'http://www.locallingo.com <img border=0 src=images/excellent.gif>', ' Local Lingo provides much useful information about the Czech culture and habits. ', 60),
(125, 'http://www.czech-tradition.cz', 'http://www.czech-tradition.cz <img border=0 src=images/excellent.gif>', ' Site dealing with Czech traditions month by month, amply illustrated with texts both in English and Czech. ', 60),
(126, 'http://www.klic.cz/remesla', 'http://www.klic.cz/remesla <img border=0 src=images/excellent.gif>', ' An excellent site in Czech describing traditional Czech Arts and Crafts and folklore. Also contains a season by season description of Czech customs and superstitions. ', 60),
(127, 'http://www.cesky-svet.cz', 'http://www.cesky-svet.cz', '  Site for tourists with much useful information about Czech history, symbols and Culture. Both in English and Czech. (Some sections under construction). ', 60),
(128, 'http://www.fipro.cz/pranostiky', 'http://www.fipro.cz/pranostiky', ' List of Czech \'weather-lore\' proverbs (more complete than the one at ', 60),
(130, 'http://www.recepty.cz', 'http://www.recepty.cz', ' Traditional as well as international recipes in Czech. Great resource for language learning with much appeal to the fifth sense. ', 60),
(131, 'http://www.onelist.com/messages/Czechlist', 'http://www.onelist.com/messages/Czechlist', ' A group of Czech/English translators discussing problems with translating from Czech into English including many cultural issues. ', 60),
(132, 'http://www.divadlo.cz', 'http://www.divadlo.cz', ' All about Czech theatre including schedules. ', 60),
(133, 'http://www.cfn.cz', 'http://www.cfn.cz', ' České filmové nebe (Czech Film Heaven) contains a year-by-year listing of hundreds of Czech films since 1930 and dozens of short profiles of famous Czech actors. It is being constantly updated. ', 60),
(134, 'http://homepages.go.com/~phonik', 'http://homepages.go.com/~phonik', ' English/German site listing 255 Czech and Slovak TV serials broadcast since 1959. It contains short descriptions of some of them and profiles of several actors. ', 60),
(135, 'http://www.dokina.cz', 'http://www.dokina.cz', ' Current film listings including reviews and brief film descriptions. ', 60),
(136, 'http://www.jokes.cz', 'http://www.jokes.cz', ' Hundreds of jokes of variable taste, but all in Czech and useful for the learner. ', 60),
(137, 'http://pes.internet.cz/hudba/ukazky.htm', 'http://pes.internet.cz/hudba/ukazky.htm', ' Many samples of Czech classical and folklore music (as well as some other classical music) as part of Neviditelný pes. ', 60),
(138, 'http://www.crvp.org/book/Series04/IVA-04.htm', 'http://www.crvp.org/book/Series04/IVA-04.htm', ' Two texts dealing with issues of Czech culture and history stored at the <a href=http://www.crvp.org>Council for Research in Values and Philosophy website</a>. They are <i>Traditions and present problems of Czech political culture </i>and <i>Czech philosophy in the XXth century. </i>Other related texts are also available at the site. ', 60),
(139, 'http://www.geocities.com/goodolejoe/songs.html', 'http://www.geocities.com/goodolejoe/songs.html', 'Page with over 70 Czech Polka songs as sung in Texas. Unfortunately, it does not contain háčky and čárky (i.e. accents). ', 60),
(140, 'http://mujweb.cz/www/historycz', 'http://mujweb.cz/www/historycz <img border=0 src=images/excellent.gif>', ' A summary of Czech history in English. ', 58),
(141, 'http://www.libri.cz/capka', 'http://www.libri.cz/capka <img border=0 src=images/excellent.gif>', ' A complete Czech History in Dates in Czech. Provided by the publisher of many Czech encyclopedias. Also a comprehensive index of Czech historical personalities, their dates of birth and death and links to key events.  ', 58),
(142, 'http://www.cesky-svet.cz', 'http://www.cesky-svet.cz', '  Site for tourists with much useful information about Czech history, symbols and Culture. Both in English and Czech. (Some sections under construction). ', 58),
(143, 'http://www.czech.cz', 'http://www.czech.cz <img border=0 src=/images/excellent.gif>', ' Information resource about Czech history, culture and tourism in English, provided by the Czech Ministry of foreign Affairs. ', 52),
(144, 'http://www.radio.cz', 'http://www.radio.cz <img border=0 src=/images/excellent.gif>', ' Even though these are the pages of a Czech radio. The <b>Living Czech </b>and <b>Czechs in History</b> sections are excellent resources for learners of Czech language and culture. ', 52),
(145, 'http://www.prague-photos.com', 'http://www.prague-photos.com', ' Lots of photographs from Prague and other interesting Czech things. ', 52),
(146, 'http://www.arts.gla.ac.uk/Slavonic/MachaJedl.html', ' Karel Hynek Mácha: On patriotism and Turtle-Doves - on University of Glasgow web', 'Jan Čulík\'s translation of an essay by Josef Jedlička on the importance of the Czech poem <i>May</i> by Karel Hynek Mácha. The full text (including the translation can be found on James Naughton\'s site.', 28),
(147, 'http://www.arts.gla.ac.uk/Slavonic/NemcovaJedl.html', ' The Grandmother: A modest idyll - on University of Glasgow web', 'Jan Čulík\'s translation of an essay by Josef Jedlička on the importance of a famous book by Boena Němcová <i>Babička</i>.', 28),
(148, 'http://www.google.com/search?q=learning+styles&btnG=Google+Search', 'Výsledek hledání \'learning styles\' na Google', 'Podívejte se na některé odkazy z této stránky. Bohuel vechny jsou anglicky. Textů o učebních stylech v četině je bohuel velice málo.', 142),
(149, 'http://www.google.com/search?q=4mat+mccarthy&btnG=Google+Search', 'Stránky k systému 4MAT', 'Zde je několik uitečných stránek, které se hlouběji zabývají učebním stylem 4MAT.', 142),
(150, 'http://www.lfhk.cuni.cz/mares/doc/obsah_su.htm', '<i>Jiří Mare</i>: Styly učení u áků a studentů', 'Obsah a první kapitola jediné rozsáhlejí české publikace k učebním stylům. Vydané v roce 1998 nakladatelstvím Portál.', 142),
(151, 'http://www.resort.com/~prime8/Orwell/patee.html', 'Link to the full text of Orwell\'s essay', '', 144),
(152, 'http://www.ncsu.edu/effective_teaching/Papers/FLAnnals.pdf', 'Learning and Teaching Styles (PDF)', 'Hezký přehled různých stylů učení i výuky a toho, jaký mají vztah k výuce jazyků. (Ve formátu PDF, vyaduje Acrobat.)', 142),
(153, 'http://www.bohemica.com/czechkeyboard', 'Czech keyboard instructions', 'Everything about the layout of the Czech keyboard and installation instructions.', 89),
(154, 'http://prague.cybercityguides.com/', 'http://prague.cybercityguides.com/', 'Information about a range of hotels in Prague including basic overview of the city\'s attractions and night life.', 48),
(155, 'http://prague-hotel.wz.cz/', 'http://prague-hotel.wz.cz/', 'A hotel booking service covering the whole price range.', 48),
(156, 'http://www.caramba.cz/page.php?PgID=586', 'České webové stránky o zdravé výivě na serveru http://www.caramba.cz', 'Podívejte se na některé stránky o zdravé výivě a odpopovězte na otázku: Je zdravá výiva populární téma v České republice?', 155),
(157, 'http://www.ruslanghist.com', 'http://www.ruslanghist.com', 'An excellent site for the history of Russian.', 158),
(158, 'http://www.bohemica.com/slovak', 'http://www.bohemica.com/slovak', 'Slovak language learning materials available on this site.', 158),
(159, 'http://www.ssees.ac.uk', 'http://www.ssees.ac.uk', 'University of London\'s School of Slavonic and East European Studies. Contains a wide range of resources for \r\nmany languages of the region.', 158),
(160, 'http://www.slavonic.arts.gla.ac.uk', 'http://www.slavonic.arts.gla.ac.uk', 'In addition to Czech, Russian and Polish can also be studied at the University of Glasgow.', 158),
(161, 'http://mujweb.cz/www/mapy', 'http://mujweb.cz/www/mapy', 'Contains historical maps of the Czech lands.', 58),
(162, 'http://www.kdojekdo.cz', 'http://www.kdojekdo.cz', 'The Czech Who\'s Who web pages contain basic information about a number of living Czechs.', 52),
(163, 'http://www.bohemica.com/links', 'Linky uitečné pro studenty četiny', 'Podívejte se, co je na internetu k dispozici pro studenty četiny a srovnejte to s angličtinou (a například s jiným slovanským jazykem).', 156),
(164, 'http://www.atlas.cz', 'Český portál', 'Podívejte se na tento český portál, rozeberte podrobněji jednu kategorii a srovnejte ji s ekvivalentní kategorií na nějakém britském nebo světovém portálu.', 156),
(165, 'http://www.czechsite.com', 'http://www.czechsite.com', 'A great portal for tourists and expatriates alike. Contains much useful information, including a list of famous Czechs.', 48),
(166, 'http://www.bohemica.com/index.php?m=tuit&unit=3', 'Grammar Overview', 'Click here to read the details of how Czechs learn their grammar.', 97),
(167, 'http://www.gallery.cz', 'http://www.gallery.cz <img border=0 src=images/excellent.gif>', 'An excellent online exhibition of a number of Czech artists (photography, paintings, scupture, glass) with a short profile (in Czech only) of each artist. Includes some famous names.', 60),
(168, 'http://www.miami.com/mld/miamiherald/living/columnists/dave_barry/4213398.htm', 'Dave Barry: Art is in more than eye of the beholder', 'Dave Barry je jediný Američan z těchto tří. Píe v americkém Miami Herald, ale jeho sloupky jsou syndikované v mnoha dalích publikacích. Je velmi vtipný a také nejméně politicky angaovaný.', 169),
(169, 'http://argument.independent.co.uk/regular_columnists/mark_steel/story.jsp?story=313948', 'Mark Steel: Drug culture has invaded Middle England', 'Mark Steel je anglický komik, který kromě pořadu na BBC Radio 4 také pravidelně přispívá do The Independent. Tento text se týká současné debaty o legalizaci marihuany.', 169),
(170, 'http://argument.independent.co.uk/regular_columnists/simon_carr/story.jsp?story=338298', 'Simon Carr: The Sketch: The Chancellor revealed his indivisible core. It wasn\'t a pretty sight...', 'Simon Carr je politický komentátor pro The Independent. Píe tzv. Parliamentary Sketch, tj. Parlamentní diář, kde vtipně a nevybraně popisuje dění v parlamentu. Protoe představuje velice specifický ánr, je moná ze vech nejzajímavějí, ale asi také nejobtínějí.', 169),
(171, 'http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/tg/detail/-/0871131420/ref=lib_dp_TFCV/102-6108910-8994538?v=glance&vi=reader#reader-link', 'Tom Sharpe: Indecent Exposure', 'Velice vtipná kniha Toma Sharpe, který je u nás více méně neznámý, ale rozhodně stojí za to se na něj podívat. Myslím, e je poměrně populární v Německu. Tento úryvek se nachází na Amazonu a asi bych z něj vybral kusy z prvních dvou stran.', 169),
(172, 'http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/tg/detail/-/0879518014/ref=lib_dp_TFCV/102-6108910-8994538?v=glance&vi=reader#reader-link', 'Tom Sharpe: The Midden', 'Taky bychom se mohli podívat na úryvek z této novějí knihy (zatímco ta předchozí je jeho druhá), která sice není ani zdaleka tak dobrá jako celek, ale obsahuje velice zajímavou kritiku Thacherovského ekonomického liberalismu, která se nápadně podobá některým kritikám české deregulace 90. let.', 169),
(173, 'http://www2.h-net.msu.edu/~habsweb', 'http://www2.h-net.msu.edu/~habsweb', 'A site for discussing the Habsburg Monarchy and the successor states.', 58),
(174, 'http://www.geocities.com/ateliermp/thingsczech.html', 'http://www.geocities.com/ateliermp/thingsczech.html', 'A page about Czech architecture.', 52),
(175, 'http://www.psp.cz', 'Parlament České Republiky - http://www.psp.cz', 'Zde najdete informace o rozloení politických sil v českém parlamentu.', 178),
(176, 'http://www.hrad.cz', 'Kancelář prezidenta', 'Informace o úřadu prezidenta i předchozích prezidentech.', 178),
(177, 'http://www.ods.cz/', 'Stránky ODS', 'Prezentace druhé největí české parlamentní strany.', 178),
(178, 'http://www.cssd.cz', 'ČSSD', 'Stránky současné vládní strany, obsahující i odkazy na osobní stránky politiků.', 178),
(179, 'http://www.4koalice.cz', 'Koalice', 'Stránky spojení dvou parlamentních stran: KDU-ČSL a US-DEU.', 178),
(180, 'http://www.kscm.cz', 'Komunistická strana Čech a Moravy', 'Stránky nástupnické strany bývalé KSČ.', 178),
(181, 'http://www.volby.cz/', 'Volby', 'Stránky Českého statistického úřadu, popisující volební výsledky.', 178),
(182, 'http://www.svu2000.org', 'http://www.svu2000.org', '\"Czechs and Slovaks worldwide and their culture.\" The Official Site of the Czechoslovak Society of Arts and Sciences (SVU). Lots of interesting resources for information about Czech-Americans. Lots of history but also many currect issues of both the Czechs and Slovaks.', 47),
(183, 'http://www.bigissuetrip.org/poetry.html', 'Big Issue Poetry', 'Link k několika básním z Big Issue. Můete si vybrat jednu nebo několik.', 184),
(184, 'http://books.guardian.co.uk/departments/poetry/story/0,6000,650786,00.html', 'Andrew Motion: The Younger Sister', 'Báseň k příleitosti smrti princezny Margaret. Je to zajímavý příklad poezie na objednávku od oficiálního královského básníka (Poet Laureate). <a href=http://books.guardian.co.uk/specials/specials/0,5917,351492,00.html>Dalí básně k různým příleitostem jsou zde</a>.', 184),
(185, 'http://www.mattharvey.co.uk/pages/books.html', 'Matt Harvey: Free Verse', 'Několik básní od populárního básníka, který má spolu s Rory Motionem pořad v rozhlase.', 184),
(186, 'http://zena.centrum.cz/moda/index.phtml', 'Český server o módě', 'Přečtěte si, co zajímá moderní Čeky na módě.', 185),
(187, 'http://www.moda.cz', 'http://www.moda.cz', 'Dalí český server o módě.', 185),
(188, 'http://www.folklor.cz/foto', 'Fotogragie tradičních českých krojů', 'Podívejte se na tradiční kroje z Čech a Moravy. Jsou podobné jiným krojům, které znáte? Jakou měli funkci?', 185),
(189, 'http://www.folklor.cz', 'http://www.folklor.cz', 'Czech folklore server - contains much useful information about Czech traditions and upcoming events (such as folk festivals).', 60),
(190, 'http://www.vlada.cz', 'Česká vláda', 'Toto je oficiální server české vlády. Zjitěte, jaký mají vládní strany program.', 178),
(191, 'http://www.arts.gla.ac.uk/Slavonic/ss1A2002courseinfo.htm', 'Slavonic Studies Level 1 Module 1A', 'Description of the course on the departmental web. Includes information about the course including references and suggestions for further research.', 190),
(192, 'http://www.bohemica.com/?m=catalog&s=59', 'More links to sites dealing with Czech literature', 'Here you can find more links to all kinds of sites dealing with Czech literature.', 190),
(193, 'http://www.arts.gla.ac.uk/Slavonic/ss1Amaterial2002.htm', 'http://www.arts.gla.ac.uk/Slavonic/ss1Amaterial2002.htm', 'A valuable resource of information for 20th century literature (particularly Holub, Hrabal, kvorecký, Kundera). Includes excerpts.', 59),
(194, 'http://www.slavonic.arts.gla.ac.uk/czech/tuit/index.php?section=mb&mb_section=board&board=23', ' Czech Literature Forum', 'All students are encouraged to take part in discussions on the Literature Forum where everybody can discuss in more detail issues raised in class. Discussions of essay topics are also possible.', 190),
(195, 'http://www.bohemica.com/?m=tuit&unit=4', ' Introduction to Czech Pronunciation for Beginners', 'You can learn about Czech pronunciation and spelling here. Listen to all Czech sounds individually and in context. You can also complete two practice exercises and print them out for future reference.', 190),
(196, 'http://www.bohemica.com/?m=tuit&unit=4', 'Introduction to pronunciation for beginners', 'Includes audio examples and two practive exercises.', 76),
(197, 'http://www.bohemica.com/czechkeyboard', ' Using Czech on the computer', 'Instructions for using the Czech keyboard layout and installing it on a computer.', 190),
(198, 'http://www.wordbook.cz/slovnik.php?fjazyk=en', 'Czech dictionary online', 'Search for the meaning of Czech words and/or look up English words in Czech. This dictionary allows you to enter accented Czech characters on any computer. For serious dictionary work use a printed dictionary such as the award-winning Czech/English dictionary by Josef Fronek.', 190),
(199, 'http://www.guide-prague.cz', 'http://www.guide-prague.cz', 'If you\'re looking for a tour guide, this directory of licensed tourist guides guiding in various languages, might be useful.', 48),
(200, 'http://dir.seznam.cz/Umeni/Hudba/Folkova/Folkovi_zpevaci', 'Seznam webových stránek české folkové hudby', 'Zde najdete linky ke vem nejvýznamnějím českým folkovým zpěvákům a skupinám.', 196),
(201, 'http://www.nohavica.cz', 'Jaromír (Jarek) Nohavica', 'Stránky nejpopulárnějího a i nejvýznamnějího českého folkového zpěváka. Obsahují také texty jeho písní.', 196),
(202, 'http://dir.seznam.cz/Umeni/Hudba/Rockova/Rockove_skupiny', 'České rockové skupiny', 'Seznam webových stránek různých českých rockových skupin (ale také českých stránek o světovém rocku).', 196),
(203, 'http://www.vltava.cz', 'Vltava.cz - Český internotový obchod s hudbou (i knihami)', 'Na Vltavě.cz si můete nejen koupit desky, ale také poslouchat krátké úryvky z mnoha alb české hudby. Některé desky se dají koupit i ve formátu MP3. (V části Knihkupectví je také moné koupit e-knihy).', 196),
(204, 'http://mapy.atlas.cz', 'Online map of the Czech Republic', 'This should help you identify geographical references in the books you read. Click on the English flag to get to the English version of the site.', 190),
(205, 'http://www.pcv.cz/home/adamec/czech/balances.html', 'Benjamin Kuras: Czechs and Balances (Excerpts)', 'This site contains an extract from Benjamin Kuras\' book <i>Czechs and Balances: A Nation\'s Survival Guide</i>. An extremely enternaining and at times elucidating book by the author of <i>Life on Marx</i>.', 28),
(206, 'http://www.new-presence.cz/98/04/czech.htm', 'Czech students talk about \"being Czech\"', 'An article in  The New Presence journal with interviews with Czech students about what they feel being Czech is all about.', 28),
(207, 'http://www.ce-review.org/thematicarchives/czech/ta_czechsociety.html', 'The Central Europe Review: Czech Society section of the Thematic Archive', 'Articles on Czech society which have appeared in past issues of CER since 1998. An extremely interesting collection of analyses and social polemics by both Czech and international commentators. Most of them don\'t deal with the issues of \'culture\' as approached by this site, but they will provide useful insights to anyone wanting to learn about Czech values and believes.', 28),
(208, 'http://www.ce-review.org/thematicarchives/czech/ta_czechculture.html', 'http://www.ce-review.org/thematicarchives/czech/ta_czechculture.html', 'Czech Culture section of the Thematic Archive on The Central Europe Review. A lot of useful information can be found there.', 60),
(209, 'http://www.ce-review.org/thematicarchives/czech/ta_czechmain.html', 'http://www.ce-review.org/thematicarchives/czech/ta_czechmain.html', 'Archive of articles on a whole range of Czech issues (most connected to politics) on The Central Europe Review.', 61),
(210, 'http://www.charta77.org', 'http://www.charta77.org', 'A site devoted to Czech political dissent in the 1970s and 1980s. Most resources are in Italian only.', 61),
(211, 'http://www.nova.cz/tvarchiv', 'Archív pořadů televize NOVA', 'Najdete tu nejen Televizní noviny, ale také dalí zpravodajské a investigativní pořady.', 201),
(212, 'http://www.ct1.cz', 'Aktuální zprávy ČT1', 'Zde se můete podívat na poslední Události, ale najdete tu také archív starích zpravodajských pořadů.', 201),
(213, 'http://tv.idnes.cz/tv_zpravy.asp', 'TV iDnes', 'Různé zpravodajské videoklipy z mnoha zdrojů. Jsou uitečné předevím proto, e kadá zpráva tu má svou poloku.', 201),
(214, 'http://live.atlas.cz', 'LIVE Atlas', 'Tato stránka atlasu obsahuje celou kálu uitečných videoklipů (nejen zpravodajských) a linky na dalí zdroje informací.', 201),
(215, 'http://www.bbc.co.uk/news24', ' BBC News 24', 'Na této stránce se můete podívat na poslední zprávy jak z BBC24, tak z BBC 1. Na stránkách BBC také najdete jednotlivé zprávy jako klipy.', 201),
(216, 'http://www.itv.com/news', ' ITV News', 'Zde jsou komerční zprávy stanice ITV. Jen některé poloky jsou k dispozici jako video.', 201),
(217, 'http://www.sky.com/skynews/worldnews', ' Sky NEWS', 'Mezinárodní zprávy na komerční satelitní televizi. Opět jen některé zprávy jsou k dispozici jako video.', 201),
(218, 'http://www.fingertipsoft.com/cestart', 'http://www.fingertipsoft.com/cestart', 'Central European Starter Kit 2.0. This is a commercial software but it should solve your keyboard problems on older versions of Windows. Trial version is available. Probably not worth it on Windows 98 and higher.', 46),
(219, 'http://www.vilner.net/nikitiny/pesni.html', 'http://www.vilner.net/nikitiny/pesni.html', 'These poems are also songs. The sound-files can be found here.', 206),
(220, 'http://www.bohemica.com/czechgrammar', 'Czech Grammar Online', 'You can use this online reference on Bohemica.com as a further resource for your study.', 89),
(221, 'http://web.isp.cz/jcrane/Czech_hero.html', 'Gallery of Czech Heroes and Villains', 'An interesting website listing some 20 Czech historical figures with brief bios.', 32),
(222, 'http://web.isp.cz/jcrane/ceindex.html', 'http://web.isp.cz/jcrane/ceindex.html', 'A class page for Central European history which includes much useful information on Czech identity as well as Czech history including a gallery of Czech heroes and villains.', 52),
(223, 'http://www.bonusweb.cz/clanky/skodlivosther/nasilivehrach010130.html', 'Mají hry vliv na dětskou kriminalitu', 'Dalí zajímavý článek zabývající se vlivem televize a počítačů na děti.', 216),
(224, 'http://www.osu.cz', 'http://www.osu.cz', 'UNIVERSITY of OSTRAVA offers Summer Slavic Course\r\nWhen: August 24, 2003 - September 14, 2003\r\nWhat: PRACTICAL LANGUAGE CLASSES \r\nOPTIONAL SEMINARS \r\nSPECIALIZED LECTURES +complementary courses of Russian, Polish, Croatian and Bulgarian.', 54),
(225, 'http://www.feminismus.cz', 'http://www.feminismus.cz', 'Webové stránky, na kterých se diskutuje feminismus v Čechách. Vyberte si alespoň dva příspěvky a zamyslete se nad tím, jaký mají vztah k otázkám tohoto tématu.', 226),
(226, 'http://www.prague-hotel.co.uk/affiliate.asp?email=dlukes@bohemica.com', 'http://www.prague-hotel.co.uk', 'Another site listing accommodation and hotel information. This time with a European and UK bias and focus on apartments and hotel alternatives.', 48),
(228, 'http://www.cactuslanguage.com', 'http://www.cactuslanguage.com', 'Among some 40 languages, Czech courses are also offered.', 49),
(229, 'http://www.learnslovak.com', 'http://www.learnslovak.com', 'Learn Slovak - Online Slovak language lessons taught by a full time instructor.', 255),
(230, 'http://www.czechslovak.com', 'http://www.czechslovak.com', 'Czech Slovak - Online community with discussion forums, ecards, and much more! Contains links to other related sites.', 255),
(231, 'http://www.prague-tourist-information.com', 'http://www.prague-tourist-information.com', 'Covers lots of tips tips for tourists including: visa information, maps, events, a guide to restaurants and museums, and a children\'s section.', 48),
(232, 'http://www.hotels-of-prague.com', 'http://www.hotels-of-prague.com', 'Another hotel site with quite a few mid and up-market hotels. Offers direct reservations with a number of hotels in Prague, using local agents (CSA, AVE, CODAN).', 48),
(233, 'http://www.caledonianschool.com/intensive/intensive.en.html', 'http://www.caledonianschool.com/intensive/intensive.en.html', 'Caledonian School\'s intensive summer Czech course.', 55),
(234, 'http://www.aaaahotels.com', 'http://www.aaaahotels.com', 'One of an increasing number of sites specilizing in hotels in Prague.', 48),
(235, 'http://nupress.northwestern.edu/ue', 'http://nupress.northwestern.edu/ue', 'Writings from an Unbound Europe: Publisher\'s website including some books translated from Czech.', 59),
(236, 'http://www.czechmoviehouse.com', 'http://www.czechmoviehouse.com', 'A site where people in the US can buy Czech films on tape.', 47),
(237, 'http://www.stay-prague.com', 'http://www.stay-prague.com', 'A hotel site specializing in budget accommodation.', 48);
INSERT INTO `xc_linx` (`xcl_id`, `xcl_url`, `xcl_name`, `xcl_description`, `xcl_section`) VALUES
(238, 'http://czech.meetup.com', 'http://czech.meetup.com', 'A site to help people interested in the Czech Republic to arrange regional meetings. Could be quite useful if enough people signed up. Go there now!', 47),
(239, 'http://www.ectaco.com/online/diction.php3?lang=4', 'http://www.ectaco.com/online/diction.php3?lang=4', 'A site designed to sell more powerful dictionaries in software form. This free on-line version nonetheless gives access to a reasonable range of Czech-English-Czech equivalents. Plus it is the only online dictionary to distinguish between parts of speech.', 11),
(240, 'http://www.cznet.it', 'http://www.cznet.it', 'A site about things Czech for Italians in Italian.', 48),
(241, 'http://www.bcsa.co.uk', 'http://www.bcsa.co.uk', 'British Czech and Slovak Association: Aims to raise public awareness in Britain of Czech and Slovak life in all its aspects - history, arts and literature, economies, politics and science. Organizes an annual essay competition.', 47),
(242, 'http://www.centreurope.org', 'http://www.centreurope.org', 'Centreurope.org offers a selection of 300 websites, an academic directory, online courses and other services for business with Central and Eastern Europe.', 255),
(243, 'http://www.myczechrepublic.com', 'http://www.myczechrepublic.com  <img border=0 src=images/excellent.gif>', 'The ultimate guide for the first time visitor and/or newly arrived expat.', 48),
(244, 'http://slovnik.zcu.cz/online', 'http://slovnik.zcu.cz/online', 'Open project online dictionary which will translate entire pages as well as individual words.', 11),
(245, 'http://www.bohemica.com/slovak', 'http://www.bohemica.com/slovak', 'A collection of Slovak language materials from Peace Corps Slovakia hosted on Bohemica.com.', 255),
(246, 'http://peacecorpsalbania.blogspot.com', 'Peace Corps Albania on blogspot.com', 'A weblog maintained by Michael Scherger, the PC Albania Admin Officer. Many useful links to interesting articles about Albania can be found there.', 270),
(247, 'http://news.google.com/news?hl=en&edition=usa&q=albania', 'Google News for Albania', 'Recent news stories on Albania.', 270),
(248, 'http://www.albanian.com', 'Home of the Albanians Online', 'This page contains some useful information on Albania and Albanians such as general country information, major towns\' information, local media, and other information of interests to all people visiting or wanting to know something on the country. ', 270),
(249, 'http://www.albinfo.com', 'Albinfo.com', 'This site contains useful information on Albania such as travel info, money exchange info, business, internet, computers, and more. All the information is in English.', 270),
(250, 'http://www.shqiperia.com/fjalori.php', 'Albanian Online Dictionary', 'Here you will find an online dictionary both in English-Albanian and Albanian- English. All instructions for use are in English.', 270),
(251, 'http://www.balkanweb.com/', 'Balkan Web', 'This site contains up to date news from the region. There is a separate section for Albanian news both in English and Albanian.', 270),
(252, 'http://www.shqiperia.com/', 'Shqiperia.com (Shqiperia is Albania in Albanian)', 'Although all in Albanian, this site has extensive information on Albanian history, culture, art, events, etc. You will also find a photo album with pictures from all over Albania.', 270),
(253, 'http://www.shqiperia.com/foto/galeria/lezha', 'Lezha pictures', 'Pre-Service training site (Lezha) pictures.', 270),
(254, 'http://www.shqiperia.com/foto/shkodra-lezha.php', 'More Lezha pictures', 'A few more pictures of your PST site, Lezha, as well as a few pictures of Shkodra a town on hour north of Lezha. ', 270),
(255, 'http://www.geocities.com/albaweb4/personalities.htm', 'Albanian personalities from Durrës', 'An interesting page describing some important Albanians from the city of Durrës.', 270),
(256, 'http://www.rosettaproject.org/live/search/showpages?ethnocode=ALN&doctype=morsyn&scale=six&version=1&allpages=1', 'About Albanian Grammar', 'More detailed description for those interested in Grammar.', 270),
(257, 'http://www.discoverczech.com', 'http://www.discoverczech.com', 'An ingenious \"Trip Planner\" sets this tourist site apart from others.', 48),
(258, 'http://www.czechforum.net', 'http://www.czechforum.net', 'Not to be confused with Bohemica\'s forum, this site offers a chance to discuss many things related to visiting the Czech Republic.', 48),
(259, 'http://www.linglets.co.uk/czcases.htm', 'http://www.linglets.co.uk/czcases.htm', 'Home of a piece of software to help you practice Czech cases. Worth having a look.', 12),
(260, 'http://www.praguemonitor.com', 'http://www.praguemonitor.com', 'Great English-language overview of the Czech press and Czech events with a free subscription.', 51),
(261, 'http://www.saxongifts.com', 'http://www.Saxongifts.com', 'Buy <a href=http://www.saxongifts.com/index.asp?PageAction=VIEWCATS&Category=212>Czech dolls and ceramic toys</a> on this website specializing in Germanic trinkets.', 52),
(263, 'http://www.geocities.com/dablyler/page.html', 'http://www.geocities.com/dablyler/page.html', 'A home of an (reportedly very entertaining) expatriate novel set in Pilsen called \"Steffi\'s Club\".', 48),
(264, 'http://www.czechmarionettes.org', 'http://www.czechmarionettes.org', 'Buy marionettes or check out performance schedules at the Czechoslovak-American Marionette Theater web site.', 60),
(265, 'http://www.czechmarionettes.org', 'http://www.czechmarionettes.org', 'Czechoslovak-American Marionette Theater is a great oportunity to see Czech puppet theater in the USA.', 47),
(271, 'http://www.slawistyka.ath.bielsko.pl/czeski', 'http://www.slawistyka.ath.bielsko.pl/czeski', 'Czech for native speakers of Polish in Bielsko.', 49),
(272, 'http://www.worldwide-hotel-reservation.com/czech-republic', 'http://www.worldwide-hotel-reservation.com/czech-republic', 'International hotel reservation site that has links to decent hotels in regional capitals in the Czech Republic.', 48),
(273, 'http://www.ceemarket.com', 'http://www.ceemarket.com', 'Market portals for Poland, Czech Republic, Hungary, Russia and Slovakia. Some sister sites worth visiting are <a href=http://www.ceeretail.com>http://www.ceeretail.com</a> and <a href=www.ceeitandtelecom.com>www.ceeitandtelecom.com</a>.', 255),
(274, 'http://www.centomag.org', 'http://www.centomag.org', 'Online literary journal which publishes works of fiction and poetry, essays, artwork and other material.  Czech literature is one of several main areas of interest, and the site currently features a number of Czech authors, including Jiri Kratochvil, Jiri Weil, Jan Skacel, Petr Mikes, Milan Uhde, Martin Zet and Miroslav Huptych.', 59),
(275, 'http://www.akcent.cz/czech-foreigners.php', 'http://www.akcent.cz/czech-foreigners.php', 'A well-established Prague language school offering both summer and other language courses. ', 55),
(276, 'http://www.akcent.cz/czech-foreigners.php', 'http://www.akcent.cz/czech-foreigners.php', 'A well-established Prague language school offering both summer and other language courses. ', 55),
(278, 'http://www.slavica.com/teaching/Kresin.html', 'http://www.slavica.com/teaching/Kresin.html', 'An excellent article outlinging resources for learning Czech as a foreign language.', 53),
(279, 'http://www.prague.st', 'http://www.prague.st', 'Hotel site in English and German. Makes reservations and offers some accommodation outside Prague as well.', 48),
(280, 'http://euro.typo.cz', 'http://euro.typo.cz', 'A guide to Central European typography. Lots and lots of information about typography.', 46),
(281, 'http://www.czechworldnews.com', 'http://www.czechworldnews.com', 'Brief overview of world news related to interests of Czechs in the US. In Czech.', 47),
(282, 'http://www.users.bigpond.net.au/airx/default.htm', 'http://www.users.bigpond.net.au/airx/default.htm', 'Czech artist living in Australia.', 47),
(283, 'http://ceslit.org', 'http://ceslit.org', 'A place where you can find reviews and translated samples of Central and East European literature. As of fall 2004, most entries concerned Czech literature.', 59),
(284, 'http://www.pragueservices.com', 'http://www.pragueservices.com', 'Useful information for visitors to Prague (Culture, Tours, Transport, Eating out, Night life), including much more than just accommodation. Run by <a href=http://www.ctegroup.biz>http://www.ctegroup.biz</a>.', 48),
(285, 'http://www.allaboutprague.com', 'http://www.allaboutprague.com', 'Guide to Prague hotels of all categories including links to other useful information. Run by <a href=http://www.ctegroup.biz>http://www.ctegroup.biz</a>.', 48),
(286, 'http://dg.travelnow.com/index.jsp?action=viewLocation&locationId=34266&cid=101478', 'http://www.415travel.com', 'If you want a succinct and well-formulated reason for visiting Prague along with links to some beautifully positioned if upmarket hotels, this is your site (otherwise it is a general purpose travel agent).', 48),
(287, 'http://www.auccj.org', 'http://www.auccj.org', 'Association of Teachers of Czech as a Foreign Language. In Czech only.', 53),
(288, 'http://www.slovio.com', 'http://www.slovio.com', 'Site of the simplified international Slavic language.', 255),
(289, 'http://www.fdicts.com/czech/', 'http://www.fdicts.com/czech', 'An interesting free dictionary project which includes can help you translate between Czech and several other languages. Users can correct translations and add new entries.', 11),
(290, 'http://www.motylek.com', 'http://www.motylek.com', 'A hotel directory of Prague, with pictures, description and prices. Accommodation in all kind of facilities in Prague.', 48),
(291, 'http://www.prague-rooms.com', 'http://www.prague-rooms.com', 'Rooms in all types of hotels in Prague. Also a section with decent prices on transportation from airport and train stations.', 48),
(292, 'http://www.appliedlanguage.com/languages/czech_translation.shtml', 'http://www.appliedlanguage.com/languages/czech_translation.shtml', 'Czech translation services on the web.', 48),
(293, ' http://www.hotel.com.au/cities/Prague-Czech-Republic-hotels.asp', ' http://www.hotel.com.au/cities/Prague-Czech-Republic-hotels.asp', 'A hotel site for travellers coming to Prague from Australia.', 48),
(294, 'http://www.czechbook.co.uk', 'http://www.czechbook.co.uk', 'A great site for anybody wishing to visit the Czech Republic. Run by an expat Czech afficionado with a unique perspective on much more than just Prague.', 48),
(295, 'http://www.expatscafe.com/prague', 'http://www.expatscafe.com', 'A lively forum, chatroom and general info for English-speaking expats in Prague.', 48),
(296, 'http://www.topbicycle.com', 'http://www.topbicycle.com', 'Bicycle tours of the Czech Republic. Very interesting and a wide range of options.', 48),
(297, 'http://www.hotel-prague-tobook.com', 'http://www.hotel-prague-tobook.com', 'Hotel booking service specializing in mid-to-upper range hotels.', 48),
(298, 'http://www.worldwidelearn.com/language-courses', 'http://www.worldwidelearn.com/language-courses', 'Links to other online language courses including Bohemica.', 6),
(299, 'http://www.lingo24.com', 'http://www.lingo24.com', 'Translation service for many Central and Eastern European languages including Czech.', 48),
(300, 'http://www.pravidla.cz', 'http://www.pravidla.cz <img border=0 src=/images/excellent.gif>', 'A complete online version of the Czech spelling rules including a searchable database. An essential site for anybody who writes in Czech but could also be of use to beginner and intermediate students who want to check their spelling.', 11),
(301, 'http://lidovky.centrum.cz/cesky_sok', 'http://lidovky.centrum.cz/cesky_sok <img border=0 src=/images/excellent.gif>', 'Brief statements from over 50 foreigners living in the Czech Republic about how they view the Czechs and their culture. All in Czech.', 52),
(302, 'http://www.czechforum.net', 'http://www.czechforum.net', 'A general purpose discussion forum about all things Czech.', 6),
(303, 'http://www.memoria.cz', 'http://www.memoria.cz', 'Online collection of Czech historical documents (combined free and subscription-based) including the essential Dalimil\'s Chronicle. (Navigation in Czech and English. Documents in original languages and translation.)', 58),
(304, 'http://hotelplan.cz/', 'http://hotelplan.cz/', 'Last minute deals on apartments and hotels in Prague and the rest of the Czech Republic.', 48),
(305, 'http://www.speedhotels.com/eu_cz.html', 'http://www.speedhotels.com/eu_cz.html', 'Hotels in the Czech Republic and other European countries.', 48),
(306, 'http://hotels.iloveprague.com/', 'http://hotels.iloveprague.com/', 'Prague accommodation agency. No online database - just personalized service.', 48),
(307, 'http://nlp.fi.muni.cz/nlp/aisa/NlpCz/Frekvence_slov_lemmat.html', 'http://nlp.fi.muni.cz/nlp/aisa/NlpCz/Frekvence_slov_lemmat.html', 'A list of most common words in Czech (sorted by nouns, adjectives, verbs and pairs of words).', 11),
(308, 'http://www.abaka.com/Czech', 'http://www.abaka.com/Czech', 'Hotels and apartments in Prague and even some smaller regional towns.', 48),
(309, 'http://www.all-prague.com', 'http://www.all-prague.com', 'Prague hotels, tours and car rentals. Including information about the city.', 48),
(310, 'http://www.czech4you.com', 'http://www.czech4you.com', 'A wonderful website devoted to Brno, the beautiful Czech city, second largest in the country and unofficial capital of Moravia.', 48),
(311, 'http://www.czlit.cz', 'http://www.czlit.cz', 'A Czech Literature portal with links, excerpts and news. (in Czech)', 59),
(312, 'http://www.ceska-poezie.cz', 'http://www.ceska-poezie.cz', 'A wonderful website containing the entire (seachable) corpus of 19th century Czech poetry. It is also free to use upon registration.', 59),
(313, 'http://www.ohp.cz', 'http://www.ohp.cz', 'Online Hotel Booking in Prague. Includes very useful survival information about the country. All content in English, German and Hungarian.', 48),
(314, 'http://www.prague-vacation.com', 'http://www.prague-vacation.com', 'Comprehensive hotel site with info and links to other tourist services. Links to hotels, apartments and pensions from 10 Euro to 5-star hotel. Interface in English, German, Hungarian, Spanish and Dutch.', 48),
(315, 'http://www.travelprague.net', 'http://www.travelprague.net', 'Mediates hotels and other accommodation in Prague. Includes guided tours and other useful info such as interesting restaurants, museums and other points of interest.', 48),
(316, 'http://www.pragueconnect.com', 'http://www.pragueconnect.com', 'Much of interest to anybody visiting Prague. Apart from the usual accommodation and hotel links, it has info in the form of articles on a variety of subjects including cycling. Also contains classified ads.', 48),
(317, 'http://www.accomm-prague.cz', 'http://www.accomm-prague.cz', 'Reasonably-priced accommodation in Prague.', 48),
(318, 'http://www.prague-hotel.co.uk', 'http://www.prague-hotel.co.uk', 'Accommodation in Prague for the British with special attention to travellers from Britain.', 48),
(319, 'http://www.myteacher.cz/english', 'http://www.myteacher.cz', 'Find a teacher in the Czech Republic or advertise your services as a teacher on this new site.', 49),
(320, 'http://www.czecheverything.co.uk', 'http://www.czecheverything.co.uk', 'A slightly clunky UK site where different Czech products (gifts, CDs, DVDs, VHS) can be bought.', 52),
(321, 'http://www.csplanet.com', 'http://www.csplanet.com', 'Also known as cscommunitynews.com, the \"Self helping CS Network NewsLetter in USA,Canada\", this site provides useful information about and for the Czech and Slovak community in the USA.', 47),
(322, 'http://www.aaaahotels.com', 'http://www.aaaahotels.com', 'All sorts of hotels in Prague (from 5 stars to hostels) with the possibility of online booking.', 48),
(323, 'http://www.slovodne.cz', 'http://www.slovodne.cz', 'Slovo dne (or Word of the Day) is a blog with lighthearted comments on the Czech language in both English and Czech.', 53),
(324, 'http://www.hotelprague.org.uk', 'http://www.hotelprague.org.uk', 'Name-your price style hotel website for Prague. ', 48),
(325, 'http://www.prague-wedding.com', 'http://www.prague-wedding.com', 'An agency specializing in organizing weddings in Prague. Contains an interesting section on Czech wedding traditions. Also <a href=http://www.destination-wedding.cz>http://www.destination-wedding.cz</a>.', 48),
(326, 'http://www.hotels-prague.org', 'http://www.hotels-prague.org', 'Site specializing in Prague hotel reservations.', 48),
(327, 'http://hurontaria.baf.cz/KNIHY', 'http://hurontaria.baf.cz/KNIHY', 'A collection of Czech texts.', 59),
(328, 'http://www.guidingprague.com', 'http://www.guidingprague.com', 'A site of guided tours in Prague.', 48),
(329, 'http://humoresky.blogspot.com', 'http://humoresky.blogspot.com', 'Goulash People: A blog of expats in the Czech Republic.', 48),
(330, 'http://pragueweddings.co.uk', 'http://pragueweddings.co.uk', 'Weddings in Prague for Brits.', 48),
(331, 'http://www.livingprague.com', 'http://www.livingprague.com', 'Great independent website with information for visitors and residents alike. Its personal touch makes it all the more valuable.', 48),
(332, 'http://www.kosherprague.com', 'http://www.kosherprague.com', 'The title says it all. An ideal website for Jewish visitors of Prague or those interested in the rich (if sporadically tragic) history of the Jewish community of Prague which has contributed much to the city\'s appeal.', 48),
(333, 'http://www.prague-apartment-rentals.com/', 'http://www.prague-apartment-rentals.com/', 'Alternatives to hotel accommodation in Prague.', 48),
(334, 'http://www.ohp.cz', 'http://www.ohp.cz', 'Hotels not just in Prague but other major Czech cities.', 48),
(335, 'http://www.pragueexperience.com', 'http://www.pragueexperience.com', 'A complete guide to Prague. From hotels to dinners to culture and fun. Also has specific information about events such as Prague\'s New Year\'s celebrations.', 48),
(336, 'http://www.cedok.com', 'http://www.cedok.com', 'For tourists who want to explore all of Czech Republic. This is the English version of the oldest Czech Travel Agent <i>Čedok</i> offering travel to both the usual and out of the way spots.', 48),
(337, 'http://studyczech.blogspot.com', 'http://studyczech.blogspot.com', 'An excellent blog by a teacher of Czech containing culture notes, language notes and audio samples.', 53);
INSERT INTO `xc_sections` (`xcs_id`, `xcs_name`, `xcs_title`, `xcs_short_description`, `xcs_description`, `xcs_previous`, `xcs_time`, `xcs_priority`, `xcs_subpriority`, `xcs_logo`, `xcs_url`, `xcs_options`) VALUES
(1, 'Bohemica', 'All About Czech Language and Culture', '', '', 0, '2007-08-01 05:35:23', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(3, 'Czech Language', 'Czech Online', 'Czech Grammar, Conversation, Exercises, Games and Dictionary', '<center>\r\nThese pages are sponsored by <a href=\"http://www.stranslation.com\">Advanced International Translations</a>\r\n <br />\r\n<a href=\"http://www.translation3000.com/redir.html?bohemica\"><img height=\"120\" src=\"http://www.translation3000.com/affiliate_images/banner3.gif\" width=\"160\" border=\"0\" />\r\n </a>\r\n<br />\r\n<a href=\"http://www.anycount.com/redir.html?bohemica\"><img height=\"120\" src=\"http://www.anycount.com/img/banner7.gif\" width=\"120\" border=\"0\" />\r\n </a>\r\n<br />\r\n<a href=\"http://www.projetex.com/redir.html?bohemica\"><img height=\"120\" src=\"http://www.projetex.com/Banners/banner_projetex_120x120.gif\" width=\"120\" border=\"0\" />\r\n </a>\r\n</center>', 1, '2005-07-16 07:19:54', 10, 1, '/images/logos/czechonline_top.jpg', '', 0),
(4, 'Czech Linguistics', 'Czech Linguistics', 'Pages of the Prague Linguistic Circle. Links to other sites of linguistic interest.', 'Pages of the Prague Linguistic Circle. Links to other sites of linguistic interest. \r\n', 1, '2007-03-06 06:50:44', 10, 4, '', '', 0),
(5, 'Czech Culture', 'Czech Culture', 'Guide to Czech people, their likes and dislikes. Tips for foreign visitors, both short and long-term.', '', 1, '2004-02-06 00:40:35', 10, 2, '/images/logos/czechculture_top.jpg', '', 0),
(6, 'Czech Links', 'Czech Links', 'Links for the language learner. Authentic texts, newspapers, and television and radio webcasts.', 'The purpose of this collection of links is very specific. They have the language learner and student of Czech culture in mind. Some of them require a certain level of Czech from beginner to advanced, although many contain information in English. The sites listed are from all around the world but most of them come from the Czech Republic, USA, and the UK. Because of the interest a section of links relevant for tourists and expatriates living in Prague has also been added. The links are sorted in alphabetical order.<p>Czech Internet under the domain .cz contains many extremely useful resources and is growing at a rapid pace. The links listed here are thought to be of direct interest to learners. Thousands of other resources can be found through <a href=\"index.php?m=catalog&s=50\">portals and search engines</a>\r\n.&nbsp;</p>\r\n', 1, '2005-11-10 18:17:11', 10, 7, '', '', 0),
(7, 'Czech Bookstore', 'Czech Bookstore', 'Help keep this site running: Buy Czech books from selected online bookstores.', 'This site offers you a chance to buy books on-line in cooperation with major on-line book sellers. Books were sorted into categories and annotated by bohemica.com  but the responsibility for delivery and payment processing remains with the individual booksellers. If you want to buy other books go to the <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/redirect?tag=bohemicacom&path=ts/browse-books/21\">Reference</a> section on <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/redirect-home/bohemicacom\">Amazon.com</a> or <a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/redirect-home?tag=bohemicacom0d&site=amazon\">Amazon.co.uk</a>.', 1, '2006-09-29 23:20:33', 15, 2, '', '', 0),
(8, 'Czech Teachers', 'Czech Teachers', 'Students find a teacher - teachers find students!', 'This is a free new service for teachers and students of Czech. Teachers who offer private lessons or teach as part of an institution may advertise on this page. For the time being, this page is free for institutions offering Czech classes as well. <p>Teachers are listed according to the country where they teach. Countries are categorized by continent with a special category for teachers in the Czech Republic. </p>\r\n<p><a href=\"\\&quot;contact/newteacher.htm\\&quot;\">Teachers/Institutions <br />\r\nSign up here! </a>\r\n</p>\r\n', 1, '2006-10-30 01:46:14', 10, 3, '', '', 0),
(9, 'Czech Forum', 'Czech Forum', 'Ask and answer questions about the Czech language and culture', 'The Czech Forum is here for everybody to share questions about all things Czech. Students, teachers, tourists or academics may find it interesting to discuss issues of Czech language and culture. There are four discussion groups to make it easier to keep on a certain topic. <p>\r\n \r\nAnybody can contribute but contributions deemed irrelevant or inappropriate may be removed. \r\n \r\n', 1, '2003-02-20 14:20:53', 15, 3, '', '', 0),
(10, 'Czech Course', 'Czech Course', 'An online interactive course in Czech with a Czech teacher.', '<br />\r\n', 1, '2006-10-30 01:49:25', 17, 1, '', '', 0),
(11, 'Online Dictionaries', 'Online Dictionaries', 'Sites where you can look up Czech words and expand your vocabulary.', '', 6, '2002-10-13 19:35:56', 10, 30, '', '', 0),
(12, 'Online Grammars', 'Online Grammars', 'Sites with different levels of information about the structure of Czech.', '', 6, '2006-05-09 11:13:12', 10, 20, '', '', 0),
(13, 'Prague Circle of Linguistics', 'Prague Circle of Linguistics', 'A recently updated site on the Prague School of linguistics its history and recent activities has moved to its own domain <a href=\"http://www.praguelinguistics.org\">http://www.praguelinguistics.org</a>  after five years of being hosted on Bohemica.com.\r\n', '&nbsp;', 4, '2006-12-10 19:30:13', 1, 100, '', 'http://www.praguelinguistics.org', 0),
(14, 'Linguistic Essays', 'Linguistic Essays - Travaux Linguistiques Electroniques', 'Right now only a few are available. Hopefully this section will grow further. Feel free to submit more of your work (in Czech or English).', '', 4, '2005-11-10 18:06:49', 20, 100, '', '', 0),
(16, 'Essays', 'Writing  by Dominik Luke', 'Essays, newspaper articles and other writing by Dominik Luke.', 'These essays were written by <a href=\"contact/contactessays.htm\">Dominik Luke</a> as part of various projects. Some of them have been published or submitted for publication. \r\n\r\nThe subjects covered are linguistics, education and culture.  \r\n\r\nThere are also a few translations. \r\n\r\nMost of the work was written in English but there is a fair share of stuff written in my native Czech (particularly the journalism). \r\n', 1, '2005-08-31 03:16:19', 100, 100, '/images/logos/articles_top.jpg', '', 1),
(17, 'Czech Language', 'Essays on Czech Language', 'Essays written about Czech language for learners. Many more short essays are included in the trivia section of Czech Online.', '\r\nThese essays were written by Dominik Luke as part of various projects. Some of them have been published or submitted for publication. \r\n\r\nThe subjects covered are linguistics, education and culture.  \r\n\r\nThere are also a few translations. \r\n\r\nMost of the work was written in English but there is a fair share of stuff written in my native Czech (particularly the journalism). \r\n', 16, '2005-08-31 03:14:31', 10, 1, '/images/logos/articles_top.jpg', '', 0),
(18, 'Czech Culture', 'Essays on Czech Culture', 'A few essays and translations trying to explain  the Czechs and their culture. Much more on this can  be found in Czech Culture Guide.', '\r\nThese essays were written by Dominik Luke as part of various projects. Some of them have been published or submitted for publication.\r\n\r\nThe subjects covered are linguistics, education and culture. \r\n\r\nThere are also a few translations.\r\n\r\nMost of the work was written in English but there is a fair share of stuff written in my native Czech (particularly the journalism).', 16, '2005-08-31 03:15:50', 10, 2, '/images/logos/articles_top.jpg', '', 0),
(19, 'Linguistic Essays', 'Linguistic Essays', 'Several papers of general linguistic interest.', '\r\nThese essays were written by Dominik Luke as part of various projects. Some of them have been published or submitted for publication. \r\n\r\nThe subjects covered are linguistics, education and culture.  \r\n\r\nThere are also a few translations. \r\n\r\nMost of the work was written in English but there is a fair share of stuff written in my native Czech (particularly the journalism). ', 16, '2005-08-31 03:14:46', 10, 4, '/images/logos/articles_top.jpg', '', 0),
(25, ' Czech Republic', ' Czech Republic', 'Teachers and institution with residence in the Czech Republic.', 'This is a free new service for teachers and students of Czech. Teachers who offer private lessons or teach as part of an institution may advertise on this page. For the time being, this page is free for institutions offering Czech classes as well. <p>\r\n\r\nTeachers are listed according to the country where they teach. Countries are categorized by continent with a special category for teachers in the Czech Republic. <p>\r\n\r\n<a href=\"contact/newteacher.htm\">Teachers/Institutions <br>\r\nSign up here! </a>\r\n  \r\n', 8, '2003-01-05 20:41:55', 100, 1, '', '', 0),
(26, 'Europe', 'Europe', 'Teachers residing in Europe including Russia and the UK.', 'This is a free new service for teachers and students of Czech. Teachers who offer private lessons or teach as part of an institution may advertise on this page. For the time being, this page is free for institutions offering Czech classes as well. <p>\r\n\r\nTeachers are listed according to the country where they teach. Countries are categorized by continent with a special category for teachers in the Czech Republic. <p>\r\n\r\n<a href=\"contact/newteacher.htm\">Teachers/Institutions <br>\r\nSign up here! </a>\r\n  \r\n', 8, '2002-10-12 22:19:06', 100, 2, '', '', 0),
(27, 'North America', 'North America', 'Teachers residing in the US or Canada.', 'This is a free new service for teachers and students of Czech. Teachers who offer private lessons or teach as part of an institution may advertise on this page. For the time being, this page is free for institutions offering Czech classes as well. <p>\r\n\r\nTeachers are listed according to the country where they teach. Countries are categorized by continent with a special category for teachers in the Czech Republic. <p>\r\n\r\n<a href=\"contact/newteacher.htm\">Teachers/Institutions <br>\r\nSign up here! </a>\r\n  \r\n', 8, '2003-11-17 00:21:39', 100, 3, '', '', 0),
(28, 'Essays and Translations', 'Essays and Translations', 'Several essays and translations about the Czech culture.', 'These essays hope to help you approach the study of Czech culture from different perspectives and offer more than just a list of Dos and Don\'ts. There are two translations one from Russian into English and Czech and and one from Czech into English and several original essays dealing with the intersection of language and culture.<p>\r\n\r\nThis section also contains links to essays on other sites.', 5, '2002-11-16 15:09:03', 110, 100, '', '', 0),
(29, 'Worksheets', 'Czech Culture Guide: Worksheets', 'These worksheets allow you to see how much you\'ve learned in the other texts.', '', 5, '2004-08-29 17:40:21', 101, 100, '', '', 0),
(30, 'Living in CR', 'Czech Culture Guide: Official Requirements on Staying in the Czech Republic', 'Here you can find some information relevant for those who wish to live in the Czech Republic long-term. It is accurate as of 1999.', 'All knowledge of the new culture is useless if you cannot cut through all the red tape and stay there. Every country has a complicated set of rules which apply to foreigners, here you will find basic information applicable to most people.\r\n\r\n<UL>\r\n<li>Visa and conditions of stay.</li>\r\n<li>Getting a job. </li>\r\n<li>Finding and leasing an apartment. </li>\r\n<li>Starting a business. </li>\r\n<li>Buying and owning property. Investing. </li>\r\n</UL>\r\n\r\nA lot of this information is limited to basic pointers and you will need outside help to complete some of the more complicated tasks. It is accurate as of 1999. Any comments and corrections are welcome.\r\n', 5, '2002-09-23 00:48:11', 100, 4, '', '', 0),
(31, 'History, Art and Geography', 'Czech Culture Guide: History, Art and Geography', 'Learn here about facts and figures from Czech history, art and geography. If nothing else, these will provide a great topic for conversation with a Czech.', 'Learn here about facts and figures from Czech history, art and geography. If nothing else, these will provide a great topic for conversation with a Czech.\r\n\r\nHistory is an important aspect of any nations life and self-awareness. It is doubly important for Czechs with their proud history. Here you will find information on:\r\n\r\n<UL>\r\n  <LI>Top ten figures of Czech history and culture. </LI>\r\n  <LI>Most important events in Czech history.</LI>\r\n  <LI>National prides: literature, music, painting, architecture.</LI>\r\n  <LI>Basic Czech geography.</LI>\r\n  <LI>What to see, hear or read.</LI>\r\n</UL>\r\n\r\n\r\n', 5, '2002-10-12 19:33:13', 100, 3, '', '', 0),
(32, 'Czech Cultural Values', 'Czech Culture Guide: Cultural Values', 'Find here some information about what constitutes Czech culture, the values that Czechs hold and how they influence their behavior.', 'These materials contain information on several aspects of Czech culture often compared with other cultures, especially those of the English speaking world. The following issues are dealt with:\r\n\r\n<UL>\r\n  <LI>Czech values and attitudes.</LI>\r\n  <LI>Private and public space.</LI>\r\n  <LI>Meeting people and making friends.</LI>\r\n  <LI>Czechs and foreigners.</LI>\r\n  <LI>Gestures, postures and taboos.</LI>\r\n  <LI>Daily dos and donts.</LI>\r\n  <LI>Basic survival Czech and where to learn more.</LI>\r\n</UL>', 5, '2007-08-01 05:44:45', 100, 2, '', '', 0),
(33, 'About Culture', 'Czech Culture Guide: Theory of Culture', 'This section offers a bit about what culture is, where to find it and how to deal with the shocks of entering a new culture. Some of the materials were adopted from elsewhere.', 'Culture is what guides people in their lives, shapes their behavior and determines their attitude. To live and successfully adjust in a foreign culture requires a lot of information about what to do and what to avoid, what to talk about and how, and above all how to handle culture shock which will arrive.  \r\n\r\nThis section mainly focuses on two questions: 1) What is culture? and 2) What is culture shock and how to deal with it? It is useful for anybody wishing to know more about cultural adjustment in general.', 5, '2007-08-01 05:56:30', 100, 1, '', '', 0),
(35, 'Czech Linguistics', 'Bookstore: Czech Linguistics', 'Monographs by and about Czech linguists.', '', 7, '2007-08-01 05:42:51', 100, 5, '', '', 0),
(36, 'Czech Travel Guides', 'Bookstore: Czech Travel Guides', 'All sorts of guides to take with you when traveling to the Czech Republic. ', '', 7, '2007-08-01 05:43:39', 100, 6, '', '', 0),
(37, 'Czech Literature', 'Bookstore: Czech Literature', 'Works of fiction and poetry by Czech authors translated into English.', '', 7, '2007-08-01 05:57:41', 100, 4, '', '', 0),
(38, 'Czech Culture', 'Bookstore: Czech Culture', 'Books about Czech culture, history, film, theater.', '', 7, '2007-08-01 05:58:08', 100, 3, '', '', 0),
(39, 'Reference', 'Bookstore: Reference (Dictionaries and Grammars)', 'Grammars, dictionaries, encyclopedias and other general books about the language.', '', 7, '2005-05-29 23:36:37', 100, 2, '', '', 0),
(40, 'Language Textbooks', 'Bookstore: Czech Language Textbooks', 'Annotated textbooks of Czech for foreign language learners.', '', 7, '2002-10-12 18:51:27', 100, 1, '', '', 0),
(41, 'Czech Multimedia', 'Bookstore: Czech Multimedia', 'CD-ROMs for learning Czech or helpful for students of Czech language and culture.', '', 7, '2002-10-12 18:59:25', 110, 100, '', '', 0),
(42, 'South America', 'South America', 'Teachers from countries south of the US. From Mexico to Argentina. First two teachers since 2004.', 'This is a free new service for teachers and students of Czech. Teachers who offer private lessons or teach as part of an institution may advertise on this page. For the time being, this page is free for institutions offering Czech classes as well. <p>Teachers are listed according to the country where they teach. Countries are categorized by continent with a special category for teachers in the Czech Republic. </p>\r\n<p><a href=\"contact/newteacher.htm\">Teachers/Institutions <br />\r\nSign up here! </a>\r\n</p>\r\n', 8, '2006-12-09 21:23:26', 100, 6, '', '', 0),
(43, 'Africa', 'Africa', 'Teachers from any African country. So far no teachers in this section.', '\r\nThis is a free new service for teachers and students of Czech. Teachers who offer private lessons or teach as part of an institution may advertise on this page. For the time being, this page is free for institutions offering Czech classes as well. <p>\r\n\r\nTeachers are listed according to the country where they teach. Countries are categorized by continent with a special category for teachers in the Czech Republic. </p><p>\r\n\r\n<a href=\"contact/newteacher.htm\">Teachers/Institutions <br />\r\nSign up here! </a></p>', 8, '2006-10-30 01:46:14', 195, 100, '', '', 0),
(44, 'Asia', 'Asia', 'Teachers from any part of Asia. (Now teachers in Japan, Korea, Taiwan, and Kazakhstan).', '\r\nThis is a free new service for teachers and students of Czech. Teachers who offer private lessons or teach as part of an institution may advertise on this page. For the time being, this page is free for institutions offering Czech classes as well. <p>\r\n\r\nTeachers are listed according to the country where they teach. Countries are categorized by continent with a special category for teachers in the Czech Republic. </p><p>\r\n\r\n<a href=\"contact/newteacher.htm\">Teachers/Institutions <br />\r\nSign up here! </a></p>', 8, '2005-09-22 15:41:46', 100, 4, '', '', 0),
(45, 'Australia', 'Australia', 'Teachers offering services in Australia and New Zealand. Now two teachers!', 'This is a free new service for teachers and students of Czech. Teachers who offer private lessons or teach as part of an institution may advertise on this page. For the time being, this page is free for institutions offering Czech classes as well. <p>\r\n\r\nTeachers are listed according to the country where they teach. Countries are categorized by continent with a special category for teachers in the Czech Republic. <p>\r\n\r\n<a href=\"contact/newteacher.htm\">Teachers/Institutions <br>\r\nSign up here! </a>', 8, '2003-11-17 00:21:08', 100, 5, '', '', 0),
(46, 'Fonts and Keyboards', 'Fonts and Keyboards', 'Sites where fonts for Czech (and other languages) can be obtained.', '', 6, '2005-02-17 23:24:45', 90, 10, '', '', 0),
(47, 'Czechs Abroad', 'Czechs Abroad', 'Resources about, for, and by Czech expatriates around the world.', '', 6, '2002-10-13 20:37:14', 30, 20, '', '', 0),
(48, 'Expats and Tourists', 'Expats and Tourists', 'Resources for tourists planning a trip to the Czech Republic, expatriates living there or people doing business with Czechs.', '', 6, '2005-02-15 17:28:23', 30, 10, '', '', 0),
(49, 'Summer Schools & Courses', 'Summer Schools/Courses', 'Links to sites with information about courses teaching Czech. Most of them are summer schools taking place in the Czech Republic.', '\r\n        <p>This section lists sites with information about Summer Schools and\r\n        Courses in the Czech Republic. The list is by no means exclusive,\r\n        focusing mostly on schools that provide at least one summer intensive\r\n        program. Nearly all private language schools in Prague also offer Czech\r\n        for Foreigners.</p>\r\n        <p>Czech courses (as well as those of other \'Less Commonly Taught\r\n        Languages) available in the USA at all levels are listed at <a href=\"http://carla.acad.umn.edu/lctl/access.html\">http://carla.acad.umn.edu/lctl/access.html</a>.\r\n        In the UK, Czech is taught at <a href=\"http://www.ssees.ac.uk\">University\r\n        College London</a>, <a href=\"http://www.bristol.ac.uk\">University of\r\n        Bristol</a>, <a href=\"http://www.ox.ac.uk\">Oxford University</a>, <a href=\"http://www.gla.ac.uk\">University\r\n        of Glasgow</a>, <a href=\"http://www.sheffield.ac.uk\">University of\r\n        Sheffield</a> and <a href=\"http://www.wolverhampton.ac.uk\">University of\r\n        Wolverhampton</a>. </p>\r\n        <p>If you want to know where to learn Czech in your country get in touch\r\n        with a local embassy or consulate. Many Czech Centers associated with\r\n        embassies also offer Czech courses. A list of all Czech embassies,\r\n        consulates  and Czech Centers  can be found at <a href=\"http://www.czech.cz\">http://www.czech.cz</a>\r\n        (The Czech Ministry of Foreign Affairs web site).</p>\r\n        <p>A very comprehensive if slightly out-of-date list can be found\r\n        at  <a href=\"http://www.slavic.ohio-state.edu/people/holdeman/czech/main.htm\">http://www.slavic.ohio-state.edu/<br /> people/holdeman/czech/main.htm</a>.\r\n        Some of the information is incomplete or no longer accurate but always a\r\n        good pointer.</p>\r\n', 6, '2005-10-13 19:10:26', 10, 40, '', '', 0),
(50, 'Portals and Search Engines', 'Portals and Search Engines', 'Czech portals and search engines where more information can be found.', '', 6, '2002-11-16 14:51:48', 20, 40, '', '', 0),
(51, 'Czech Media', 'Czech Media', 'Links to sites with online versions of Czech newspapers, radios and TVs. Start here, if you want to listen to Czech or see some Czech visuals.', '', 6, '2005-06-12 21:45:49', 20, 20, '', '', 0),
(52, 'Culture, History, Literature', 'Culture, History, Literature', 'Various sites with information about Czech culture, history and literature. Some in Czech and some in English.', '', 6, '2002-10-15 04:12:11', 20, 10, '', '', 0),
(53, 'Czech Language Info', 'Information about Czech', 'Sites with all sorts of information about the Czech language. Some with broader purpose (such as the Czech national corpus).', '<br />\r\n', 6, '2005-11-10 18:17:11', 10, 10, '', '', 0),
(54, 'Courses Outside Prague', 'Courses Outside Prague', 'Courses and Summer Schools based in the Czech Republic and outside Prague. Given Prague\'s location, these are highly recommended.', '', 49, '2002-08-10 23:50:59', 100, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(55, 'Prague-Based Courses', 'Prague-Based Courses', 'Courses based in Prague. Their advantage is in their location with all the expected disadvantages. Too much English spoken, too many distractions and high prices.', '', 49, '2002-08-10 23:52:12', 100, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(56, 'Czech Radio and TV', 'Czech Radio and TV', 'Radio and TV stations offering audio and video broadcasts in Czech. Many offer a host of other resources as well.', '', 51, '2005-12-21 02:09:17', 100, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(57, 'Newspapers online', 'Newspapers online', 'Czech newspapers and magazines offering their editions online. Some online-only publications as also included.', '', 51, '2002-10-20 15:51:54', 100, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(58, 'Czech History', 'Czech History', '', '', 52, '2002-10-16 16:18:35', 100, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(59, 'Czech Literature', 'Czech Literature', '', '', 52, '2002-10-24 01:23:23', 100, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(60, 'Czech Culture', 'Czech Culture', '', '', 52, '2002-10-12 22:15:17', 100, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(61, 'Czech Politics', 'Czech Politics', '', '', 52, '2002-10-17 02:28:24', 100, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
(64, 'Czech Language', 'Czech Language', 'Ask and answer questions about Czech. What do words mean? How to say something? How does Czech work? Help with translations.', '', 9, '2002-09-07 18:27:52', 10, 1, '', '?section=mb&mb_section=board&board=13', 0),
(65, 'Czech Culture/Travel', 'Czech Culture/Travel', 'Live in the Czech Republic? Going to visit? Discuss what it\'s like to interact with Czechs. Share dos and don\'ts. Offer insights and travel tips.', '', 9, '2002-10-17 22:03:28', 10, 2, '', '?section=mb&mb_section=board&board=14', 0),
(66, 'Czech Students', 'Czech Students', 'Discuss your progress. Share successes, frustrations and learning tips and tricks.', '', 9, '2002-10-17 22:03:47', 10, 3, '', '?section=mb&mb_section=board&board=15', 0),
(67, ' Czech Teachers', '', 'Share lesson ideas and discuss issues related to teaching Czech. In Czech or English.\r\n', '', 9, '2002-11-08 05:42:45', 10, 4, '', '?section=mb&mb_section=board&board=16', 0),
(68, 'Česká konverzace', 'Česká konverzace', 'Česká diskuse o české hudbě, českém filmu, četině,  České Republice a víc.  <i>[Discussion in Czech about Czech film, music, language and more.]</i>', '', 9, '2003-02-20 14:20:53', 10, 5, '', '?section=mb&mb_section=board&board=17', 0),
(70, 'Grammar Exercises', 'Grammar Exercises', 'Practice your grammar with these exercises.', 'The exercises in this section are intended to help you practice the language in a controlled environment.  <p>\r\nThese exercises form a part of a course for registered students. They are free for all to use but only fee-paying students will have them corrected by a Bohemica.com teacher. (This service is not yet available).<p>\r\n\r\nThey are sorted by grammar following the structure of the Yellow Pages. Obviously some exercises fit more than one category. \r\n\r\n<p> You will need to install Czech keyboard on your computer. \r\n', 3, '2002-10-18 05:11:19', 10, 2, '', '', 0),
(71, 'Reading', 'Czech Reading Course', 'A full Czech reading course. The materials can also be used to practice Czech reading skills for students focusing on conversation.', 'This section presents a collection of reading materials for beginners and intermediate students. Each unit covers progressively more complex grammar and wider vocabulary. All exercises are intended to promote comprohension rather than production. To allow students to practice new vocabulary and grammar more thoroughly the first 15 units end with an exercise of translation from English into Czech. <p>\r\n\r\nYou will need to install Czech keyboard on your computer.\r\n', 3, '2002-10-20 16:09:58', 10, 3, '', '', 0),
(72, 'Games', 'Games', 'Quizzes and puzzles are a useful tool for learning languages. Expand your vocabulary while playing one of four different games.', 'Quizzes and puzzles are a useful tool for learning languages. Expand your vocabulary while playing one of four different games.', 3, '2002-10-20 22:40:23', 10, 4, '', '', 0),
(73, 'Grammar Book', 'The Yellow Pages of the Czech Language', 'This section contains a full version of <b>The Yellow Pages of the Czech Language</b>. Learn more about making sentences, using idioms and quite a bit of useful and interesting information about the language.', 'This section contains a full version of <b>The Yellow Pages of the Czech Language</b>. Learn more about making sentences, using idioms and quite a bit of useful and interesting information about the language.\r\n\r\n<p>The Yellow\r\nPages summarize in a comprehensive way all grammar points important in the\r\nstudy of Czech as a second language. They are organized into a system customary\r\nin the description of Czech grammar. That is the one a student is most likely\r\nto find in other Czech textbooks. The first section outlines this system\r\nbriefly along with the usual terminology. The following sections enlarge on\r\nindividual points, and contain the relevant charts. The final two sections deal\r\nwith trivia related to Czech such as idioms and the history of the language.</p>', 3, '2002-10-20 21:42:19', 15, 1, '', '', 0),
(74, 'Dictionary', 'Czech Dictionary', 'If you don\'t know a word used on Czech Online you will find it here. Several specialist dictionaries are also available.\r\n', 'If you don\'t know a word used on Czech Online you will find it here. Several specialist dictionaries are also available.\r\n', 3, '2002-10-24 14:02:09', 15, 2, '', '', 0),
(75, 'Course Login', 'Course Login', 'If you are a registered student, login here. Also click here, if you want to learn more about the subscription.', '', 3, '2004-02-06 00:30:13', 20, 3, '', 'http://www.bohemica.com/?m=catalog&s=10', 0),
(76, 'Conversation', 'Czech Conversation', 'A full course in Czech conversation at all levels. Tourist, beginner, advanced. ', 'Most of this section is still under construction. Eventually, it will provide conversation materials for students at all levels from the Casual tourist to advanced level. Most of this section will only be available by paid subscription, although it will be possible to view individual execises.', 3, '2004-09-12 18:40:30', 10, 1, '', '', 0),
(78, 'Czech Keyboard', 'Using and Installing the Czech Keyboard on the Computer', 'How to install it and use it. Plus other information about Czech and the computer.', '', 3, '2005-05-29 23:37:26', 200, 100, '', '', 1),
(79, 'Keyboard Layout', 'Czech Keyboard Layout', 'The Czech keyboard layout is very similar to the English layout. This document shows you how to enter the accented characters.', '', 78, '2002-10-24 15:20:28', 10, 1, '', '', 0),
(80, 'Keyboard Installation', 'Installing the Czech Keyboard', 'This document shows you how to install the Czech keyboard layout on your computer, which will allow you to enter Czech characters into any document, including exercises on Bohemica.com. Now, includes instructions for Windows XP.', '', 78, '2005-05-29 23:37:26', 10, 2, '', '', 0),
(81, 'Essays', 'Essays on the Czech Language', 'Essays by several authors dealing with different aspects of the Czech language.', 'Two authors have contributed to this section so far. Interesting contributions by others will also be considered. Please contact Dominik Luke, if you think you have something interesting to add.', 3, '2002-10-22 01:43:07', 15, 3, '', '', 0),
(82, 'Dominik Luke', 'Czech Essays by Dominik Luke', 'A range of essays on different aspects of Czech as a foreign language. Some of these have been published in the Prague Post and the Czech Republic Business Guide.', 'These essays were written by Dominik Luke as part of various projects. Some of them have been published or submitted for publication. These essays look at the Czech language from the perspective of a Czech teacher who\'s spent a lot of time with English-speaking students (both serious and not exactly as serious as that). <a href=index.php?m=catalog&s=84>You can read more about Dominik here</a>. \r\n<p>\r\n\r\nYou can read more essays by Dominik on other subjects including his published work in Czech for Lidové Noviny and Respekt <a href=index.php?m=catalog&s=16>here</a>. \r\n', 81, '2002-10-24 03:58:26', 1, 100, '', '', 0),
(83, 'Erik Piper', 'Essays on the Czech Language by Erik Piper', 'These essays concentrate on interesting aspects of Czech grammar from the perspective of a learner and a translator.', 'These essays were written by Erik Piper especially for Bohemica.com. Erik is a professional translator and likes to look at things in depth.<p>\r\n\r\nErik Piper, 31, translator, living in Brno. Born in Chicago, grew up in small-town Ohio, studied French and communications (with a concentration in public relations) at Wartburg College in Waverly, Iowa. Joined the Church of the Brethren\'s volunteer program, Brethren Volunteer Service, right after graduation, ending up as an assistant to Hnutí DUHA, a Czech homegrown environmental movement, in 1993-95. My most important achievement there was Not Stopping [the] Temelín [NPP]. Since then I have gone through several jobs, the longest-lasting of which was as a software tester for Moravia Translations (now Moravia IT). Married, 1 daughter.<p>\r\n<img src=images/people/erikpic.jpg>\r\n\r\n', 81, '2003-02-03 04:24:18', 2, 100, '', '', 0),
(84, 'Dominik Luke', 'About Dominik Luke - Bohemica\'s Creator', '', '', 16, '2002-10-25 18:19:25', 100, 100, '', '', 1),
(85, 'Introduction to Czech', 'Introduction to Studying Czech Language', 'A collection of articles published in the <a href=http://www.praguepost.cz>Prague Post</a>. ', '', 17, '2002-10-30 20:04:00', 10, 1, '', '', 0),
(86, 'Czech Tidbits', 'Czech Tidbits - Short Essays on Czech', 'Several essays about Czech language and culture from English language (especially American) perspective. ', '', 17, '2002-11-01 02:36:45', 10, 2, '', '', 0),
(88, 'Czech in Glasgow', 'Czech in Glasgow', '', '', 76, '2004-06-28 14:46:21', 100, 100, 'http://www.bohemica.com/images/logos/czechinglasgow.gif', '', 1),
(89, 'Czech Level 1', 'Czech Level 1', 'Pages associated with Czech Level 1. Course outline. Introduction to grammar.', 'This course is taught jointly by Dominik Luke and Ilona Bílková (Course Convener). Dominik teaches 4 classes a week and Ilona teaches one hour of conversation a week. Students are also required to attend one introductory grammar class a week taught by John Dunn. In the second term, one hour of work with literary texts taught by Jan Čulík will replace one of the classes taught by Dominik.', 88, '2004-06-28 14:46:21', 10, 10, 'http://www.bohemica.com/images/logos/czechinglasgow.gif', '', 0),
(90, 'Czech Level 2', 'Czech Level 2', 'Pages for students of the Czech Level 2 course.', 'This course is taught jointly by Robert Porter, Ilona Bílková and Dominik Luke. Ilona teaches two hours of grammar a week, Dominik teaches one hour of conversation a week plus one hour of translation into English every other week. Bob teaches two hours of working with literary texts.', 88, '2002-11-25 17:07:00', 10, 20, 'images/logos/czechinglasgow.gif', '', 0),
(91, 'Czech Level 3', 'Czech Level 3', 'Pages related to the Czech Level 3 course', '', 88, '2002-11-13 02:41:31', 10, 30, 'images/logos/czechinglasgow.gif', '', 0),
(92, 'Czech Senior Honours', 'Czech Level 4 - Senior Honours', 'Pages related to the Czech Level 4 course', '', 88, '2003-03-10 07:08:02', 10, 40, 'images/logos/czechinglasgow.gif', '', 0),
(93, 'National Identity', 'Uncovering a Nation\'s Identity: A case of the little Czech and the Great Czech nation', 'Pages for the Honours Option course <i>Uncovering a Nation\'s Identity: A case of the little Czech and the Great Czech nation</i>.', '<SPAN style=\"mso-ansi-language: EN-US\">A reading seminar on the anthropological \r\napproach to cultural and political studies of Central and Eastern Europe taking \r\nas its departure point and methodological benchmark Ladislav H</SPAN><SPAN \r\nlang=CS>olýs 1996 </SPAN><SPAN style=\"mso-ansi-language: EN-US\">book <I>The \r\nLittle Czech and the Great Czech Nation: National Identity and the \r\nPost-Communist Transformation of Society</I>. </SPAN>\r\n<p>\r\nThe seminar will meet once a week to discuss a portion of the central text and/or one of the supplemental readings. Students reading will be guided by worksheets prepared to facilitate better understanding of the text and put it into a broader context. Over the course of two semesters, students will be asked to write two essays one from a personal perspective and the other being a symbolic analysis of a chosen area of the nationalist discourse. Together with the worksheets, the essays will serve as a basis for  assessment (see below). On several occasions, students will be asked to participate in a simulation activity to demonstrate the personal level of group identity.\r\n\r\n', 88, '2002-11-09 19:40:27', 20, 100, 'images/logos/czechinglasgow.gif', '', 0),
(94, 'Conversation Forums', 'Conversation Forums', 'You can practice conversation on a variety of topics at all levels taught here.', 'This section contains links to discussion boards. The discussion board related to individual classes are available only to registered students who must log in to the course first, before they use them.<p>\r\nThe General Czech Discussion (containing 5 forums) is hosted by Bohemica.com and is available to everybody without a password. All University of Glasgow students are encouraged to take part in the Public discussion as well.', 88, '2002-11-09 19:40:42', 30, 10, 'images/logos/czechinglasgow.gif', '', 0),
(95, 'Coursework Login', 'Coursework Login', 'Registered students can login here, to see their latest assignments and do their homework.', '', 88, '2002-11-25 17:06:38', 24, 9, '', 'http://www.arts.gla.ac.uk/slavonic/czech/tuit/index.php', 0),
(97, 'Czech Grammar as Czechs Learn It', 'Czech Grammar as Czechs Learn It', 'This section presents Czech grammar as Czechs know it. It will be useful to you when you communicate with your teachers or read Czech textbooks. ', 'This section presents Czech grammar as Czechs know it. It will be useful to you when you communicate with your teachers or read Czech textbooks. The English terminology is often not the same as you know it from the grammar of English. It is very likely, however, that you will find these terms in a typical Czech textbook.', 73, '2002-11-07 18:25:25', 10, 10, '', '', 0),
(98, 'Parts of Speech', 'Parts of Speech', 'Nouns (gender, cases, classes and lots of useful charts), adjectives, pronouns, numerals, verbs (tense, aspect, conjugation), adverbs, conjunctions, prepositions, and more.', '', 73, '2002-11-13 22:45:54', 10, 15, '', '', 0),
(99, 'Pronunciation and spelling', 'Pronunciation and spelling', 'Learn how to pronounce words and full sentences. It is also important to learn how to write what you hear.', '', 73, '2002-11-16 14:59:32', 10, 30, '', '', 0),
(100, 'Word order', 'Word order', 'Learn how to put words together into phrases, clauses and sentences. Learn how to stress the importance of things through rearranging the order of words in the sentence.', '', 73, '2002-10-13 04:01:27', 10, 40, '', '', 0),
(101, 'Idioms and vocabulary', 'Idioms and vocabulary building', 'Language is so much more than just grammar. In fact, without all these idioms and thematic vocabulary lists, you couldn\'t say much at all.', '', 73, '2002-11-25 13:18:13', 10, 50, '', '', 0),
(102, 'Czech Trivia', 'Czech Trivia', 'Learn about the history of Czech, how it compares to other languages and other interesting tidbits.', '', 73, '2002-11-25 15:05:34', 20, 10, '', '', 0),
(103, 'Course Record', 'Course Record', 'A record of what happens in class every week.', 'The record of what happened in class will appear every day here so please check this page regularly for updates. It will be particularly important when the time comes for revision. ', 89, '2003-04-22 01:36:02', 10, 10, '', '', 0),
(104, 'Homework', 'Homework', 'Description of homework from week to week.', 'All homework assignments will appear in this section. Please, check here if you\'re not sure what the assignment was. If you have any questions, post them on the <a href=http://www.slavonic.arts.gla.ac.uk/czech/tuit/index.php?section=mb&mb_section=board&board=18>Czech Level 1 Conversation forum</a>. You teacher will respond. Alternatively, you can send an email directly to <a href=mailto:d.lukes@arts.gla.ac.uk>Dominik</a> or <a href=mailto:i.bilkova@arts.gla.ac.uk>Ilona</a>.', 89, '2003-03-17 19:10:32', 10, 20, '', '', 0),
(105, 'Online Conversation', 'Online Conversation: Czech Level 1', 'Practice your conversation skills online.', '', 89, '2002-11-25 13:24:03', 10, 30, '', 'http://www.slavonic.arts.gla.ac.uk/czech/tuit/index.php?section=mb&mb_section=board&board=18', 0),
(106, 'Grammar Introduction', 'Grammat Introduction', 'Notes and exercises to help you grasp the basic principles of Czech grammar in comparison with English grammar.', '', 89, '2002-11-25 14:14:01', 20, 10, '', 'http://www.bohemica.com/?m=tuit&unit=3', 0),
(107, 'Czech Level 1 Conversation', '', 'Online conversation forum for students of Czech Level 1. Discuss in Czech the assigned conversation topics to practice or ask in English if you have trouble with your homework or any other general class related question.', '', 94, '2002-11-12 17:51:31', 10, 10, '', 'http://www.slavonic.arts.gla.ac.uk/czech/tuit/index.php?section=mb&mb_section=board&board=18', 0),
(108, 'Czech Level 2 Conversation', '', 'Online conversation for students at Level 2. Větina diskuse by měla být česky. Conversation in Czech only but urgent (complicated) questions are permitted. ', '', 94, '2002-11-25 14:19:20', 10, 20, '', 'http://www.slavonic.arts.gla.ac.uk/czech/tuit/index.php?section=mb&mb_section=board&board=19', 0),
(109, 'Czech Level 3 Conversation', '', 'Diskusní fórum pro vechny pokročilé studenty, ale nejdůleitějí pro studenty úrovně 3. Povoleny jsou pouze české příspěvky.', '', 94, '2002-11-25 14:18:08', 10, 30, '', 'http://www.slavonic.arts.gla.ac.uk/czech/tuit/index.php?section=mb&mb_section=board&board=20', 0),
(110, 'National Identity', '', 'Discussion for students attending course: <i>Uncovering a Nation\'s Identity: A Case of the Little Czech and the Great Czech Nation</i>.', '', 94, '2002-11-22 14:38:48', 20, 10, '', 'http://www.slavonic.arts.gla.ac.uk/czech/tuit/index.php?section=mb&mb_section=board&board=22', 0),
(111, 'General Czech Discussion', '', 'Link to Czech discussion Forums on <a href=http://www.bohemica.com/forum>Bohemica.com</a>. Debate things Czech together with the wider public.', '', 94, '2002-10-13 17:33:11', 40, 10, '', 'http://www.bohemica.com/forum/index.php', 0),
(112, 'Czech Links', '', 'Links to a variety of internet resources for learners of Czech hosted by Bohemica.com.', '', 88, '2002-11-24 18:17:04', 30, 15, '', 'http://www.bohemica.com/links', 0),
(113, 'Nouns', 'Nouns', 'Everything about nouns: classes, declension (cases), etc.', '', 98, '2002-11-30 01:31:59', 10, 10, '', '', 0),
(114, 'Adjectives', 'Adjectives', 'What types of adjectives are there. How to change their form. How to compare things or say that something is best.', '', 98, '2002-11-21 19:30:59', 10, 20, '', '', 0),
(115, 'Conversation Topics', 'Conversation Topics', 'A list of conversation topics for the conversation class.', '', 89, '2002-12-17 19:44:38', 10, 25, '', '', 0),
(117, 'Conversation Topics', 'Conversation Topics', 'Conversation topics for the next two semester. ', 'This list outlines the basic topics for conversation classes in the academic year 2002/2003. Sections containing relevant materials and detailed assignments will be added.\r\n\r\n<p>1.	Problém času v dnení době - Máme volného času moc nebo málo?<br>\r\n2.	Ve zdravém těle zdravý duch<br>\r\n3.	Má nejzajímavějí cesta do zahraničí<br>\r\n4.	Móda - jak se oblékali moji rodiče a jak se oblékám já<br>\r\n5.	Srovnání Glasgow a Prahy<br>\r\n6.	Televize - pro i proti<br>\r\n7.	České dějiny a česká přítomnost<br>\r\n8.	Čechy a Evropa ve 21. století<br>\r\n9.	Obchody a sluby v České republice a ve Velké Británii<br>\r\n10.	Můj oblíbený spisovatel a já<br>\r\n11.	Jak člověk pokozuje ivotní prostředí<br>\r\n12.	Výhody a nevýhody městské hromadné dopravy<br>\r\n13.	Co mi přináí studium četiny<br>\r\n14.	Nejlepí film (divadelní hra) tohoto roku<br>\r\n15.	Na co jsou Čei hrdí a za co se stydí? (Je historie národa důleitá pro pochopení jeho vývoje?)</p>\r\n', 90, '2003-04-22 17:06:26', 10, 10, '', '', 0),
