(190, 'Czech Literature Presentations', 'Czech Literature Presentations', 'Pages for Czech Component of student presentations of Slavonic Studies Level 1, Module 1A. Students can also further discuss issues raised in class on the Literature Forum.', 'This section is designed to supplement the Czech Component of Slavonic Studies Level 1, Module 1A. <p>\r\nStudents wishing to post their handouts and notes here, can do so. <p>\r\n\r\n<b>All students are encouraged to take part in discussions on the <a href=http://www.slavonic.arts.gla.ac.uk/czech/tuit/index.php?section=mb&mb_section=board&board=23>Literature Forum</a> where everybody can discuss in more detail issues raised in class.</b><p>\r\n\r\nIf you have any questions about this site or the Czech component presentations, please contact <a href=mailto:d.lukes@arts.gla.ac.uk>Dominik Luke</a>.\r\n\r\n<p><i>For technical reasons, parts of this section are currently hosted by Bohemica.com</i>\r\n', 88, '2005-07-02 15:38:18', 20, 110, 'images/logos/czechinglasgow.gif', '', 0),
