(203, 'Poetry Contest', 'Poetry Contest 2002: Czech, Polish, Russian', 'Take part in the Department of Slavonic Studies\' <b>Poetry Contest</b> in Czech, Polish and Russian. Anybody can participate (including beginners).', 'Welcome to the University of Glasgow Department of Slavonic Studies <b>Poetry Contest 2002</b>.<p>\r\n\r\n<ol>\r\n  <li>Choose any poem from the nine presented (in Czech, Polish, Russian). One of the poems in each language was chosen specifically for Level 1 students.</li>\r\n  <li>Translate it into English.</li>\r\n  <li>Submit your entry to the Departmental Office by 5 p.m. on Thursday 12 December.</li>\r\n  <li>A jury will assess all the entries (anonymously) and nominate a winner for each of the languages.</li>\r\n  <li>The best poems will be read out at the official ceremony.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n\r\n<center>The <b>official prize-giving ceremony</b> will take place on <br>\r\n<b>18 December, 2.30 p.m.</b> <br>\r\nall students, staff and friends are welcome.\r\n</center>', 88, '2002-11-25 15:02:28', 20, 120, 'images/logos/czechinglasgow.gif', '', 0),
