goya@rio.odn.ne.jp\">elsnagoya@rio.odn.ne.jp</a>\r\n </p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr><td width=\"14%\" valign=\"top\"><b>Services:</b>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"86%\" valign=\"top\" colspan=\"3\"><p>Czech language, Beginners -&gt; Advance Courses</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<hr />\r\n<table width=\"100%\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"2\" border=\"0\"><tbody><tr><td width=\"14%\" valign=\"top\"><b>Name:</b>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"34%\" valign=\"top\"><p>Adéla Stoulilová \r\n</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"15%\" valign=\"top\"><b>Location:</b>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"43%\" valign=\"top\">Taiwan, Taipei</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr><td width=\"14%\" valign=\"top\"><b>Contact:</b>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"86%\" valign=\"top\" colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"mailto:adela.stoulilova@gmail.com\">adela.stoulilova@gmail.com</a> \r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr><td width=\"14%\" valign=\"top\"><b>Services:</b>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"86%\" valign=\"top\" colspan=\"3\"><p>Available to teach Czech (private, individual, groups), fluent in English and Chinese. </p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table><hr style=\"width: 100%; height: 2px;\" /> <table width=\"100%\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"2\" border=\"0\"><tbody><tr><td width=\"14%\" valign=\"top\"><b>Name:</b>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"34%\" valign=\"top\"><p>Roman Cihlář <img width=\"34\" height=\"10\" border=\"0\" src=\"../images/new.gif\" />\r\n</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"15%\" valign=\"top\"><b>Location:</b>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"43%\" valign=\"top\">Taiwan, Taipei</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr><td width=\"14%\" valign=\"top\"><b>Contact:</b>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"86%\" valign=\"top\" colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"mailto:djthunder@centrum.cz\">djthunder@centrum.cz</a><br /></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr><td width=\"14%\" valign=\"top\"><b>Services:</b>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"86%\" valign=\"top\" colspan=\"3\"><p>I provide private one-on-one Czech and English lessons. Fluent in English.<br /> </p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table><hr style=\"width: 100%; height: 2px;\" /> \r\n<table width=\"100%\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"2\" border=\"0\"><tbody><tr><td width=\"14%\" valign=\"top\"><b>Name:</b>\r\n </td>\r\n<td width=\"34%\" valign=\"top\"><p>Jan Sláma <img width=\"34\" height=\"10\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://www.bohemica.com/images/new.gif\" />\r\n </p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td width=\"15%\" valign=\"top\"><b>Location:</b>\r\n </td>\r\n<td width=\"43%\" valign=\"top\">Thailand, Bangkok<br /></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr><td width=\"14%\" valign=\"top\"><b>Contact:</b>\r\n </td>\r\n<td width=\"86%\" valign=\"top\" colspan=\"3\"><p align=\"left\"><a href=\"mailto:janslama007@yahoo.com\">janslama007@yahoo.com</a> <br /></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr><td width=\"14%\" valign=\"top\"><b>Services:</b>\r\n </td>\r\n<td width=\"86%\" valign=\"top\" colspan=\"3\"><p>Translation service, czech lessons - grammar and conversation topics.</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<hr />\r\n<br /><br />', 44, 0, 1),
(16, '', 'Sorry. There are no teachers in this section yet. Please feel free to recomment that they sign up. <p>\r\n\r\nAny teachers or institutions residing in this area are welcome to place information about themselves <a href=\"contact/newteacher.htm\"> here for free!</a>', 43, 0, 1),
(17, '', '<table cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"2\" width=\"100%\" border=\"0\"><tbody><tr><td valign=\"top\" width=\"14%\"><b>Name:</b>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"34%\"><p>Pedro Alexandre Barreto Coelho</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"15%\"><b>Location:</b>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"43%\">Brazil, Belo Horizonte </td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr><td valign=\"top\" width=\"14%\"><b>Contact:</b>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"86%\" colspan=\"3\"><p align=\"left\">+ 55 31 9209 0733; <a href=\"mailto:pabc00@hotmail.com\">pabc00@hotmail.com</a>\r\n<font size=\"2\"> </font>\r\n</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr><td valign=\"top\" width=\"14%\"><b>Services:</b>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"86%\" colspan=\"3\"><p>I was a Rotary Youth Exchange Student in the Czech Republic (Ostrava), and I lived there from 2003 to 2004 and on my one year stay in the Czech i learned a lot not just the language but about the culture, what is really interesting. I\'m opening for contacts, so if you want to learn Czech or just want to know some information about the Czech Republic where&nbsp;I had the \"best year of my life\" just contact me.I will be glad if you are interest about this amazing and incredible country.Thank you very much! </p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<hr />\r\n<p><table cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"2\" width=\"100%\" border=\"0\"><tbody><tr><td valign=\"top\" width=\"14%\"><b>Name:</b>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"34%\"><p>Mario Enrique Espitia López <img height=\"10\" src=\"http://www.bohemica.com/images/new.gif\" width=\"34\" border=\"0\" />\r\n</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"15%\"><b>Location:</b>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"43%\">Colombia, Bogotá</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr><td valign=\"top\" width=\"14%\"><b>Contact:</b>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"86%\" colspan=\"3\"><p align=\"left\">571 6927409; <a href=\"mailto:Mario.Espitia@seznam.cz\">Mario.Espitia@seznam.cz</a>\r\n </p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr><td valign=\"top\" width=\"14%\"><b>Services:</b>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"86%\" colspan=\"3\"><p>Hello friends!!!. I lived in Czech Republik since 1985 to 1992. I studied in Prague, but I learned Czech in Dobruka. I also learned about their culture and history. I´m opening to share with you, not only my experince in this very nice land, but the language.</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</p>\r\n<hr />\r\n<p>Any more teachers or institutions residing in this area are welcome to place information about themselves <a href=\"contact/newteacher.htm\">here for free!</a>\r\n</p>\r\n', 42, 0, 1),
(18, '', '<A HREF=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/redirect-home/bohemicacom\"><IMG SRC=\"images/logos/amazoncom.gif\" BORDER=\"0\"\r\nalt=\"Buy a book from Amazon.com!\"></A> <br> <A HREF=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/redirect-home?tag=bohemicacom0d&site=amazon\"><IMG SRC=\"images/logos/amazonuk.gif\" alt=\"In Association with Amazon.co.uk\" border=\"0\"></A>\r\n', 7, 1, 200);
INSERT INTO `xc_text` (`xct_id`, `xct_header`, `xct_text`, `xct_section`, `xct_type`, `xct_priority`) VALUES
(19, '', 'Only selected titles are available to purchase online. After you click on the title of the book you want, you will be taken to Amazon\'s site. <table cellspacing=\"1\" width=\"100%\" border=\"0\"><tbody><tr><td style=\"PADDING-RIGHT: 5.4pt; PADDING-LEFT: 5.4pt; PADDING-BOTTOM: 0cm; PADDING-TOP: 0cm\" valign=\"top\"><table width=\"100%\" border=\"0\"><tbody><tr><td valign=\"top\" width=\"20%\"><a href=\"http://images.amazon.com/images/P/0844237582.01.LZZZZZZZ.jpg\"><img height=\"140\" hspace=\"5\" src=\"http://images.amazon.com/images/P/0844237582.01.MZZZZZZZ.jpg\" width=\"89\" align=\"left\" vspace=\"3\" border=\"1\" />\r\n </a>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"80%\"><p><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0844238554/bohemicacom\"><b>Teach Yourself Czech<br />\r\n</b>\r\n</a>\r\n<font color=\"#800000\">by David Short (1993)</font>\r\n - A professional-looking book best-suited to very motivated students. It is very well organized if a little too traditional. More advanced learners may profit from the dialogues which often contain less common phrases. The same fact may obscure the meaning of some dialogues to a less through beginner. The plentiful grammatical explanations are very thorough and detail. Also contains useful appendices (index, vocabulary list). It also contains a lesson on archaic language used in written texts of today.&nbsp;<small><small><small><b><span lang=\"EN-US\"><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/0340571209/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990033\"><br />\r\nBuy from Amazon.co.uk</font>\r\n </a>\r\n</span>\r\n</b>\r\n</small>\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\"><b><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>- </small>\r\n</font>\r\n</b>\r\n</span>\r\n</small>\r\nbook and tape; <b><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/0844237582/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy from Amazon.co.uk</small>\r\n </font>\r\n</a>\r\n<small></small>\r\n</small>\r\n</span>\r\n</font>\r\n</b>\r\n</small>\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small><small><small>- </small>\r\n</small>\r\n</small>\r\n</b>\r\n</font>\r\n</span>\r\n<small>book only; <span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/0340571217/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small><small>Buy from Amazon.co.uk</small>\r\n </small>\r\n</font>\r\n</a>\r\n<small><small></small>\r\n</small>\r\n</b>\r\n</font>\r\n<small><small><font face=\"Arial\">- </font>\r\n</small>\r\n</small>\r\n</span>\r\ntape only<small>;<small><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b> </b>\r\n</font>\r\n</span>\r\n</small>\r\n</small>\r\n<a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0844238554/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small>Buy from Amazon.com</small>\r\n </b>\r\n</font>\r\n</a>\r\n<font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small>&nbsp;</small>\r\n </b>\r\n</font>\r\n</small>\r\n<font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small><small><small><span lang=\"EN-US\">- </span>\r\n</small>\r\n</small>\r\n</small>\r\n</b>\r\n</font>\r\n<small>book and tape; </small>\r\n<a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0844237582/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small><small>Buy from Amazon.com </small>\r\n</small>\r\n</b>\r\n</font>\r\n</a>\r\n<small>- book only </small>\r\n</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr><td valign=\"top\" width=\"20%\"><img height=\"140\" hspace=\"5\" src=\"http://images.amazon.com/images/P/0415161347.01.MZZZZZZZ.gif\" width=\"86\" align=\"left\" vspace=\"3\" border=\"1\" />\r\n </td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"80%\"><p class=\"TableSmall\"><b><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0415161363/bohemicacom\">Colloquial Czech</a>\r\n &nbsp;</b>\r\n <br />\r\n<font color=\"#800000\">by James Naughton (1999) </font>\r\n- New improved version of an older textbook. The old book suffered from funny dialogues, and was not well-structured and suited to learners needs. The new book is much improved but may still be difficult for complete beginners.&nbsp; More advanced learners, however, might profit from listening to the tape. Some people also like the grammatical explanations. Given the amount of material presented it contains relatively few exercises, and a modest dictionary. The language is much less colloquial than the situations.</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableSmall\" style=\"TEXT-ALIGN: justify\">Tape sold with the book which may be good for learning pronunciation of some less common or more complex phrases. It will also give you a chance to listen to fairly realistic dialogues. The recordings are very professional.<a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0415161363/bohemicacom\"><small><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small><br />\r\nBuy from Amazon.com</small>\r\n </b>\r\n</font>\r\n</small>\r\n</a>\r\n<b><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0415161363/bohemicacom\"><small><small></small>\r\n</small>\r\n</a>\r\n<small><small>/</small>\r\n </small>\r\n</font>\r\n</b>\r\n<small><b><small><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/0415161363/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy from Amazon.co.uk</small>\r\n </font>\r\n</a>\r\n</span>\r\n</font>\r\n</small>\r\n</b>\r\n</small>\r\n</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableSmall\" style=\"TEXT-ALIGN: justify\"></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<table width=\"100%\" border=\"0\"><tbody><tr><td valign=\"top\" width=\"20%\">&nbsp;<img src=\"/bookstore/pictures/stepbystepcover.jpg\" />\r\n </td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" width=\"80%\"><p class=\"TableSmall\"><u><font color=\"#800080\"><strong><a href=\"http://www.czechstepbystep.cz\">New Czech Step by Step</a>\r\n</strong>\r\n <img height=\"10\" src=\"/images/new.gif\" width=\"34\" border=\"0\" />\r\n </font>\r\n</u>\r\n<strong><br />\r\n</strong>\r\n<font color=\"#800000\">by Lída Holá</font>\r\n (2004) New, completely redesigned, edition of a popular textbook with its own website at <a href=\"http://www.czechstepbystep.cz/English/sample.htm\">http://www.czechstepbystep.cz</a>\r\n .&nbsp;This textbook is&nbsp;more in the style of internationally popular&nbsp;texts for English, French or German. Its main focus is on communication with the right amount of grammar. It has an attractive,&nbsp;clear and easy to navigate layout (see sample on webpage) and fairly realistic and interesting dialogues and texts. It comes with a very good workbook and a 120-min Audio CD of very good quality (particularly when compared to some of the competition). It can be purchased at a Czech online bookstore <a href=\"http://www.kosmas.cz/\">http://www.kosmas.cz</a>\r\n which unfortunately only has a Czech interface.</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<br />\r\n<p class=\"TableSmall\" style=\"TEXT-ALIGN: justify\"><b>Communicative Czech (Elementary and Intermediate)<br />\r\n</b>\r\n<font color=\"#800000\">by Ivana Bednářová and Magda Pintarová, (1996)</font>\r\n Although far from perfect, these books belong among the top communicative textbooks of Czech as a foreign language. They cover a wide range of grammar and communicative topics. A vocabulary list and a collection of grammar charts are useful supplements. They come with a workbook and tapes as well.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Tschechisch anders NEU</strong>\r\n <img height=\"10\" src=\"http://www.bohemica.com/images/new.gif\" width=\"34\" border=\"0\" />\r\n<br />\r\n<font color=\"#8b0000\">Aigner, Alena - Gruber, Olga (2004)</font>\r\n An updated version of an older textbook (see below) this time with an 80-min &nbsp;CD rather than a cassette. More info and orders at <a href=\"mailto:aigner@eec.at\">aigner@eec.at</a>\r\n.</p>\r\n<font size=\"2\"><p class=\"TableSmall\" style=\"TEXT-ALIGN: justify\"><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0415115426/bohemicacom\"><b><br />\r\nColloquial Slovak : The Complete Course for Beginners</b>\r\n </a>\r\n&nbsp;<br />\r\n<font color=\"#800000\">by J. D. Naughton. Paperback (1997) </font>\r\n- Similar in style and structure to <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0415161363/bohemicacom\">Colloquial Czech</a>\r\n .</p>\r\n</font>\r\n<a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0415115426/bohemicacom\"><b><br />\r\nColloquial Slovak : The Complete Course for Beginners</b>\r\n </a>\r\n&nbsp;<br />\r\n<font color=\"#800000\">by J. D. Naughton. Paperback (1997) </font>\r\n- Similar in style and structure to <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0415161363/bohemicacom\">Colloquial Czech</a>\r\n .<p><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/0852615361/bohemicacom0d\"><b>Mluvte s námi Česky</b>\r\n <br />\r\n</a>\r\n<font color=\"#800000\">by Josef Fronek (1996) </font>\r\nAn interesting textbook from the University of Glasgow, Language Centre.<font face=\"geneva, arial, helvetica\" size=\"-1\"><br />\r\n</font>\r\n<b><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\"><small>Not at Amazon.com /&nbsp; </small>\r\n</font>\r\n</b>\r\n<small><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/0852615361/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy from Amazon.co.uk</small>\r\n </font>\r\n</a>\r\n</small>\r\n</b>\r\n</font>\r\n</span>\r\n</small>\r\n</p>\r\n<p><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0893570982/bohemicacom\"><b>Contemporary Czech<br />\r\n</b>\r\n</a>\r\n<font color=\"#800000\">by Michael Heim<span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"FONT-FAMILY: \" new=\"\" times=\"\"> (</span>\r\n 1982)</font>\r\n <font color=\"#808000\"></font>\r\n- A more advanced book presupposing some knowledge of a related Slavic language (Russian, Polish), certainly not very good for communicative study but could be useful for reference.<small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0893570982/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small><br />\r\nBuy from Amazon.com</small>\r\n </b>\r\n</font>\r\n</a>\r\n</small>\r\n<b><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\"><small>/&nbsp; </small>\r\n</font>\r\n</b>\r\n<small><b><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/0893570982/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy from Amazon.co.uk</small>\r\n </font>\r\n</a>\r\n</span>\r\n</font>\r\n</b>\r\n</small>\r\n&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0893571547/bohemicacom\"><b>Readings in Czech (UCLA Slavic Studies, Vol 13)</b>\r\n </a>\r\n<font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\" size=\"-1\"><br />\r\n</font>\r\n<font color=\"#800000\">by Michael Heim, et al. (1985) </font>\r\nGreat companion to <a href=\"http://\">Contemporary Czech</a>\r\n contains annotated texts from a variety of sources.<small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0893571547/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small><br />\r\nBuy from Amazon.com</small>\r\n </b>\r\n</font>\r\n</a>\r\n</small>\r\n&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/078944433X/bohemicacom\"><b>Hugo: Czech In Three Months (with Cassette)</b>\r\n </a>\r\n<br />\r\n<font color=\"#800000\">by Elisabeth Billington. Audio Cassette (1999)&nbsp;</font>\r\n Not a bad book despite its greatly misleading title. No language can be learned in three months no matter what. But this book provides good info.<small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/078944433X/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small><br />\r\nBuy from Amazon.com</small>\r\n </b>\r\n</font>\r\n</a>\r\n</small>\r\n<b><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\"><small>/&nbsp; </small>\r\n</font>\r\n</b>\r\n<small><b><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/078944433X/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy from Amazon.co.uk</small>\r\n </font>\r\n</a>\r\n</span>\r\n</font>\r\n</b>\r\n</small>\r\n&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0874152941/bohemicacom\"><b>A Practical Czech Course for English-Speaking Students</b>\r\n </a>\r\n<font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\" size=\"-1\"><br />\r\n</font>\r\n<font color=\"#800000\">by Milo Sova. Paperback (1962) </font>\r\nOld classic. May be worth having as a source of additional exercises and reference. The language and methodology are obviously dated but don\'t make the book useless.<small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0874152941/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small><br />\r\nBuy from Amazon.com</small>\r\n </b>\r\n</font>\r\n</a>\r\n</small>\r\n&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/2831569494/bohemicacom\"><b>Berlitz Czech Cassette and Book Pack</b>\r\n </a>\r\n<b></b>\r\n<font color=\"#990000\">1999<br />\r\n</font>\r\nA quality Berlitz tape. Unlike the Fast and Easy Czech tape, it gives you more time to repeat. The speakers pronounce more distinctly and the first utterance is always slower than the second. Good for jogging, cooking, or driving. The pack also contains a script and a phrasebook with a negligible dictionary and grammar section. The phrasebook can be purchased separately.<a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/2831569494/bohemicacom\"><small><b><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small><br />\r\nBuy from Amazon.com</small>\r\n </font>\r\n</b>\r\n</small>\r\n</a>\r\n<font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small></small>\r\n</b>\r\n</font>\r\n<b><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\"><small>/&nbsp; </small>\r\n</font>\r\n</b>\r\n<small><b><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/2831569494/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy from Amazon.co.uk</small>\r\n </font>\r\n</a>\r\n</span>\r\n</font>\r\n</b>\r\n</small>\r\n</p>\r\n<p><b>Vítáme vás! (Ein Tschechischleshrwerk für Anfänger)&nbsp;&nbsp;<br />\r\n</b>\r\n<font color=\"#800000\">by Věra Amorová</font>\r\n (1993) This is one of the most modern and communicatively oriented textbooks of Czech I\'ve seen. It is very similar to modern textbooks of German or English (such as Headway). Even though it was written for German-speaking learners it uses virtually no German in the text itself and could be used by anybody with a good teacher. It is definitely not a teach-yourself book. It is also very professional-looking, printed on good paper with plenty of good graphics (both hand-drawn and black and white photos). It takes a very cavalier approach to grammar. Grammar is introduced as and when communication requires it which in Czech could be quite overwhelming. On the other hand, the in-text explanations are clear, simple and limited to the necessary rules only. At the end of the book, there is a grammar overview which is all in German, though. It also contains a key to exercises and a small dictionary. It comes in two volumes (a textbook and a workbook). It contains several silly errors but other than that it is a very reliable communicative resource. </p>\r\n<p class=\"TableSmall\" style=\"TEXT-ALIGN: justify\">Although it was first published in 1993, it is not very well known and I\'ve only just had a chance to see it. The publisher is Hueber and the book appeared in the Sprachen der Welt series.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableSmall\" style=\"TEXT-ALIGN: justify\"><b>Czech Step by Step&nbsp; <br />\r\n</b>\r\n<font color=\"#800000\">by Lída Holá</font>\r\n (2000)&nbsp; Good layout and colors make it easy to use (for example, vocabulary lists use colors to differentiate between genders). Also, there are many interesting texts, such as an original interview with the famous Czech hockey player Jaromír Jágr. On the downside, it is centered around grammar rather than conversation topics, although each unit has a theme. However, the grammar is well explained and appropriate.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableSmall\" style=\"TEXT-ALIGN: justify\">If the textbook may seem too focused on grammar, the accompanying <b>workbook</b>\r\n has just the right mix of grammar and communication. Some of the exercises quite creatively practice different areas of communication. They can be used even by teachers and students who do not use the textbook as their main course material. There are also tapes which I haven\'t heard yet but since they use professional actors, I assume, they will be of quite good standard.</p>\r\n<p><b>Czech for Everyone</b>\r\n <br />\r\n<font color=\"#800000\">by Karin Rigerová, (2000)</font>\r\n &nbsp; Lively new textbook with nice layout and illustrations. Slightly too traditional in its approach to grammar but it has been successfully used in conversation courses run by the author. Contains a key to all exercises and can be used for self-study.</p>\r\n<p><b>Četina pro ekonomy</b>\r\n <br />\r\n<font color=\"#800000\">by Elga Čechová and Helena Remediosová (1999)</font>\r\n One of the few Czech textbooks for a specific purpose. It is designed for advanced students. Exercises are structured around business texts. Aside from its aim, it is fairly traditional with lots of grammar and not very exciting layout.</p>\r\n<p><b>Četina pro cizince</b>\r\n <font color=\"#800000\"><br />\r\nby Hronová and Turzíková , (1989)</font>\r\n A revised edition of a classic. Very comprehensive but also very traditional. Includes many dialogues, pictures, charts, and a lot of useful phrases. In the back, it has a small dictionary with equivalents in 3 languages.</p>\r\n<p><b>Učíme se česky I. and II.&nbsp;<br />\r\n</b>\r\n<font color=\"#800000\">by Kami (1992)</font>\r\n Nicely printed textbook in nice covers. Plenty of pictures but also very traditionally grammatically oriented. Contains no English.</p>\r\n<p><b>Czech For You</b>\r\n <br />\r\n<font color=\"#800000\">by Milena Kelly&nbsp; (1993)</font>\r\n Contains many drills and countless flashcards. Otherwise it is very superficial and not well outlined. The dialogues are sometimes inappropriate to the context, and not very well structured. Its main virtue is the 8 tapes, all recorded by professional speakers, giving you enough time to repeat everything several times. The book contains several mistakes.</p>\r\n<p><b>Do You Want To Speak Czech (Available in French, German, Italian, Spanish, Russian)</b>\r\n <br />\r\n<font color=\"#800000\">by Čechová M., H. Trabelsiová, H. Putz, (1993) </font>\r\nDo You Want To Speak Czech is not very suitable as a course book. The language is too hard and sometimes unnatural. Very often grammar introduced in a lesson is not sufficiently practiced in the subsequent exercises. More advanced students, however, will find this book very useful. It will help them to see what theyve learned in a different light.</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableSmall\" style=\"TEXT-ALIGN: justify\">The 2 tapes that come with it are not very good because the recordings are too fast, and hard to follow.</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableSmall\" style=\"TEXT-ALIGN: justify\">A version for advanced students is also available. A new improved edition of the beginner book is now also available.</p>\r\n<p><b>Tschechish Anders/Četina jinak<br />\r\n</b>\r\n<font color=\"#800000\">by Aignerová, A. (1994) </font>\r\nGerman-based textbook but very interesting. It is the only one I know that uses songs for its dialogues. It also contains many interesting exercises. You can buy a tape with all the songs. I would recommend it to people who speak some German, or to those who can read music. A tape containing all the songs comes with the book.</p>\r\n<p><b>Tschechish Wieder Anders/Četina zase jinak<br />\r\n</b>\r\n<font color=\"#800000\">by Aignerová, A. (1998) </font>\r\nShorter than the first book but with two tapes which include drills of all phrases. Again, most songs use well-known melodies and introduce important phrases. All songs rhyme which is aids memorization but on the downside sometimes the word order is changed to aid the rhyme. Still a useful book.</p>\r\n<p><b>Czech For Foreigners&nbsp;</b>\r\n <br />\r\n<font color=\"#800000\">by Parolková and Nováková, (1993) </font>\r\nContains a plenty of pictures and flashcards. It also has some very interesting exercises. It is far from comprehensive and generally disliked by students using it regularly. It may be a good springboard to better things.</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableSmall\" style=\"TEXT-ALIGN: justify\">The book is accompanied by a fairly good tape. It is the only tape, however, that contains comprehension exercises, and dictations. Unfortunately, the authors tried to squeeze too much into little space. I would recommend it for self study at a more advanced level to increase comprehension.</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableSmall\" style=\"TEXT-ALIGN: justify\">A set of scored tests are available with the book but it doesnt tell you what the scores mean.</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableSmall\" style=\"TEXT-ALIGN: justify\"><b>Český jazyk - 2000&nbsp;</b>\r\n <br />\r\n<font color=\"#800000\">by Jekaterina Aizpurvit, (2000) </font>\r\nCzech for Russian speakers. A very traditional but thourough book focusing mostly on translation exercises. It contains good grammar explanations, an extensive dictionary and interesting reading texts. The same publisher also specializes in Czech translations of modern Russian authors such as Boris Akunin.</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableSmall\" style=\"TEXT-ALIGN: justify\"><b>Czech (Pimsleur&nbsp; Language Program) <img height=\"10\" src=\"../images/new.gif\" width=\"34\" border=\"0\" />\r\n </b>\r\n<br />\r\n<font color=\"#800000\">by Malinovská, E., Malinovský, M, (1999) </font>\r\nAn audio only course of Czech for beginners published by Simon & Schuster (<a href=\"http://www.simonsays.com\">http://www.simonsays.com</a>\r\n ). I haven\'t actually seen it but I have no doubt that it is a good supplemental set of materials which cannot, however, replace a course and a textbook. It might work better for some people than others, too. Be very sceptical of the claims the website makes about this method in general. There are NO miracles in language learning. Just hard work.</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 40, 0, 1),
(20, '', 'Bohemica.com is preparing a course on CD-ROM. There are only two other Czech CD-ROMs available. <br />\r\n<p><strong>Talk Now! Learn Czech&nbsp;&nbsp;<br />\r\n</strong>\r\nNewly available CD-ROM on Amazon.com or Amazon.co.uk.<br />\r\n<a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/tg/detail/-/B0000899M8/qid=1113526220/sr=8-3/ref=sr_8_xs_ap_i3_xgl65/102-5008598-3051365?v=glance&s=software&n=507846\">http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/tg/detail/-/B0000899M8/qid=1113526220/sr=8-3/ref=sr_8_xs_ap_i3_xgl65/102-5008598-3051365?v=glance&s=software&n=507846</a>\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/B00004YZI9/ref=pd_ecs_sw_h__b_a/202-8700201-7118246\">http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/B00004YZI9/ref=pd_ecs_sw_h__b_a/202-8700201-7118246</a>\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<strong>Vocatude&nbsp;<br />\r\n</strong>\r\n<font color=\"#080000\">available at</font>\r\n<a href=\"\\&quot;http://www.volny.cz/vocatude/index.htm\\&quot;\"><font face=\"\\&quot;Arial\\&quot;\" size=\"\\&quot;2\\&quot;\"><br />\r\n</font>\r\nhttp://www.volny.cz/vocatude<br />\r\n</a>\r\nNew CD-ROM for vocabulary practice. It does no more than that (for example, it is not a dictionary, although it&nbsp; contains word lists) but it may be perfect for students who want to expand their passive vocabulary.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><b>Euro Talk Czech<br />\r\n</b>\r\n<font color=\"#080000\">available at </font>\r\n<a href=\"\\&quot;http://www.eurotalk.co.uk\\&quot;\">http://www.eurotalk.co.uk</a>\r\n<br />\r\nNot a very good product based on a template used for dozens of other languages. It only teaches the students selected vocabulary and a few phrases. Vocabulary is practiced through two different games. No other language information is available.</p>\r\n<p><b>WinCzEdu</b>\r\n<a href=\"\\&quot;http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0893570982/bohemicacom\\&quot;\"><b><br />\r\n</b>\r\n</a>\r\n<font color=\"#080000\">available at </font>\r\n<a href=\"\\&quot;http://mujweb.cz/www/winczeduc\\&quot;\">http://mujweb.cz/www/winczeduc<br />\r\n</a>\r\nA much superior product although it uses a very non standard interface. It is based on written&nbsp; texts about Czech history and contains a complete set of interactive grammar charts linked to the text. There are translation and fill-in-the-blank exercises to practice on. No conversation but all texts are read out by a professional voice.</p>\r\n', 41, 0, 1),
(21, '', 'Only selected titles are available to purchase online. After you click on the title of the book you want, you will be taken to Amazon\'s site. <table width=\"\\&quot;100%\\&quot;\" border=\"\\&quot;0\\&quot;\"><tbody><tr><td valign=\"\\&quot;top\\&quot;\" width=\"\\&quot;70%\\&quot;\"><p class=\"\\&quot;TableSmall\\&quot;\"><b><a href=\"\\&quot;http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/8085927489/bohemicacom0d\\&quot;\">English-Czech/Czech-English Dictionary</a>\r\n</b>\r\n<br />\r\n<font color=\"#080000\">by J. Fronek (1999) </font>\r\nWithout argument the very best dictionary for learners of Czech on the market. Provides useful grammatical information, context and clear layout. A must have for a serious learner. <font face=\"\\&quot;Arial\\&quot;\" color=\"#009000\" size=\"\\&quot;-1\\&quot;\"><b><small>Not at Amazon.com /&nbsp; </small>\r\n</b>\r\n</font>\r\n<span lang=\"\\&quot;EN-US\\&quot;\"><font face=\"\\&quot;Arial\\&quot;\" color=\"#009000\"><b><small><a href=\"\\&quot;http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/8085927489/bohemicacom0d\\&quot;\"><font face=\"\\&quot;Arial\\&quot;\" color=\"#009000\"><small>Buy from Amazon.co.uk</small>\r\n</font>\r\n</a>\r\n</small>\r\n</b>\r\n</font>\r\n</span>\r\n</p>\r\n<p class=\"\\&quot;TableSmall\\&quot;\">An older version of the Czech/English part from 1993 is also available separately. It doesn\\\'t include the grammar charts which make the bi-directional dictionary so great for students of English. <span lang=\"\\&quot;EN-US\\&quot;\"><font face=\"\\&quot;Arial\\&quot;\" color=\"#009000\"><b><small><a href=\"\\&quot;http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/8004243827/bohemicacom0d\\&quot;\"><font face=\"\\&quot;Arial\\&quot;\" color=\"#009000\"><small>Buy from Amazon.co.uk</small>\r\n</font>\r\n</a>\r\n</small>\r\n</b>\r\n</font>\r\n</span>\r\n</p>\r\n<p class=\"\\&quot;TableSmall\\&quot;\">Both of these dictionaries are also available from the publisher <a href=\"\\&quot;http://www.leda.cz\\&quot;\">Leda </a>\r\non CD-ROM.</p>\r\n<a href=\"\\&quot;http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0781806534/bohemicacom\\&quot;\"><b>Anglicko-Český / Česko-Anglický Dictionary</b>\r\n</a>\r\n <strong><font face=\"\\&quot;verdana,arial,helvetica\\&quot;\"><br />\r\n</font>\r\n</strong>\r\n<font color=\"#080000\">by Ivan Poldauf, Jan Caha, Alena Kepecká, Jiří Krámský&nbsp; (1998)</font>\r\n<br />\r\n<small><a href=\"\\&quot;http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0781806534/bohemicacom\\&quot;\"><font face=\"\\&quot;Arial\\&quot;\" color=\"#009000\"><b><small>Buy from Amazon.com</small>\r\n</b>\r\n</font>\r\n</a>\r\n </small>\r\n<font face=\"\\&quot;Arial\\&quot;\" color=\"#009000\"><b><small><font face=\"\\&quot;Arial\\&quot;\" color=\"#009000\" size=\"\\&quot;-1\\&quot;\"><small>/&nbsp; </small>\r\n</font>\r\n<span lang=\"\\&quot;EN-US\\&quot;\"><small><a href=\"\\&quot;http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/0781806534/bohemicacom0d\\&quot;\"><font face=\"\\&quot;Arial\\&quot;\" color=\"#009000\"><small>Buy from Amazon.co.uk</small>\r\n</font>\r\n</a>\r\n</small>\r\n</span>\r\n</small>\r\n</b>\r\n</font>\r\n <p class=\"\\&quot;TableSmall\\&quot;\"><b><a href=\"\\&quot;http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0870529811/bohemicacom\\&quot;\">Czech-English/English-Czech Concise Dictionary</a>\r\n<br />\r\n</b>\r\n<font color=\"#080000\">by Nina Trnka </font>\r\nThe only dictionary published in the US, designed specifically for non-native speakers. It is the only dictionary to give phonetic transcriptions of Czech words. Its main limitation is the vocabulary range. While potentially useful for complete beginners, it will not be enough for serious learners.<small><a href=\"\\&quot;http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0870529811/bohemicacom\\&quot;\"><font face=\"\\&quot;Arial\\&quot;\" color=\"#009000\"><b><small><br />\r\nBuy from Amazon.com</small>\r\n</b>\r\n</font>\r\n</a>\r\n</small>\r\n<font face=\"\\&quot;Arial\\&quot;\" color=\"#009000\"><b><small> <font face=\"\\&quot;Arial\\&quot;\" color=\"#009000\" size=\"\\&quot;-1\\&quot;\"><small>/&nbsp; </small>\r\n</font>\r\n<span lang=\"\\&quot;EN-US\\&quot;\"><small><a href=\"\\&quot;http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/0870529811/bohemicacom0d\\&quot;\"><font face=\"\\&quot;Arial\\&quot;\" color=\"#009000\"><small>Buy from Amazon.co.uk</small>\r\n</font>\r\n</a>\r\n</small>\r\n</span>\r\n</small>\r\n</b>\r\n</font>\r\n</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"\\&quot;top\\&quot;\" width=\"\\&quot;30%\\&quot;\"><b><a href=\"\\&quot;http://www.ectaco.com/cgi-bin/url.pl?refid=763\\&quot;\">Etaco Electronic Pocket Dictionaries and Translators</a>\r\n</b>\r\n <p><a href=\"\\&quot;http://www.ectaco.com/cgi-bin/url.pl?refid=763\\&quot;\"><img alt=\"\\&quot;Language\" src=\"\\&quot;http://www.ectaco.com/cgi-bin/banner.pl?size=100x100&refid=763\\&quot;\" talking=\"\" pocket=\"\" electronic=\"\" />\r\n</a>\r\n </p>\r\n<p>I\\\'ve decided to present these on Bohemica.com. As with all, all-purpose dictionary, it has its limitations but having tried their web-based dictionary, I believe that it can be used by learners. The only grammatical information is on parts of speech, but that is better than most. By buying one of these dictionaries through this <a href=\"\\&quot;http://www.ectaco.com/cgi-bin/url.pl?refid=763\\&quot;\">link</a>\r\n, you will support Bohemica.com.</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p><strong>New Czech Grammar by James Naughton:<br />\r\n</strong>\r\n<a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/0415287847/qid=1113526626/sr=8-5/ref=sr_8_xs_ap_i5_xgl/202-8700201-7118246\">http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/0415287847/qid=1113526626/sr=8-5/ref=sr_8_xs_ap_i5_xgl/202-8700201-7118246</a>\r\n<br />\r\n<br />\r\n<a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/tg/detail/-/0415287847/qid=1113526742/sr=8-12/ref=sr_8_xs_ap_i11_xgl14/102-5008598-3051365?v=glance&s=books&n=507846\">http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/tg/detail/-/0415287847/qid=1113526742/sr=8-12/ref=sr_8_xs_ap_i11_xgl14/102-5008598-3051365?v=glance&s=books&n=507846</a>\r\n<a href=\"\\&quot;http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0781807328/bohemicacom\\&quot;\"><b><br />\r\n<br />\r\nHippocrene Children\\\'s Illustrated Czech Dictionary : English-Czech/Czech-English<br />\r\n</b>\r\n<font color=\"#080000\">(</font>\r\n</a>\r\n<font color=\"#080000\">1999)</font>\r\n&nbsp; An interesting idea. I haven\\\'t seen it yet, though.<small><a href=\"\\&quot;http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0781807328/bohemicacom\\&quot;\"><font face=\"\\&quot;Arial\\&quot;\" color=\"#009000\"><b><small><br />\r\nBuy from Amazon.com</small>\r\n</b>\r\n</font>\r\n</a>\r\n </small>\r\n<font face=\"\\&quot;Arial\\&quot;\" color=\"#009000\"><b><small><font face=\"\\&quot;Arial\\&quot;\" color=\"#009000\" size=\"\\&quot;-1\\&quot;\"><small>/&nbsp; </small>\r\n</font>\r\n<span lang=\"\\&quot;EN-US\\&quot;\"><small><a href=\"\\&quot;http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/0781807328/bohemicacom0d\\&quot;\"><font face=\"\\&quot;Arial\\&quot;\" color=\"#009000\"><small>Buy from Amazon.co.uk</small>\r\n</font>\r\n</a>\r\n</small>\r\n</span>\r\n</small>\r\n</b>\r\n</font>\r\n </p>\r\n<p><b><a href=\"\\&quot;http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0415047552/bohemicacom\\&quot;\">The Slavonic Languages (Routledge Language Family Descriptions)</a>\r\n<br />\r\n</b>\r\n<font color=\"#080000\">by Bernard Comrie, Greville G. Corbett (Editor). Hardcover (1993) </font>\r\nPricey at $160.00 but it contains the only respectable English language description of Czech grammar written by David Short.&nbsp; You get other Slavonic languages as well in the same book.<small><a href=\"\\&quot;http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0415047552/bohemicacom\\&quot;\"><font face=\"\\&quot;Arial\\&quot;\" color=\"#009000\"><b><small><br />\r\nBuy from Amazon.com</small>\r\n</b>\r\n</font>\r\n</a>\r\n</small>\r\n<font face=\"\\&quot;Arial\\&quot;\" color=\"#009000\"><b><small> <font face=\"\\&quot;Arial\\&quot;\" color=\"#009000\" size=\"\\&quot;-1\\&quot;\"><small>/&nbsp; </small>\r\n</font>\r\n<span lang=\"\\&quot;EN-US\\&quot;\"><small><a href=\"\\&quot;http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/0415047552/bohemicacom0d\\&quot;\"><font face=\"\\&quot;Arial\\&quot;\" color=\"#009000\"><small>Buy from Amazon.co.uk</small>\r\n</font>\r\n</a>\r\n</small>\r\n</span>\r\n</small>\r\n</b>\r\n</font>\r\n </p>\r\n<p><b><a href=\"\\&quot;http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0231099371/bohemicacom\\&quot;\">Modern Czech Grammar</a>\r\n</b>\r\n<font face=\"\\&quot;verdana,arial,helvetica\\&quot;\" size=\"\\&quot;-1\\&quot;\"><br />\r\n</font>\r\n<font color=\"#080000\">by William E. Harkins (1953) </font>\r\nOld traditional grammar of Czech. The only Czech grammar book available.<small><a href=\"\\&quot;http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0231099371/bohemicacom\\&quot;\"><font face=\"\\&quot;Arial\\&quot;\" color=\"#009000\"><b><small><br />\r\nBuy from Amazon.com</small>\r\n</b>\r\n</font>\r\n</a>\r\n</small>\r\n<font face=\"\\&quot;Arial\\&quot;\" color=\"#009000\"><b><small> <font face=\"\\&quot;Arial\\&quot;\" color=\"#009000\" size=\"\\&quot;-1\\&quot;\"><small>/&nbsp; </small>\r\n</font>\r\n<span lang=\"\\&quot;EN-US\\&quot;\"><small><a href=\"\\&quot;http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/0231099371/bohemicacom0d\\&quot;\"><font face=\"\\&quot;Arial\\&quot;\" color=\"#009000\">Buy from Amazon.co.uk</font>\r\n</a>\r\n</small>\r\n</span>\r\n</small>\r\n</b>\r\n</font>\r\n </p>\r\n<p class=\"\\&quot;TableSmall\\&quot;\"><b>Slovník spisovné četiny<br />\r\n</b>\r\n<font color=\"#080000\">by Filipec et al. (1994) </font>\r\nVery good reference work. Pretty much the only single-volume Czech-Czech dictionary. Gives you all the necessary grammatical information and more. Its entries often contain short examples. The downside: Everything is in Czech for Czechs. Also available on CD-ROM from <a href=\"\\&quot;http://www.leda.cz\\&quot;\">Leda</a>\r\n.</p>\r\n<p class=\"\\&quot;TableSmall\\&quot;\"><b>Anglicko - český slovník I.-IV.<br />\r\n</b>\r\n<font color=\"#080000\">by Hais, Hodek (1993-94)</font>\r\n The largest English-Czech dictionary available. Designed for Czech users with no regard to foreign learner. Recently also published in a two-volume revised edition. Available on CD-ROM from <a href=\"\\&quot;http://www.leda.cz\\&quot;\">Leda</a>\r\n which is a great thing for translators but at 10&nbsp;000 Kč pricey for mere mortals.</p>\r\n<p class=\"\\&quot;TableSmall\\&quot;\"><b>Anglicko-Český/Česko-Anglický Slovník<br />\r\n</b>\r\n<font color=\"#080000\">Kneovič et al (1993)</font>\r\n This is a dictionary for Czechs, therefore, while being the most comprehensive pocket dictionary available it has severe limitations in providing necessary grammatical information (gender, aspect). When using it the student has about a fifty percent chance of getting the right equivalent, and much less of being able to use it correctly.</p>\r\n<p class=\"\\&quot;MsoNormal\\&quot;\" style=\"&quot;MARGIN: \" 0px=\"\" 0px=\"\" 6pt=\"\"><b>Everything You Always Wanted to Know About Czech&nbsp;<br />\r\n</b>\r\n<font color=\"#080000\">by Karen von Kunes</font>\r\n</p>\r\n<p class=\"\\&quot;NormalFirst\\&quot;\" style=\"&quot;MARGIN: \" 0px=\"\" 0px=\"\" 0cm=\"\"><span lang=\"\\&quot;EN-US\\&quot;\">Collection of short essays about the Czech language published in the Prague Post. Cannot be used as a textbook but has much interesting information.</span>\r\n</p>\r\n<p class=\"\\&quot;NormalFirst\\&quot;\" style=\"&quot;MARGIN: \" 0px=\"\" 0px=\"\" 0cm=\"\"></p>\r\n<p class=\"\\&quot;NormalFirst\\&quot;\" style=\"&quot;MARGIN: \" 0px=\"\" 0px=\"\" 0cm=\"\"><span lang=\"\\&quot;EN-US\\&quot;\"><b>240 Ways of Looking at Czech </b>\r\n</span>\r\nis a collection of more essays by the same author.</p>\r\n<p align=\"\\&quot;left\\&quot;\"><a href=\"\\&quot;http://www.unforgettablelanguages.com/frames_a10.html\\&quot;\"><b>www.unforgettablelanguages.com/frames_a10.html</b>\r\n</a>\r\n<b>&nbsp;</b>\r\n<br />\r\nAlthough it brands itself a full language course, this is too ambitious. But it can be recommended as an interesting vocabulary building aid which may be very useful to some users. It introduces Czech words through associations with English words and phrases. No grammar is mentioned. Only a sample is free but a full course can be had for relatively little (under US$10).&nbsp; <br />\r\n<br />\r\n<a href=\"\\&quot;http://www.401czechverbs.com/\\&quot;\"><strong>http://www.401czechverbs.com</strong>\r\n</a>\r\n<br />\r\nWebsite accompanying the book entitled <strong>401 Czech Verbs</strong>\r\n. This book claims that: <em>This is the only book that provides information on the conjugation of over 1680 verbs. More importantly, this is the only book that provides a simple way to look up the prepositions and cases associated with these verbs. </em>\r\nI did not have the opportunity to examine the book myself but it sounds like an absolute must for any serious student of Czech as a foreign language.<br />\r\n</p>\r\n</td />\r\n</tr />\r\n</table />\r\n', 39, 0, 1);
INSERT INTO `xc_text` (`xct_id`, `xct_header`, `xct_text`, `xct_section`, `xct_type`, `xct_priority`) VALUES
(22, '', 'Only selected titles are available to purchase online. After you click on the title of the book you want, you will be taken to Amazon\'s site. <<A href=\"http://www.bohemica.com/bookstore.htm\">Back</A>>\r\n<P></P>\r\n<P style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0px 0px\"></P><A href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1851090118/bohemicacom\"><B>Czechoslovakia (World Bibliographical Series, Vol 68)</B><FONT face=verdana,arial,helvetica size=-1><BR></FONT></A><FONT color=#800000>by David Short (1986) </FONT>Excellent resource of references to works published on all aspects of Czechoslovakia up to 1986. Pricey but worth it to researchers.<SMALL><A href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1851090118/bohemicacom\"><FONT face=Arial color=#990000><B><SMALL><BR>Buy from Amazon.com</SMALL></B></FONT></A></SMALL><FONT face=Arial color=#990000><B><SMALL> <FONT face=Arial color=#990000 size=-1><SMALL>/ </SMALL></FONT><SPAN lang=EN-US><SMALL><A href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/1851090118/bohemicacom0d\"><FONT face=Arial color=#990000><SMALL>Buy from Amazon.co.uk</SMALL></FONT></A></SMALL></SPAN></SMALL></B></FONT> \r\n<P><B><A href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1851093044/bohemicacom\">Czech Republic</A></B><BR><FONT color=#800000>by Vlaďka Edmondson with David Short (1999)</FONT><FONT face=verdana,arial,helvetica size=2> </FONT>Excellent resource of references to works published on all aspects of Czechoslovakia up to 1986. Pricey but worth it to researchers.<SMALL><A href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1851093044/bohemicacom\"><FONT face=Arial color=#990000><B><SMALL><BR>Buy from Amazon.com</SMALL></B></FONT></A> </SMALL><FONT face=Arial color=#990000><B><SMALL><FONT face=Arial color=#990000 size=-1><SMALL>/ </SMALL></FONT><A href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/1851093044/bohemicacom0d\"><SPAN lang=EN-US><FONT face=Arial color=#990000><SMALL><SMALL>Buy from Amazon.co.uk</SMALL></SMALL></FONT></SPAN></A></SMALL></B></FONT> \r\n<P><B><A href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/186034075X/bohemicacom\">Customs and Ettiquette in the Czech Republic</A></B><B style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal\"><SPAN lang=CS style=\"mso-ansi-language: CS\"><BR></SPAN></B><FONT color=#800000>by David Short </FONT><SPAN lang=EN-US>Excellent introduction to Czech manners and habits. Friendly, pocket-sized books to get you started. Slightly dated in some practical matters. <A href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/186034075X/bohemicacom\"><FONT face=Arial color=#990000><B><BR><SMALL><SMALL>Buy from Amazon.com</SMALL></SMALL></B></FONT></A><FONT face=Arial color=#990000><B><SMALL> <FONT face=Arial color=#990000 size=-1><SMALL>/ </SMALL></FONT><SMALL><A href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/186034075X/bohemicacom0d\"><FONT face=Arial color=#990000><SMALL>Buy from Amazon.co.uk</SMALL></FONT></A></SMALL></SMALL></B></FONT></SPAN> \r\n<P><B><A href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0521431557/bohemicacom\">Bohemia in History</A></B><BR><FONT color=#800000>by Mikulas Teich (Editor) </FONT>Collection of essays on the history of Czech Lands from 9th century until 1989.<BR><SMALL><A href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0521431557/bohemicacom\"><FONT face=Arial color=#990000><B><SMALL>Buy from Amazon.com</SMALL></B></FONT></A></SMALL><FONT face=Arial color=#990000><B><SMALL> <FONT face=Arial color=#990000 size=-1><SMALL>/ </SMALL></FONT><SPAN lang=EN-US><SMALL><A href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/0521431557/bohemicacom0d\"><FONT face=Arial color=#990000><SMALL>Buy from Amazon.co.uk</SMALL></FONT></A></SMALL></SPAN></SMALL></B></FONT> \r\n<P><B><A href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1856100200/bohemicacom\">Old Czech Legends</A></B><FONT color=#800000><BR>by Alois Jirásek </FONT><SPAN lang=EN-US>Translation of a 19<SUP>th</SUP> century book of old Czech legends. Patently historically inaccurate but well known (if not actually read) by most Czechs.</SPAN> \r\n<P class=MsoNormal style=\"MARGIN: 0cm 0px 0px\"><SMALL><A href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1856100200/bohemicacom\"><FONT face=Arial color=#990000><B><SMALL>Buy from Amazon.com</SMALL></B></FONT></A></SMALL><FONT face=Arial color=#990000><B><SMALL> <FONT face=Arial color=#990000 size=-1><SMALL>/ </SMALL></FONT><SPAN lang=EN-US><SMALL><A href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/1856100200/bohemicacom0d\"><FONT face=Arial color=#990000><SMALL>Buy from Amazon.co.uk</SMALL></FONT></A></SMALL></SPAN></SMALL></B></FONT></P>\r\n<P class=MsoNormal style=\"MARGIN: 0cm 0px 0px\"></P>\r\n<TABLE width=\"100%\" border=0>\r\n<TBODY>\r\n<TR>\r\n<TD vAlign=top width=\"19%\"><FONT face=verdana,arial,helvetica size=-1><A href=\"http://images.amazon.com/images/P/0691057605.01.LZZZZZZZ.gif\"><IMG height=140 src=\"http://images.amazon.com/images/P/0691057605.01.MZZZZZZZ.gif\" width=107 border=1></A></FONT> </TD>\r\n<TD vAlign=top width=\"81%\">\r\n<P class=MsoNormal style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0px 0px\"><B><A href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0691057605/bohemicacom\">Coasts of Bohemia: A Czech History</A> <BR></B><FONT color=#800000>by Derek Sayer (1998) </FONT>- <SPAN lang=EN-US>Most recent original account of Czech history in English. Shows Czech history in the context of cultural events. Title a variation on famous Shakespeares sentence mistakenly attributing a coast to Bohemia.</SPAN></P>\r\n<P class=NormalFirst style=\"MARGIN: 0cm 0px 0px\"><SMALL><A href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0691057605/bohemicacom\"><FONT face=Arial color=#990000><B><SMALL>Buy from Amazon.com</SMALL></B></FONT></A></SMALL><FONT face=Arial color=#990000><B><SMALL> <FONT face=Arial color=#990000 size=-1><SMALL>/ </SMALL></FONT><SPAN lang=EN-US><SMALL><A href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/0691057605/bohemicacom0d\"><FONT face=Arial color=#990000><SMALL>Buy from Amazon.co.uk</SMALL></FONT></A></SMALL></SPAN></SMALL></B></FONT></P>\r\n<P class=NormalFirst style=\"MARGIN: 0cm 0px 0px\"></P>\r\n<P class=NormalFirst style=\"MARGIN: 0cm 0px 0px\">Also available in paperback.</P>\r\n<P class=NormalFirst style=\"MARGIN: 0cm 0px 0px\"><SMALL><A href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/069105052X/bohemicacom\"><FONT face=Arial color=#990000><B><SMALL>Buy from Amazon.com</SMALL></B></FONT></A></SMALL><FONT face=Arial color=#990000><B><SMALL> <FONT face=Arial color=#990000 size=-1><SMALL>/ </SMALL></FONT><SPAN lang=EN-US><SMALL><A href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/069105052X/bohemicacom0d\"><FONT face=Arial color=#990000><SMALL>Buy from Amazon.co.uk</SMALL></FONT></A></SMALL></SPAN></SMALL></B></FONT></P>\r\n<P class=NormalFirst style=\"MARGIN: 0cm 0px 0px\"></P></TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE>\r\n<TABLE width=\"100%\" border=0>\r\n<TBODY>\r\n<TR>\r\n<TD vAlign=top width=\"19%\"><A href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1558683038/bohemicacom\"><IMG height=150 alt=\"Culture Shock! Czech Republic\" src=\"http://www.bohemica.com/images/bookstore/cultureshock.jpg\" width=100 border=0></A></TD>\r\n<TD vAlign=top width=\"81%\">\r\n<P class=MsoNormal style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0px 0px\"><B><A href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1558683038/bohemicacom\">Culture Shock: Czech Republic</A> </B><BR><FONT color=#800000>by Tim Nollen </FONT>- <SPAN lang=EN-US>Part of well-known series. Provides much useful and accurate information. Sometimes the account is a little too one sided. Slightly dated in some practical matters, most notably housing. </SPAN></P>\r\n<P class=MsoNormal style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0px 0px\"></P>\r\n<P class=NormalFirst style=\"MARGIN: 0cm 0px 0px\"><SMALL><A href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1558683038/bohemicacom\"><FONT face=Arial color=#990000><B><SMALL>Buy from Amazon.com</SMALL></B></FONT></A></SMALL></P>\r\n<P></P></TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE>\r\n<TABLE width=\"100%\" border=0>\r\n<TBODY>\r\n<TR>\r\n<TD vAlign=top width=\"19%\"><A href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1572160101/bohemicacom\"><IMG height=156 alt=\"Czech Proverbs\" src=\"http://www.bohemica.com/images/bookstore/proverbs.jpg\" width=100 border=0></A></TD>\r\n<TD vAlign=top width=\"81%\"><A href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1572160101/bohemicacom\"><B>Czech Proverbs<BR></B></A><FONT color=#990033>by Joanne Asala (Editor) (1998) </FONT>Czechs love using proverbs. Many people claim that proverbs tell you much about a country\'s values and habits. \r\n<P><SMALL><A href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1572160101/bohemicacom\"><FONT face=Arial color=#990000><B><SMALL>Buy from Amazon.com</SMALL></B></FONT></A></SMALL></P></TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE>\r\n<TABLE width=\"100%\" border=0>\r\n<TBODY>\r\n<TR>\r\n<TD vAlign=top width=\"19%\"><A href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/068812593X/bohemicacom\"><IMG height=140 hspace=5 src=\"http://images.amazon.com/images/P/068812593X.01.MZZZZZZZ.gif\" width=103 align=left vspace=3 border=1></A> </TD>\r\n<TD vAlign=top width=\"81%\"><A href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/068812593X/bohemicacom\"><B>Favorite Fairy Tales Told in Czechoslovakia (Favorite Fairy Tales, Book 10)</B></A><FONT face=verdana,arial,helvetica size=-1><BR></FONT><FONT color=#800000>by Virginia Haviland, Anca Hariton (1995) </FONT>What better way into a nations heart and soul than through its fairytales.<BR>\r\n<P class=NormalFirst style=\"MARGIN: 0cm 0px 0px\"><SMALL><A href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/068812593X/bohemicacom\"><FONT face=Arial color=#990000><B><SMALL>Buy from Amazon.com</SMALL></B></FONT></A></SMALL><FONT face=Arial color=#990000><B><SMALL> <FONT face=Arial color=#990000 size=-1><SMALL>/ </SMALL></FONT><SPAN lang=EN-US><SMALL><A href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/068812593X/bohemicacom0d\"><FONT face=Arial color=#990000><SMALL>Buy from Amazon.co.uk</SMALL></FONT></A></SMALL></SPAN></SMALL></B></FONT></P></TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE>\r\n<P class=MsoNormal style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0px 0px\"><A href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/8085890976/bohemicacom0d\"><B>Czechs and Balances: Nations Survival Kit </B></A><B style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal\"><A href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/8085890976/bohemicacom0d\"><SPAN lang=EN-US><BR></SPAN></A></B><FONT color=#800000>by Benjamin Kuras</FONT></P>\r\n<P class=NormalFirst style=\"MARGIN: 0cm 0px 0px\"><SPAN lang=EN-US>Witty and well-informed if somewhat insensitive account of Czech character from a historical perspective. Written by a British journalist living and writing in the Czech Republic. <SMALL><A href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/8085890976/bohemicacom\"><FONT face=Arial color=#990000><B><SMALL>Buy from Amazon.com</SMALL></B></FONT></A></SMALL><FONT face=Arial color=#990000><B><SMALL> <FONT face=Arial color=#990000 size=-1><SMALL>/ </SMALL></FONT><SMALL><SMALL>Not at Amazon.co.uk</SMALL></SMALL></SMALL></B></FONT></SPAN></P>\r\n<P class=MsoNormal style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0px 0px\"><B><A href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0864426240/bohemicacom\">Lonely Planet Prague<BR></A></B><FONT color=#800000>by John King, Richard Nebesky (1999)</FONT> - <SPAN lang=EN-US>A very accurate guide for short stays in Prague. Part of well known series.<FONT face=verdana,arial,helvetica size=-1> </FONT></SPAN></P>\r\n<P class=NormalFirst style=\"MARGIN: 0cm 0px 0px\"><SMALL><A href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0864426240/bohemicacom\"><FONT face=Arial color=#990000><B><SMALL>Buy from Amazon.com</SMALL></B></FONT></A></SMALL><FONT face=Arial color=#990000><B><SMALL> <FONT face=Arial color=#990000 size=-1><SMALL>/ </SMALL></FONT><SPAN lang=EN-US><SMALL><A href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/0864426240/bohemicacom0d\"><FONT face=Arial color=#990000><SMALL>Buy from Amazon.co.uk</SMALL></FONT></A></SMALL></SPAN></SMALL></B></FONT></P>\r\n<P class=NormalFirst style=\"MARGIN: 0cm 0px 0px\"></P>\r\n<TABLE width=\"100%\" border=0>\r\n<TBODY>\r\n<TR>\r\n<TD vAlign=top width=\"19%\"><FONT face=\"geneva, arial, helvetica\" size=-1><A href=\"http://images.amazon.com/images/P/8023827499.02.LZZZZZZZ.gif\"><IMG height=140 src=\"http://images.amazon.com/images/P/8023827499.02.MZZZZZZZ.gif\" width=95 border=1></A></FONT></TD>\r\n<TD vAlign=top width=\"81%\">\r\n<P class=MsoNormal style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0px 0px\"><A href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/8023827499/bohemicacom0d\"><B>For the Love of Prague</B></A><B style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal\"><I style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal\"><SPAN lang=EN-US> </SPAN></I><SPAN lang=EN-US><BR></SPAN></B><FONT color=#800000>by Gene Deitch (1998)</FONT></P>\r\n<P class=NormalFirst style=\"MARGIN: 0cm 0px 0px\"><SPAN lang=EN-US>Written by an American cartoon film director whos lived in the Czech Republic for forty years. Describes his personal relationships and impressions.</SPAN></P><FONT face=Arial color=#990000><B><SMALL><SPAN lang=EN-US><SMALL><A href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/8023827499/bohemicacom0d\"><FONT face=Arial color=#990000><SMALL>Buy from Amazon.co.uk</SMALL></FONT></A></SMALL></SPAN></SMALL></B></FONT> \r\n<P class=NormalFirst style=\"MARGIN: 0cm 0px 0px\"><SPAN lang=EN-US><A href=\"http://www.fortheloveofprague.com/\">http://www.fortheloveofprague.com</A></SPAN></P>\r\n<P class=NormalFirst style=\"MARGIN: 0cm 0px 0px\"></P></TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE>\r\n<TABLE width=\"100%\" border=0>\r\n<TBODY>\r\n<TR>\r\n<TD vAlign=top width=\"19%\"><A href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0517505479/bohemicacom\"><IMG height=151 alt=\"Czechoslovak Cookbook\" src=\"http://www.bohemica.com/images/bookstore/czecookbook.jpg\" width=100 border=0></A></TD>\r\n<TD vAlign=top width=\"81%\"><A href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0517505479/bohemicacom\"><B>Czechoslovak Cookbook</B></A> <BR><FONT color=#800000>by Joa Břízová et al.</FONT> <SPAN lang=EN-US>Title says it all. For those who like Czech food and wish to inflict it upon themselves.</SPAN> \r\n<P><SMALL><A href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0517505479/bohemicacom\"><FONT face=Arial color=#990000><B><SMALL>Buy from Amazon.com</SMALL></B></FONT></A></SMALL><FONT face=Arial color=#990000><B><SMALL> <FONT face=Arial color=#990000 size=-1><SMALL>/ </SMALL></FONT><SPAN lang=EN-US><SMALL><A href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/0517505479/bohemicacom0d\"><FONT face=Arial color=#990000><SMALL>Buy from Amazon.co.uk</SMALL></FONT></A></SMALL></SPAN></SMALL></B></FONT></P></TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE>\r\n<TABLE width=\"100%\" border=0>\r\n<TBODY>\r\n<TR>\r\n<TD vAlign=top width=\"19%\"><A href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0781804922/bohemicacom\"><IMG height=159 alt=\"The Best of Czech Cooking\" src=\"http://www.bohemica.com/images/bookstore/bestcooking.jpg\" width=100 border=0></A></TD>\r\n<TD vAlign=top width=\"81%\">\r\n<P><A href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0781804922/bohemicacom\"><B>The Best of Czech Cooking</B></A><B> </B><BR><FONT color=#800000>by Peter Trnka </FONT>Another cookbook to look into.</P>\r\n<P class=MsoNormal style=\"MARGIN: 0cm 0px 0px\"><SMALL><A href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0781804922/bohemicacom\"><FONT face=Arial color=#990000><B><SMALL>Buy from Amazon.com</SMALL></B></FONT></A></SMALL><FONT face=Arial color=#990000><B><SMALL> <FONT face=Arial color=#990000 size=-1><SMALL>/ </SMALL></FONT><SPAN lang=EN-US><SMALL><A href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/0781804922/bohemicacom0d\"><FONT face=Arial color=#990000><SMALL>Buy from Amazon.co.uk</SMALL></FONT></A></SMALL></SPAN></SMALL></B></FONT></P></TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE>\r\n<P class=MsoNormal style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0px 0px\"><FONT face=Verdana><SPAN class=small><FONT size=2> </FONT></FONT><FONT face=Verdana><FONT size=2> </FONT></SPAN></FONT><BR><STRONG><A href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1553696182/bohemicacom\">A Bohemian Odyssey</A><BR></STRONG><FONT color=#800000><STRONG>by Craig Mracek </STRONG></FONT><FONT color=#000000>Stories by an American finding his way around the Czech town of Pardubice in the early 1990s.</FONT><BR><SMALL><A href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1553696182/bohemicacom\"><FONT face=Arial color=#990000><SMALL><STRONG>Buy from Amazon.com</STRONG></SMALL></FONT></A></SMALL><STRONG><FONT face=Arial color=#990000><SMALL> <FONT face=Arial color=#990000 size=-1><SMALL>/ </SMALL></FONT><SPAN lang=EN-US><SMALL><A href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/1553696182/bohemicacom0d\"><FONT face=Arial color=#990000><SMALL>Buy from Amazon.co.uk</SMALL></FONT></A></SMALL></SPAN></SMALL></FONT> </STRONG></P>\r\n<P class=MsoNormal style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0px 0px\"><STRONG></STRONG> </P>\r\n<P class=MsoNormal style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0px 0px\"><B><A href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/0851157874/bohemicacom0d\">Art and Propaganda: Charles IV of Bohemia, 1346-1378</A></B><BR><FONT color=#800000>by Iva Rosario </FONT>This is the first study in English to look at the phenomenon of Charles\'s early use of the arts to consolidate his power. It focuses particularly on some thirty portraits of Charles IV, to demonstrate how and why the court harnessed the visual arts to legitimise, glorify and sacralise the great medieval ruler. By placing each portrait in its historical context, the author gives a fascinating insight into the art of political propaganda in an important European court of the middle ages. </P>\r\n<P class=MsoNormal style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0px 0px\"></P>\r\n<P class=MsoNormal style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0px 0px\"><B>Everything You Always Wanted to Know About Czech <BR></B><FONT color=#800000>by Karen von Kunes </FONT><SPAN lang=EN-US>Collection of short essays about the Czech language published in the Prague Post. Cannot be used as a textbook but has much interesting information.</SPAN></P>\r\n<P class=NormalFirst style=\"MARGIN: 0cm 0px 0px\"></P>\r\n<P class=NormalFirst style=\"MARGIN: 0cm 0px 0px\"><SPAN lang=EN-US><B>240 Ways of Looking at Czech </B></SPAN>is a collection of more essays.</P>\r\n<P class=NormalFirst style=\"MARGIN: 0cm 0px 0px\"></P>\r\n<P class=MsoNormal style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0px 0px\"><B>Bridging the Gap <BR></B><FONT color=#800000>by Grace Hammot and Anna Nováková</FONT> <SPAN lang=EN-US>One of the first, if not the first, books on Czech culture and life from an expatriate perspective. It is out of print but well worth reading if you can find it.</SPAN></P>\r\n<P class=MsoNormal style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0px 0px\"><B>An Outline of Czech History </B><SPAN lang=EN-US><B style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal\"><BR></B></SPAN><FONT color=#800000>by Petr Čornej </FONT>- <SPAN lang=EN-US>Brief, objective and fairly comprehensive booklet written by a leading Czech historian. Available also in other languages.</SPAN></P>\r\n<P class=MsoNormal style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0px 0px\"><B>Czech Republic Business Guide</B></P>\r\n<P class=MsoNormal style=\"MARGIN: 0cm 0px 0px\"><SPAN lang=EN-US>Collection of practical advise for all expatriates with relevant listings in many categories. Published annually.</SPAN></P>\r\n<P class=MsoNormal style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0px 0px\"><B>EveryDay Prague</B></P>\r\n<P class=MsoNormal style=\"MARGIN: 0cm 0px 0px\"><SPAN lang=EN-US>Listings of services in various categories. Comes with a useful discount card.</SPAN></P>\r\n<P class=MsoNormal style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0px 0px\"><B>Prague PhoneBook</B></P>\r\n<P class=NormalFirst style=\"MARGIN: 0cm 0px 0px\"><SPAN lang=EN-US>Expat oriented phonebook and yellow pages.</SPAN></P>\r\n<P align=left></P></TD></TR></TABLE>', 38, 0, 1),
(165, '', '<h2>Pondělí</h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Review of dative (determining the indirect object)\r\n<li>Strong and weak forms of personal pronouns\r\n</ul>', 253, 0, 100),
(166, '', '<B><FONT face=Arial size=4>\r\n<P align=justify>Úkoly</P>\r\n<UL></B></FONT><FONT face=\"Times New Roman\" size=3>\r\n<P align=justify>\r\n<LI>Najděte slova a výrazy, které vyjadřují odsouzení.</LI></UL>\r\n\r\n<UL>\r\n<LI><FONT face=\"Times New Roman\" size=3>Jaký je postoj autora ke kvalitě slueb v Čechách?</FONT></LI>\r\n<LI><FONT face=\"Times New Roman\" size=3>S čím sluby v Čechách srovnává?</LI>\r\n<LI></FONT><FONT size=3>Souhlasíte s autorovou analýzou?</FONT></LI>\r\n<LI><FONT face=\"Times New Roman\" size=3>Stalo se něco podobného vám (v Čechách nebo jinde)? Popite, co se stalo a řekněte proč.</FONT></LI>\r\n<LI><FONT face=\"Times New Roman\" size=3>Odpovězte na autorovu otázku v posledním odstavci? Shrňte pro a proti.</LI>\r\n<P></P></UL></FONT>', 256, 0, 10);
INSERT INTO `xc_text` (`xct_id`, `xct_header`, `xct_text`, `xct_section`, `xct_type`, `xct_priority`) VALUES
(23, '', 'This\r\n      section doesn\'t provide an exhaustive list. It is rather a <b>must-read\r\n      Top 5-10 of Czech literature</b>. All the books are available to purchase\r\n      through Amazon bookstores. </p>\r\n       \r\n      <h1><font color=\"#990033\"><a name=\"Top 5 Czech Authors\">Top 5 Czech Authors</a></font></h1>\r\n      <p>[Top 5 Czech Authors][<a href=\"#Other books of interest\">Other Books of\r\n      Interest</a>]<br>\r\n      [<a href=\"#Czech Poetry\">Czech Poetry</a>][<a href=\"#About Czech Literature\">About\r\n      Czech Literature</a>]</p>\r\n      <font face=\"geneva, arial, helvetica\" size=\"-1\"><table border=\"0\" cellPadding=\"3\" cellSpacing=\"0\" width=\"100%\">\r\n        <tbody>\r\n          <tr vAlign=\"top\">\r\n            <td><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0140182748/bohemicacom\"><img border=\"1\" src=\"http://images.amazon.com/images/P/0140182748.01.MZZZZZZZ.jpg\" width=\"88\" height=\"140\"></a></td>\r\n            <td>\r\n              <p></font>\r\n              <b><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0140182748/bohemicacom\">The\r\n      Good Soldier vejk and His Fortunes in the World War</a><br>\r\n              </b><font color=\"#990033\">by Jaroslav Haek, Josef\r\n      Lada (Illustrator), Cecil\r\n      Parrott (Translator) </font></p>\r\n              <p>Most popular humorous novel\r\n          from the First World War considered by many to be a reflection of the\r\n              Czech attitude to authority and Czech national character in\r\n              general.</p>\r\n              <p><font face=\"geneva, arial, helvetica\" size=\"-1\"> <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0140182748/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small>Buy\r\n          from Amazon.com</small></b></font></a><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small>\r\n          <font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\"><small>/  </small></font><span lang=\"EN-US\"><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/0140182748/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy\r\n          from Amazon.co.uk<br>\r\n          </small></font></a></small></span></small></b></font></p>\r\n            </font></td>\r\n          </tr>\r\n          <tr vAlign=\"top\">\r\n            <td><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0945774109/bohemicacom\"><img border=\"1\" hspace=\"5\" src=\"http://images.amazon.com/images/P/0945774109.01.MZZZZZZZ.gif\" vspace=\"3\" width=\"90\" height=\"140\"></a></td>\r\n            <td>\r\n            \r\n            <b><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0192810103/bohemicacom\">R.\r\n          U. R. and the Insect Play</b></a><b> <br>\r\n              </b><font color=\"#990033\"> by Karel Čapek (1961) (Insect Play\r\n              co-written with brother Josef Čapek)</font> RUR is a science-fiction play from the 1930s which\r\n          introduced the word <i>robot</i> into world\'s languages.\r\n              <p><small><small><small><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0192810103/bohemicacom\"><b><small><font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\" color=\"#990033\">Buy\r\n          from Amazon.com</font></small></b></a></small></small></small></small><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\"><b><small>\r\n          <small>/  </small><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/0192810103/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy\r\n          from Amazon.co.uk</small></font></a></small></font></span></small></b></font> </p>\r\n              <p><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0945774109/bohemicacom\"><b>War\r\n          With the Newts<br>\r\n              </b></a><font color=\"#990000\">(1990)</font></p>\r\n              <p><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0945774109/bohemicacom\"><b><small><font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\" color=\"#990033\">Buy\r\n          from Amazon.com</font></small></b></a></small><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\"><b><small>\r\n          <small>/  </small><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/0945774109/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy\r\n          from Amazon.co.uk<br>\r\n          </small></font></a></small></font></span></small></b></font> </td>\r\n          </tr>\r\n          <tr vAlign=\"top\">\r\n            <td><a href=\"http://images.amazon.com/images/P/0060932139.01.LZZZZZZZ.gif\"><img border=\"1\" hspace=\"5\" src=\"http://images.amazon.com/images/P/0060932139.01.MZZZZZZZ.gif\" vspace=\"3\" width=\"92\" height=\"140\"></a>\r\n            </td>\r\n            <td><b><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0060932139/bohemicacom\">The Unbearable Lightness of\r\n      Being (Perennial Classics)</a></b><font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\" size=\"-1\"><br>\r\n              </font><font color=\"#990033\">\r\n      by Milan\r\n      Kundera, Michael\r\n      Henry Heim (Translator) </font>Popular\r\n          novel by the internationally best-known Czech novelist currently\r\n          living in France.\r\n              <p><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0060932139/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small>Buy\r\n      from Amazon.com</small></b></font></a></small><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small>\r\n      <font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\"><small>/  </small></font><span lang=\"EN-US\"><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/0060932139/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy\r\n      from Amazon.co.uk</small></font></a></small></span></small></b></font></p>\r\n              <p>Other books by Kundera to buy at Amazon: <font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\" size=\"-1\"><b><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0060932147/bohemicacomhttp://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0060932147/bohemicacomhttp://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0060932147/bohemicacom\">The\r\n          Book of Laughter and Forgetting (Perennial Classics)</a>, <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0060930314/bohemicacom\">Identity</a>,\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0060932384/bohemicacom\">Immortality</a>,<br>\r\n           <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0060912227/bohemicacom\">Jacques\r\n          and His Master : An Homage to Diderot in Three Acts</a>, <br>\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/006099505X/bohemicacom\">The\r\n          Joke (Definitive Version)</a>, <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0060997036/bohemicacom\">Laughable\r\n          Loves</a>, <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0060997028/bohemicacom\">Life\r\n          Is Elsewhere<br>\r\n              </a>\r\n          </b></font>\r\n            </td>\r\n          </tr>\r\n          <tr vAlign=\"top\">\r\n            <td><img border=\"1\" src=\"http://images.amazon.com/images/P/0679727868.01.MZZZZZZZ.gif\" width=\"89\" height=\"140\"></td>\r\n            <td><b><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0679727868/bohemicacom\">I Served the King of\r\n      England<br>\r\n              </a></b><font color=\"#990033\">\r\n      by Bohumil\r\n      Hrabal</font>\r\n              <p>A short novel by a\r\n          popular recently deceased Czech novelist.</p>\r\n      <p><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0679727868/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small>Buy\r\n      from Amazon.com</small></b></font></a></small><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small>\r\n      <font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\"><small>/  </small></font><span lang=\"EN-US\"><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/0679727868/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy\r\n      from Amazon.co.uk</small></font></a></small></span></small></b></font></p>\r\n            </td>\r\n          </tr>\r\n          <tr vAlign=\"top\">\r\n            <td><font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\" size=\"-1\"><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0679727868/bohemicacom\"><img border=\"1\" hspace=\"5\" src=\"http://images.amazon.com/images/P/0810112787.01.MZZZZZZZ.gif\" vspace=\"3\" width=\"92\" height=\"140\"></a></font></td>\r\n            <td>\r\n          <p style=\"margin-left: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-top: 6.0pt; margin-bottom: 0\"><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0679727868/bohemicacom\"><b>Closely\r\n          Watched Trains (European Classics)</b></a>\r\n          <p style=\"margin-left: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-top: 6.0pt; margin-bottom: 0\">Another\r\n          novel by Hrabal which served as an inspiration to a 1968 Oscar winning\r\n          film. <small> <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0679727868/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small>Buy\r\n      from Amazon.com</small></b></font></a></small><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small>\r\n      <font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\"><small>/  </small></font><span lang=\"EN-US\"><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/0679727868/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy\r\n      from Amazon.co.uk</small></font></a></small></span></small></b></font>\r\n      <p><b><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0151238103/bohemicacom\">Dancing Lessons for the\r\n      Advanced in Age : A Novel</a><br>\r\n      </b><font color=\"#990033\">\r\n      by Bohumil\r\n      Hrabal </font><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0151238103/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small>Buy\r\n      from Amazon.com</small></b></font></a></small><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small>\r\n      <font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\"><small>/  </small></font><span lang=\"EN-US\"><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/0151238103/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy\r\n      from Amazon.co.uk</small></font></a></small></span></small></b></font></p>\r\n              <p> </td>\r\n          </tr>\r\n          <tr vAlign=\"top\">\r\n            <td><a href=\"http://images.amazon.com/images/P/1564781992.01.LZZZZZZZ.gif\"><img border=\"1\" hspace=\"5\" src=\"http://images.amazon.com/images/P/1564781992.01.MZZZZZZZ.gif\" vspace=\"3\" width=\"92\" height=\"140\"></a></td>\r\n            <td><p style=\"margin-left: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-top: 6.0pt; margin-bottom: 0\"><b><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/091294675X/bohemicacom\">The Cowards</a> <br>\r\n      </b><font color=\"#990033\">by Josef\r\n          kvorecký</font><b> </b>Novel describing situation in\r\n          post-war Czechoslovakia by a popular Czech novelist currently living\r\n          in Canada. <b><font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\" size=\"-1\"><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/091294675X/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy\r\n          from Amazon.com</small></font></a>\r\n          </font> <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1564781992/o/qid=956267741/sr=2-2/002-9889902-6280218\"> <font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\"><small>/ \r\n              </small></font></a><font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\" size=\"-1\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><small><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/091294675X/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy\r\n          from Amazon.co.uk</small></font></a></font></small></span> </font>\r\n          </b> <p style=\"margin-left: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-top: 6.0pt; margin-bottom: 0\">Another\r\n      popular book by kvorecký is <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1564781992/bohemicacom\"><b>The\r\n          Engineer of Human Souls</b></a><b><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1564781992/bohemicacom\">:</a>\r\n              </b><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1564781992/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small>Buy\r\n      from Amazon.com</small></b></font></a></small><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small>\r\n      <font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\"><small>/  </small></font><span lang=\"EN-US\"><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/1564781992/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy\r\n      from Amazon.co.uk</small></font></a></small></span></small></b></font>\r\n            </td>\r\n          </tr>\r\n        </tbody>\r\n      </table>\r\n      <h1><font color=\"#990033\"><a name=\"Other books of interest\">Other Books of\r\n      Interest</a></font></h1>\r\n      <p>[<a href=\"#Top 5 Czech Authors\">Top 5 Czech Authors</a>][Other Books of\r\n      Interest]<br>\r\n      [<a href=\"#Czech Poetry\">Czech Poetry</a>][<a href=\"#About Czech Literature\">About\r\n      Czech Literature</a>]</p>\r\n      <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0945774265/bohemicacom\"><b>Talks With\r\n      T.G. Masaryk</b></a><font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\" size=\"-1\"><br>\r\n      </font><font color=\"#990033\">\r\n      by T.\r\n      G. Masaryk, Karel Čapek </font>Autobiography of the first president of\r\n      Czechoslovakia compiled by Karel Čapek also translated into English\r\n      as  <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0405027397/bohemicacom\"><b>President\r\n      Masaryk Tells His Story</b></a><b>.</b><br>\r\n      <font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\" size=\"-1\"><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0945774265/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small>Buy\r\n      from Amazon.com</small></b></font></a>\r\n      </font><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\"><b><small> <small>/ \r\n      </small><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/0945774265/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy\r\n      from Amazon.co.uk</small></font></a></small></font></span></small></b></font>\r\n      <p><b><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0465037194/bohemicacom\">Václav\r\n      Havel : A Political Tragedy in Six Acts</a><br>\r\n      </b><font color=\"#990033\">\r\n      by John Keane (2000) </font>A controversial account of the political\r\n      development of the Czech President.<font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\" size=\"-1\"><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0465037194/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small><br>\r\n      Buy\r\n      from Amazon.com</small></b></font></a></font>\r\n      <font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\"><b><small> <small>/  </small><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/0465037194/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy\r\n      from Amazon.co.uk</small></font></a></small></font></span></small></b></font>\r\n      <p> <table border=\"0\" cellPadding=\"3\" cellSpacing=\"0\" width=\"600\" height=\"154\">\r\n        <tbody>\r\n          <tr vAlign=\"top\">\r\n            <td width=\"119\" height=\"148\"><b><a href=\"http://images.amazon.com/images/P/0679744975.01.LZZZZZZZ.gif\"><img border=\"1\" src=\"http://images.amazon.com/images/P/0679744975.01.MZZZZZZZ.gif\" width=\"90\" height=\"140\"></a></b></td>\r\n            <td width=\"465\" height=\"148\">\r\n      <p><b><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0679744975/bohemicacom\"><br>\r\n      Summer\r\n      Meditations</a> </b><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0679744975/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small><b><font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\" size=\"-1\"><br>\r\n      </font>\r\n      </b></small></font></a><font color=\"#990033\">by Václav Havel</font>\r\n      Political musings by the Czech president playwright and philosopher.<a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0679744975/bohemicacom\"><b><font color=\"#990033\"><font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\" size=\"-1\"><small><br>\r\n      Buy\r\n      from Amazon.com</small></font>\r\n      </font>\r\n      </b></a><b>\r\n      <font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\"><small> <small>/  </small><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/0679744975/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy\r\n      from Amazon.co.uk</small></font></a></small></font></span></small></font></b>\r\n            </td>\r\n          </tr>\r\n          <tr vAlign=\"top\">\r\n            <td width=\"119\" height=\"148\"><img border=\"1\" hspace=\"5\" src=\"http://images.amazon.com/images/P/1882577477.01.MZZZZZZZ.gif\" vspace=\"3\" width=\"90\" height=\"140\"></td>\r\n            <td width=\"465\" height=\"148\">\r\n      <p><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1882577477/bohemicacom\"><b><br>\r\n      Renaissance\r\n            : The Rebirth of Liberty in the Heart of Europe</b></a><br>\r\n      <font color=\"#990033\">\r\n            by Václav Klaus ( 1997) </font>Political and economic credo of the\r\n      former Czech Prime Minister, credited with designing a unique system of privatization\r\n      and not reforming the legal system to go with it.<br>\r\n      <font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\" size=\"-1\"><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1882577477/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small>Buy\r\n            from Amazon.com</small></b></font></a>\r\n            </font><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\"><b><small> <small>/ \r\n      </small><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/1882577477/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy\r\n            from Amazon.co.uk</small></font></a></small></font></span></small></b></font>\r\n              </p>\r\n            </td>\r\n          </tr>\r\n        </tbody>\r\n      </table>\r\n      <p><b><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/080213307X/bohemicacom\">The Garden Party and Other\r\n      Plays</a><br>\r\n      </b><font color=\"#990033\">\r\n      by Václav\r\n      Havel </font>A collection of plays written by the Czech president in his\r\n      dissident playwright years. They are all written in the tradition of the\r\n      drama of the absurd.<br>\r\n      <small>\r\n      <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/080213307X/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small>Buy\r\n      from Amazon.com</small></b></font></a>\r\n      </small>\r\n      <font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small> <font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\"><small>/ \r\n      </small></font><span lang=\"EN-US\"><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/080213307X/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy\r\n      from Amazon.co.uk</small></font></a></small></span></small></b></font>\r\n      <p><b><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0945774176/qid=956269765/sr=1-1/002-9889902-6280218\">Catapult\r\n      : A Timetable of Rail, Sea, and Air Ways to Paradise</a><br>\r\n      </b><font color=\"#990033\">\r\n      by Vladimír Páral, William Harkins (Translator) (1993) </font>A book by\r\n      an author whose popularity was established in the 1970s and who came back\r\n      into the vogue after 1989.<small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0945774176/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small><br>\r\n      Buy\r\n      from Amazon.com</small></b></font></a></small><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small>\r\n      <font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\"><small>/  </small></font><span lang=\"EN-US\"><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/0945774176/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy\r\n      from Amazon.co.uk</small></font></a></small></span></small></b></font>\r\n      <p>Another  book by Páral is <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/094577415X/bohemicacom\"><b>The\r\n      Four Sonyas</b></a><b>. <br>\r\n </b><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/094577415X/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small>Buy\r\n      from Amazon.com</small></b></font></a></small><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small>\r\n      <font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\"><small>/  </small></font><span lang=\"EN-US\"><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/094577415X/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy\r\n      from Amazon.co.uk</small></font></a></small></span></small></b></font><p><b><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1856100200/bohemicacom\">Old\r\n              Czech Legends</a><br>\r\n      </b><font color=\"#990033\">\r\n              by Alois Jirásek </font>A classic from which many Czechs derive\r\n      their knowledge of Czech mythology and (incorrectly) Czech history. An\r\n      essential read for anybody trying to understand Czech values.<br>\r\n      <small>\r\n      <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1856100200/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small>Buy\r\n              from Amazon.com</small></b></font></a>\r\n      </small>\r\n              <font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small> <font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\"><small>/ \r\n              </small></font><span lang=\"EN-US\"><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/1856100200/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy\r\n              from Amazon.co.uk</small></font></a></small></span></small></b></font><p><b><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/078180714X/bohemicacom\">Czech,\r\n      Moravian and Slovak Fairy Tales (Library of Folklore)</a><br>\r\n      </b><font color=\"#990033\">\r\n      by Parker Fillmore, Jan Matulka (Illustrator) ( 1998)</font><font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\" size=\"-1\">\r\n      </font>\r\n      A collection of folk tales told to Czech children. Important for students\r\n      of Czech culture. <br>\r\n        <font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\" size=\"-1\"><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/078180714X/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small>Buy\r\n      from Amazon.com</small></b></font></a></font>\r\n      <font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\"><b><small> <small>/  </small><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/078180714X/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy\r\n      from Amazon.co.uk</small></font></a></small></font></span></small></b></font><p> <table border=\"0\" cellPadding=\"3\" cellSpacing=\"0\" width=\"600\" height=\"154\">\r\n        <tbody>\r\n          <tr vAlign=\"top\">\r\n            <td width=\"119\" height=\"148\"><a href=\"http://images.amazon.com/images/P/1887378057.01.LZZZZZZZ.gif\"><img border=\"1\" height=\"140\" hspace=\"5\" src=\"http://images.amazon.com/images/P/1887378057.01.MZZZZZZZ.gif\" vspace=\"3\" width=\"85\"></a>\r\n            </td>\r\n            <td width=\"465\" height=\"148\"><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1887378057/bohemicacom\"><b>Bringing\r\n      Up Girls in Bohemia</b></a><b><br>\r\n              </b><font color=\"#990033\">\r\n      by Michal Viewegh, A.G. Brain (Translator) ( 1996) </font>The most popular\r\n              Czech author of the 1990s. This book and another of his books <i>The\r\n              Wonderful Years That Sucked</i> were made into successful films.\r\n              <p><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1887378057/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small>Buy\r\n      from Amazon.com</small></b></font></a></small><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small>\r\n      <font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\"><small>/  </small></font><span lang=\"EN-US\"><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/1887378057/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy\r\n      from Amazon.co.uk</small></font></a></small></span></small></b></font>\r\n              <p> \r\n              <p> </td>\r\n          </tr>\r\n          <tr vAlign=\"top\">\r\n            <td width=\"119\" height=\"148\"><a href=\"http://images.amazon.com/images/P/0805211063.01.LZZZZZZZ.gif\"><img border=\"1\" hspace=\"5\" src=\"http://images.amazon.com/images/P/0805211063.01.MZZZZZZZ.gif\" vspace=\"3\" width=\"90\" height=\"140\"></a></td>\r\n            <td width=\"465\" height=\"148\">\r\n      <p>Another world-famous writer is closely associated with the Czech\r\n      Republic and most notably Prague. His name is <font color=\"#990033\"><b> Franz\r\n      Kafka</b></font>. He wrote all\r\n      his books in German, and although he spoke fluent Czech, he is not\r\n      typically considered to be a Czech writer. His three unfinished novels are\r\n      <i><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0805211063/bohemicacom\"><b>The\r\n      Castle</b></a>, <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0805210407/bohemicacom\"><b>The\r\n      Trial</b></a>, </i>and <i><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0805210644/bohemicacom\"><b>America</b></a></i>. He is also well-known\r\n      for his <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0805210555/bohemicacom\"> short\r\n      stories</a>. Most notably <i><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0553213695/bohemicacom\"><b>Metamorphosis</b></a></i>.\r\n      Other of his stories are worth a read as well and are available in English\r\n      in <b><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0805210555/bohemicacom\">The\r\n      Complete Stories</a>.</b>\r\n              <p> </td>\r\n          </tr>\r\n        </tbody>\r\n      </table><p><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/3631430442/bohemicacom\"><b>An\r\n      Anthology of Czech Literature (West Slavic Contributions)</b></a><b><br>\r\n      </b><font color=\"#990033\">\r\n      by Schamschula ( 1991) </font>A collection of Czech writing useful as a\r\n      sampler of essential reads.<small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/3631430442/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small><br>\r\n      <small>Buy\r\n      from Amazon.com</small></small></b></font></a>\r\n      </small><b>\r\n      <font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small><small>/  <span lang=\"EN-US\"><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/3631430442/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy\r\n      from Amazon.co.uk</small></font></a></small></span></small></small></font>\r\n      </b>\r\n      <h1><font color=\"#990033\"><a name=\"Czech Poetry\">Czech Poetry</a></font></h1>\r\n      <p>[<a href=\"#Top 5 Czech Authors\">Top 5 Czech Authors</a>][<a href=\"#Other books of interest\">Other\r\n      Books of Interest</a>]<br>\r\n      [Czech Poetry][<a href=\"#About Czech Literature\">About Czech Literature</a>]\r\n      <p>Czech poetry is much less translated and obviously much more difficult\r\n      to translate than fiction. Here are a few book available.\r\n      <p><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0140421300/bohemicacom\"><b>Three\r\n      Czech poets: Vítězslav Nezval</b></a><p>Nezval is arguably the greatest\r\n      Czech poet but his image has been tarnished by his association with with\r\n      the communist party. Well worth reading but much more enjoying in Czech. <small> <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0140421300/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small>Buy\r\n      from Amazon.com</small></b></font></a>\r\n      </small>\r\n      <p> \r\n      <p><b><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0262041707/bohemicacom\"></a><a href=\"http://images.amazon.com/images/P/0262041707.01.LZZZZZZZ.jpg\"><img align=\"left\" border=\"1\" hspace=\"5\" src=\"http://images.amazon.com/images/P/0262041707.01.MZZZZZZZ.jpg\" vspace=\"3\" width=\"128\" height=\"140\"></a>Karel\r\n      Teige: L\'Enfant Terrible of the Czech Modernist Avant-Garde<br>\r\n      </b><font color=\"#990033\">\r\n      by Rostislav Svacha, Eric Dluhosch (Editors) </font>The title says it all.\r\n      A well put-together book of the founder of Czech surrealism. \r\n      <p> <small> <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0262041707/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small>Buy\r\n      from Amazon.com</small></b></font></a>\r\n      </small>\r\n      <font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small> <font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\"><small>/ \r\n      </small></font><span lang=\"EN-US\"><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/0262041707/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy\r\n      from Amazon.co.uk</small></font></a></small></span></small></b></font>\r\n      <p><br>\r\n      </p>\r\n       <p>\r\n      <b><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/081011383X/bohemicacom\"></a><a href=\"http://images.amazon.com/images/P/0810113848.01.LZZZZZZZ.jpg\"><img align=\"left\" border=\"1\" height=\"140\" hspace=\"5\" src=\"http://images.amazon.com/images/P/0810113848.01.MZZZZZZZ.jpg\" vspace=\"3\" width=\"88\"></a>The\r\n              Early Poetry of Jaroslav Seifert : City in Tears, Sheer Love, On\r\n              the Waves of TSF, and the Nightingale Sings Poorly<br>\r\n      </b><font color=\"#990033\">\r\n              by Jaroslav Seifert, Dana Loewy (Translator) (<a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/081011383X/bohemicacom\">1997</a>/<a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0810113848/bohemicacom\">1999</a>) </font>Another\r\n      collection of the early collections of Seifert\'s poetry.\r\n      </p>\r\n      <p>  <font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\" size=\"-1\"><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/081011383X/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small>Buy\r\n              from Amazon.com</small></b></font></a>\r\n              </font><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\"><b><small> <small>/ \r\n      </small><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/081011383X/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy\r\n              from Amazon.co.uk</small></font></a></small></font></span></small></b></font>\r\n      </p>\r\n   \r\n   <p> </p>\r\n      <p> </p>\r\n      <p><b><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0945774397/qid=956270011/sr=1-4/002-9889902-6280218\">The\r\n              Poetry of Jaroslav Seifert</a><br>\r\n      </b><font color=\"#990033\">\r\n              by George Gibian(Editor), et al. (1998) </font>A collection of\r\n      papers about the poetry of Jaroslav Seifert. <font color=\"#990033\"> </font><small><b><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0945774397/bohemicacom\"><small><font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\" color=\"#990000\">Buy\r\n              from Amazon.com</font></small></a></b></small><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\"><b><small>\r\n              <small>/  </small><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/0945774397/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy\r\n              from Amazon.co.uk<br>\r\n              </small></font></a></small></font></span></small></b></font></p>\r\n      <h1><font color=\"#990033\"><a name=\"About Czech Literature\">About Czech\r\n      Literature</a></font></h1>\r\n      <p>[<a href=\"#Top 5 Czech Authors\">Top 5 Czech Authors</a>][<a href=\"#Other books of interest\">Other\r\n      Books of Interest</a>]<br>\r\n      [<a href=\"#Czech Poetry\">Czech Poetry</a>][About Czech Literature]<table border=\"0\" cellPadding=\"3\" cellSpacing=\"0\" width=\"600\" height=\"154\">\r\n        <tbody>\r\n          <tr vAlign=\"top\">\r\n            <td width=\"119\" height=\"148\"><font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\" size=\"-1\"> <a href=\"http://images.amazon.com/images/P/1883513014.01.LZZZZZZZ.gif\"><img border=\"1\" hspace=\"5\" src=\"http://images.amazon.com/images/P/1883513014.01.MZZZZZZZ.gif\" vspace=\"3\" width=\"96\" height=\"140\"></a></font>\r\n            </td>\r\n            <td width=\"465\" height=\"148\"><b><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1883513014/bohemicacom\">Prague\r\n      : A Traveler\'s Literary Companion (Travelers\' Literary Companions)</a><br>\r\n              </b><font color=\"#990033\">\r\n      by Paul Wilson(Editor) (1995) </font>An interesting way to tour Prague. It\r\n              certainly provides a new perspective on this city soaked in\r\n              literature.\r\n      <p><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1883513014/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small>Buy\r\n      from Amazon.com</small></b></font></a>\r\n      </small>\r\n      <font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small> <font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\"><small>/ \r\n      </small></font><span lang=\"EN-US\"><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/1883513014/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy\r\n      from Amazon.co.uk</small></font></a></small></span></small></b></font>\r\n      <p> </td>\r\n          </tr>\r\n        </tbody>\r\n      </table>\r\n          <p><font size=\"+1\"><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0485175193/bohemicacom\">Czech\r\n          Prose and Verse</a></font><nobr> <br>\r\n          </nobr><font color=\"#990033\">by Robert Pynsent (1979)</font> A\r\n          short but authoritative guide to Czech literature from a leading\r\n          British researcher. <small> <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0485175193/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small>Buy\r\n                  from Amazon.com</small></b></font></a></small><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small>\r\n                  <font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\"><small>/  </small></font><span lang=\"EN-US\"><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/0485175193/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy\r\n                  from Amazon.co.uk</small></font></a></small></span></small></b></font>\r\n          <p> <table border=\"0\" cellPadding=\"3\" cellSpacing=\"0\" width=\"600\" height=\"154\">\r\n        <tbody>\r\n          <tr vAlign=\"top\">\r\n            <td width=\"119\" height=\"148\"><a href=\"http://images.amazon.com/images/P/0801437172.01.LZZZZZZZ.jpg\"><img border=\"1\" hspace=\"5\" src=\"http://images.amazon.com/images/P/0801437172.01.MZZZZZZZ.jpg\" vspace=\"3\" width=\"99\" height=\"140\"></a></td>\r\n            <td width=\"465\" height=\"148\"><b><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0801437172/qid=956270256/sr=1-14/002-9889902-6280218\">The\r\n              Deserts of Bohemia : Czech Fiction and Its Social Context</a><br>\r\n      </b><font color=\"#990033\">\r\n              by Peter Steiner (2000) </font>A new monograph about Czech fiction\r\n              for those with some knowledge about Czech literature and history. \r\n              <p><small><b><small><small><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/XXXXXXXXX/bohemicacom\"><small><font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\" color=\"#990033\">Buy\r\n              from Amazon.com</font></small></a></small></small></small></b></small><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\"><b><small>\r\n              <small>/  </small><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/XXXXXXXX/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy\r\n              from Amazon.co.uk</small></font></a></small></font></span></small></b></font></td>\r\n          </tr>\r\n        </tbody>\r\n      </table>\r\n          <p> \r\n      <p> \r\n    </td>\r\n  </tr>\r\n</table>\r\n\r\n          <p><font size=\"+1\"><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1902210816/bohemicacom\">An Introduction to Twentieth-Century Czech Fiction: Comedies of Defiance\r\n</a></font><nobr> <br>\r\n          </nobr><font color=\"#990033\">by Robert Porter (2001)</font> Portraits of nine of 20th century\'s most important Czech authors. Provides an in-depth look at modern Czech fiction as a whole.<small> <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1902210816/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small>Buy\r\n                  from Amazon.com</small></b></font></a></small><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small>\r\n                  <font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\"><small>/  </small></font><span lang=\"EN-US\"><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/1902210816/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy\r\n                  from Amazon.co.uk</small></font></a></small></span></small></b></font>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n      </td>\r\n    </tr>\r\n  </table>\r\n<div align=\"center\">\r\n  <table border=\"0\" width=\"100%\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" height=\"20\" class=bottom1table>\r\n  <center>\r\n  </table>\r\n  </center>\r\n</div>', 37, 0, 1);
INSERT INTO `xc_text` (`xct_id`, `xct_header`, `xct_text`, `xct_section`, `xct_type`, `xct_priority`) VALUES
(24, '', '<table width=\"100%\" border=\"0\"><tbody><tr><td valign=\"top\" align=\"center\" width=\"50%\"><p align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0864426240/bohemicacom\"><b><font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\">Lonely Planet Prague (3rd Ed)<br />\r\n</font>\r\n</b>\r\n</a>\r\n<font color=\"#990033\">by John King, Richard Nebesky (1999)&nbsp;<br />\r\n</font>\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\">A very accurate guide for short stays in Prague. Part of well known series. <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1740593545/bohemicacom\">See here for 2003 edition. </a>\r\n</span>\r\n<br />\r\n<font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\" size=\"-1\"><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0864426240/bohemicacom\"><img height=\"140\" hspace=\"5\" src=\"http://images.amazon.com/images/P/0864426240.01.MZZZZZZZ.jpg\" width=\"92\" vspace=\"3\" border=\"1\" />\r\n <br />\r\n</a>\r\n</font>\r\n</p>\r\n<center><small><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0864426240/bohemicacom\"><b><font color=\"#990000\">Buy from Amazon.com</font>\r\n </b>\r\n</a>\r\n</small>\r\n<b><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small></small>\r\n</font>\r\n</b>\r\n</small>\r\n<b><small><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\">/&nbsp; </font>\r\n</small>\r\n</b>\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/0864426240/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy from Amazon.co.uk</small>\r\n </font>\r\n</a>\r\n</small>\r\n</b>\r\n</font>\r\n</span>\r\n</center>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" align=\"center\" width=\"50%\"><p align=\"center\">&nbsp; <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1864500123/bohemicacom\"><b><font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\">Lonely Planet Prague&nbsp;<br />\r\n(City Maps Series)</font>\r\n </b>\r\n</a>\r\n<font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\" size=\"-1\"><br />\r\n</font>\r\n<font color=\"#990033\">(1999)</font>\r\n </p>\r\n<p align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1864500123/bohemicacom\"><img height=\"140\" hspace=\"5\" src=\"http://images.amazon.com/images/P/1864500123.01.MZZZZZZZ.jpg\" width=\"58\" vspace=\"3\" border=\"1\" />\r\n </a>\r\n<font color=\"#990000\"><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1864500123/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small><small><br />\r\nBuy from Amazon.com</small>\r\n </small>\r\n</b>\r\n</font>\r\n</a>\r\n</font>\r\n<b><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small></small>\r\n</font>\r\n<small><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\">/&nbsp; </font>\r\n</small>\r\n</b>\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/1864500123/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy from Amazon.co.uk</small>\r\n </font>\r\n</a>\r\n</small>\r\n</b>\r\n</font>\r\n</span>\r\n</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr><td valign=\"top\" align=\"center\" width=\"50%\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" align=\"center\" width=\"50%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><b><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small><small>&nbsp;</small>\r\n </small>\r\n</font>\r\n</b>\r\n</span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr><td valign=\"top\" align=\"center\" width=\"50%\"><strong><font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\"><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1858283175/bohemicacom\">Rough Guide Czech and Slovak Republics (4th Edition)</a>\r\n </font>\r\n</strong>\r\n<font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\" size=\"-1\"><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1858283175/bohemicacom\"><br />\r\n</a>\r\n</font>\r\n<font color=\"#990033\">by Rob Humphreys, Tim Nollen (1998)</font>\r\n <p><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1858283175/bohemicacom\"><img height=\"158\" alt=\"Czech and Slovak Republics: The Rough Guide\" src=\"images/bookstore/roughczeslov.jpg\" width=\"100\" border=\"0\" />\r\n <br />\r\n</a>\r\n<font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\" size=\"-1\"><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1858283175/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small>Buy from Amazon.com</small>\r\n </b>\r\n</font>\r\n</a>\r\n</font>\r\n<font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\"><b><small>/&nbsp; </small>\r\n</b>\r\n</font>\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/1858283175/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy from Amazon.co.uk</small>\r\n </font>\r\n</a>\r\n</small>\r\n</b>\r\n</font>\r\n</span>\r\n</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" align=\"center\" width=\"50%\"><strong><font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\"><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0864425252/bohemicacom\">Lonely Planet Czech & Slovak Republics (2nd Ed)<br />\r\n</a>\r\n</font>\r\n</strong>\r\n<font color=\"#990033\">by Scott McNeely, Richard Nebesky, John King (1998)</font>\r\n <strong><font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\"><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0864425252/bohemicacom\"><br />\r\n</a>\r\n</font>\r\n</strong>\r\n<font color=\"#990033\"><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0864425252/bohemicacom\"><img height=\"140\" hspace=\"5\" src=\"http://images.amazon.com/images/P/0864425252.01.MZZZZZZZ.jpg\" width=\"92\" vspace=\"3\" border=\"1\" />\r\n <br />\r\n</a>\r\n</font>\r\n&nbsp;<small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0864425252/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small>Buy from Amazon.com</small>\r\n </b>\r\n</font>\r\n</a>\r\n</small>\r\n<font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small>&nbsp;</small>\r\n </b>\r\n</font>\r\n<font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\"><b><small>/&nbsp; </small>\r\n</b>\r\n</font>\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/0864425252/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy from Amazon.co.uk</small>\r\n </font>\r\n</a>\r\n</small>\r\n</b>\r\n</font>\r\n</span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr><td valign=\"top\" align=\"center\" width=\"50%\"><strong><font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\">&nbsp;</font>\r\n </strong>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" align=\"center\" width=\"50%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><b><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small><small>&nbsp;</small>\r\n </small>\r\n</font>\r\n</b>\r\n</span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr><td valign=\"top\" align=\"center\" width=\"50%\"><p align=\"center\"><strong><font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\"><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/067903000X/bohemicacom\">Fodor\'s the Czech Republic and Slovakia (3rd Ed)<br />\r\n</a>\r\n</font>\r\n</strong>\r\n<font color=\"#990033\">by Rebecca Miller, Matthew Lore (Editors)&nbsp;(1997)</font>\r\n </p>\r\n<center><br />\r\n&nbsp;</center>\r\n<font color=\"#990033\"><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/067903000X/bohemicacom\"><img height=\"140\" hspace=\"5\" src=\"http://images.amazon.com/images/P/067903000X.01.MZZZZZZZ.gif\" width=\"78\" vspace=\"3\" border=\"1\" />\r\n <br />\r\n</a>\r\n</font>\r\n<center><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/067903000X/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small>Buy from Amazon.com</small>\r\n </b>\r\n</font>\r\n</a>\r\n</small>\r\n<font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\"><b><small>/&nbsp; </small>\r\n</b>\r\n</font>\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/067903000X/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy from Amazon.co.uk</small>\r\n </font>\r\n</a>\r\n</small>\r\n</b>\r\n</font>\r\n</span>\r\n</center>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" align=\"center\" width=\"50%\"><p><strong><font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\"><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0312244614/bohemicacom\">Let\'s Go Eastern Europe 2000</a>\r\n </font>\r\n</strong>\r\n</p>\r\n<p><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0312244614/bohemicacom\"><img height=\"140\" alt=\"Let\'s Go Eastern Europe 2000\" hspace=\"3\" src=\"images/bookstore/letsgo2000.gif\" width=\"88\" vspace=\"3\" border=\"0\" />\r\n </a>\r\n</p>\r\n<font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\" size=\"-1\"><p><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0312244614/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small>Buy from Amazon.com</small>\r\n </b>\r\n</font>\r\n</a>\r\n<font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\"><b><small>/&nbsp; </small>\r\n</b>\r\n</font>\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/0312244614/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy from Amazon.co.uk</small>\r\n </font>\r\n</a>\r\n</small>\r\n</b>\r\n</font>\r\n</span>\r\n&nbsp; </p>\r\n</font>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr><td valign=\"top\" align=\"center\" width=\"50%\"><strong><font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\">&nbsp;</font>\r\n </strong>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" align=\"center\" width=\"50%\"><font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\" size=\"-1\">&nbsp;</font>\r\n </td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr><td valign=\"top\" align=\"center\" width=\"50%\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0px 0px\"><b><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1558683038/bohemicacom\">Culture Shock: Czech Republic</a>\r\n &nbsp;</b>\r\n <br />\r\n<font color=\"#800000\">byTim Nollen </font>\r\n- <span lang=\"EN-US\">Part ofwell-known series. Provides much useful and accurate information. Sometimes theaccount is a little too one sided. Slightly dated in some practical matters, most notably housing.&nbsp;<br />\r\n</span>\r\n<a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1558683038/bohemicacom\"><img height=\"150\" alt=\"Culture Shock! Czech Republic\" src=\"images/bookstore/cultureshock.jpg\" width=\"100\" border=\"0\" />\r\n </a>\r\n</p>\r\n<p class=\"NormalFirst\" style=\"MARGIN: 0cm 0px 0px\"><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1558683038/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small>Buy from Amazon.com</small>\r\n </b>\r\n</font>\r\n</a>\r\n</small>\r\n</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" align=\"center\" width=\"50%\"><p align=\"center\">&nbsp; <strong><font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\"><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1892975025/bohemicacom\">Czech & Slovak Republics Guide : Be a Traveler - Not a Tourist</a>\r\n </font>\r\n</strong>\r\n<font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\" size=\"-1\"><br />\r\n</font>\r\n<font color=\"#990033\">by Ted Brewer (1999)</font>\r\n </p>\r\n<p align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1892975025/bohemicacomwww.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1892975025/bohemicacomwww.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1892975025/bohemicacom\"><img height=\"140\" hspace=\"5\" src=\"http://images.amazon.com/images/P/1892975025.01.MZZZZZZZ.gif\" width=\"90\" vspace=\"3\" border=\"1\" />\r\n </a>\r\n</p>\r\n<p align=\"center\"><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1892975025/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small>Buy from Amazon.com</small>\r\n </b>\r\n</font>\r\n</a>\r\n</small>\r\n<font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\"><b><small>/&nbsp; </small>\r\n</b>\r\n</font>\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/1892975025/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy from Amazon.co.uk</small>\r\n </font>\r\n</a>\r\n</small>\r\n</b>\r\n</font>\r\n</span>\r\n</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr><td valign=\"top\" align=\"center\" width=\"50%\"></td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" align=\"center\" width=\"50%\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr><td valign=\"top\" align=\"center\" width=\"50%\">&nbsp;<strong><font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\"><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0822518791/bohemicacom\">Czech Republic...in Pictures (Visual Geography)</a>\r\n </font>\r\n</strong>\r\n<br />\r\n<p><font color=\"#990033\">(1995)<br />\r\nLerner Publications Company</font>\r\n </p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0px 0px\">&nbsp;<a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0822518791/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small><small>Buy from Amazon.com</small>\r\n </small>\r\n</b>\r\n</font>\r\n</a>\r\n<font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\"><b><small>/&nbsp; </small>\r\n</b>\r\n</font>\r\n<span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/0822518791/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy from Amazon.co.uk</small>\r\n </font>\r\n</a>\r\n</small>\r\n</b>\r\n</font>\r\n</span>\r\n</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" align=\"center\" width=\"50%\"><b><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/186034075X/bohemicacom\">Customsand Ettiquette in the Czech Republic</a>\r\n </b>\r\n<b style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal\"><span lang=\"CS\" style=\"mso-ansi-language: CS\"><br />\r\n</span>\r\n</b>\r\n<font color=\"#800000\">by David Short&nbsp;</font>\r\n <span lang=\"EN-US\"><br />\r\nExcellent introduction to Czech manners and habits. Friendly, pocket-sized books to get you started. Slightly dated in some practical matters.&nbsp;&nbsp;<small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/186034075X/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small><br />\r\nBuy from Amazon.com</small>\r\n </b>\r\n</font>\r\n</a>\r\n</small>\r\n<font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\"><small>/&nbsp; </small>\r\n</font>\r\n<small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/186034075X/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy from Amazon.co.uk</small>\r\n </font>\r\n</a>\r\n</small>\r\n</small>\r\n</b>\r\n</font>\r\n</span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr><td valign=\"top\" align=\"center\" width=\"50%\"><b>&nbsp;</b>\r\n </td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" align=\"center\" width=\"50%\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><b><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small><small><small>&nbsp;</small>\r\n </small>\r\n</small>\r\n</font>\r\n</b>\r\n</span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr><td valign=\"top\" align=\"center\" width=\"50%\"><p align=\"left\">Several books available in Prague are also of interest:</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0px 0px\" align=\"left\"><b style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal\"><i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">EveryDay Prague</span>\r\n </i>\r\n</b>\r\n</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"MARGIN: 0cm 0px 0px\" align=\"left\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Listings of services in various categories. Comes with a useful discount card.</span>\r\n </p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td valign=\"top\" align=\"center\" width=\"50%\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0px 0px\" align=\"left\"><b style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal\"><i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Prague PhoneBook</span>\r\n </i>\r\n</b>\r\n</p>\r\n<p class=\"NormalFirst\" style=\"MARGIN: 0cm 0px 0px\" align=\"left\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Expat oriented phonebook and yellow pages.</span>\r\n </p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"MARGIN: 6pt 0px 0px\" align=\"left\"><b style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal\"><i style=\"mso-bidi-font-style: normal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Czech Republic Business Guide</span>\r\n </i>\r\n</b>\r\n</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"MARGIN: 0cm 0px 0px\" align=\"left\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Collection of practical advise for all expatriates with relevant listings in many categories. Published annually.</span>\r\n </p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n', 36, 0, 1),
(25, '', 'This\r\n      section will hopefully grow, as more books become available to purchase\r\n      online. Currently only books in English available on either Amazon.com or\r\n      Amazon.co.uk are listed. It covers most of  the major names of Czech\r\n      linguistics both current and from the first part of the century. Go\r\n      to the <a href=\"../plk/index.htm\">Linguistics section of Bohemica.com</a>\r\n      for more information about the Prague Linguistic Circle.</p>\r\n      <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-top: 0cm; margin-bottom: 0\"> </p>\r\n      <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-top: 0cm; margin-bottom: 0\"><b><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/9027215146/bohemicacom0d\">Some\r\n      Basic and Less Known Aspects of the Prague Linguistic School<br>\r\n      </a></b><font color=\"#990033\">Josef\r\n      Vachek (Editor), Philip\r\n      Luelsdorff (Introduction)<font face=\"geneva, arial, helvetica\" size=\"2\"> </font>(1983)\r\n      </font>Collection of Czech linguistic writings compiled by one of\r\n      the  younger members of the Prague Linguistic Circle.<b><font face=\"geneva, arial, helvetica\" size=\"-1\"><br>\r\n              <span lang=\"EN-US\"><small><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/9027215146/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy\r\n              from Amazon.co.uk</small></font></a></font></small></span></font><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\"><small><small>\r\n      /  </small></small></font></span></b><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/9027215146/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small><small>Buy\r\n      from Amazon.com</small></small></font></a></b></font></span></p>\r\n      <p><b><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0686226097/bohemicacom\">Selected Writings in English\r\n      and General Linguistics<br>\r\n      </a></b>\r\n      <font color=\"#990033\">\r\n      by Josef\r\n      Vachek (1976)</font> A collection of writings of one of the most important\r\n      members of the Prague linguistic circle.\r\n      <font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\" size=\"2\"><br>\r\n      </font><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\"><b><small> </small></b></font><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0686226097/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small><small>Buy\r\n      from Amazon.com</small></small></font></a><small><small>  </small></small></b></font></span><p>\r\n    <b><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/9027930775/bohemicacom\">A Functional Analysis of\r\n        Present Day English on a General Linguistic Basis</a></b><font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\" size=\"-1\"><br>\r\n    </font>\r\n      <font color=\"#990033\">\r\n        by Vilém\r\n        Mathesius (1975) </font>An important book by the founder of the Prague\r\n      linguistic school. <font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\" size=\"-1\"><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/9027930775/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small><br>\r\n      Buy\r\n        from Amazon.com</small></b></font></a>\r\n        </font><p><b><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/9027931488/bohemicacom\">Selected Papers in\r\n        Structural Linguistics : Contributions to English and General\r\n        Linguistics Written in the Years 1928-1978</a></b><font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\" size=\"-1\"><br>\r\n    </font>\r\n    <font color=\"#990033\">\r\n        by Bohumil\r\n        Trnka, Vilem\r\n        Fried (1982) </font>Writings of an important Czech functional linguist.<br>\r\n    <small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/9027931488/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small>Buy\r\n      from Amazon.com</small></b></font></a></small>\r\n    <p><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/9027254419/bohemicacom0d\"><b>Prague\r\n            Linguistic Circle Papers Vol 1: Travaux Du Cercle Linguistique De\r\n            Prague Nouvelle Serie <br>\r\n      </b></a><font color=\"#990033\">Eva Hajičová, Miroslav Červenka, Oldřich\r\n    Leka, Petr Sgall, Joseph\r\n            Vachek (Editors) (1995) </font><b><small><font face=\"geneva, arial, helvetica\" size=\"-1\"> \r\n    </font></small></b>Renewed series building on pre-war Travaux and other\r\n    publications from the 1960s. Contains articles by younger Czech\r\n    linguists. <b>\r\n <span lang=\"EN-US\"><small>\r\n <font face=\"geneva, arial, helvetica\" size=\"-1\"><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/9027254419/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small><br>\r\n Buy\r\n                    from Amazon.co.uk</small></font></a></font></small><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\"><small><small> </small></small></font></span></b>\r\n      <p><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/9027220646/bohemicacom0d\"><b>Written\r\n            Language Revisited<br>\r\n      </b></a><font color=\"#990033\">Josef Vachek, Philip\r\n            A. Luelsdorff (Editor) (1989)<b>\r\n                    </b></font>Collection of papers from a conference on written\r\n      language.<font face=\"geneva, arial, helvetica\" size=\"-1\"><b>\r\n      <small><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/9027220646/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small><br>\r\n      Buy\r\n                    from Amazon.co.uk</small></font></a></span>\r\n      </font></small>\r\n                    </b></p>\r\n            </font>\r\n      <p><b><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/9027215480/bohemicacom0d\">Variation\r\n            in Language</a></b><br>\r\n      <font color=\"#990033\">\r\n      Petr\r\n            Sgall, Jiri\r\n            Hronek, Alexandr\r\n            Stich, Jan\r\n            Horecky (1992) </font>An essential book both for understanding the\r\n      dual (diglossic) nature of Czech (i.e. coexistence of literary and common\r\n      Czech) as well as diglossia in general.<span lang=\"EN-US\"><b><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/9027215480/bohemicacom0d\"><small> <font face=\"geneva, arial, helvetica\" size=\"-1\"><small><br>\r\n      Buy\r\n                    from Amazon.co.uk\r\n      </small>\r\n            </font></small></a>\r\n      </font></b></span></p>\r\n      <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-top: 6.0pt; margin-bottom: 0\"><b><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/9027718385/bohemicacom0d\">The\r\n      Meaning of the Sentence in Its Semantic and Pragmatic Aspects</a></b><br>\r\n      <font color=\"#990033\">\r\n      Petr Sgall, Eva Hajičová, Jarmila Panevová, Jjacob\r\n      L. Mey (1986)</font> An essential book outlining the work of the new\r\n      school of Prague linguistics, namely the functional sentence perspective. <font face=\"geneva, arial, helvetica\" size=\"-1\"><b>\r\n              <small>\r\n              <font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\"><br>\r\n              </font></small>\r\n              </b>\r\n      </font>\r\n      <small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/9027718385/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small>Buy\r\n      from Amazon.com</small></b></font></a></small>\r\n      <span lang=\"EN-US\"><b><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\"><small><small>\r\n      / </small></small></font></b></span> <font face=\"geneva, arial, helvetica\" size=\"-1\"><b>\r\n              <span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/9027718385/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy\r\n              from Amazon.co.uk</small></font></a></small></font></span>\r\n              </b></p>\r\n      </font>\r\n      <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-top: 6.0pt; margin-bottom: 0\"> </p>\r\n      <b><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/9027221464/bohemicacom0d\">Discourse\r\n      and Meaning,\r\n      Papers in Honor of Eva Hajičová</a></b><font face=\"geneva, arial, helvetica\" size=\"-1\"><br>\r\n      </font><font color=\"#990033\">Barbara Partee, Petr\r\n      Sgall (Editors)<font face=\"geneva, arial, helvetica\" size=\"-1\"> </font>(1995)</font><font face=\"geneva, arial, helvetica\" size=\"-1\"><b><br>\r\n              <span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/9027221464/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy\r\n              from Amazon.co.uk</small></font></a></small></font></span>\r\n              </b>\r\n      </font>\r\n      <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-top: 6.0pt; margin-bottom: 0\"> </p>\r\n      <b><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/0792352890/bohemicacom0d\">Topic-focus\r\n      Articulation, Tripartite Structures, and Semantic Content</a><br>\r\n      </b><font color=\"#990033\">Eva Hajičová, Barbara\r\n      H. Partee (1998) </font> <font face=\"geneva, arial, helvetica\" size=\"-1\"><b><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/0792352890/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small><br>\r\n      Buy\r\n              from Amazon.co.uk</small></font></a></small></font></span>\r\n              </b></font>\r\n      <p>Two books elaborating on the new trends in Prague linguistics.</p>\r\n      <p><b><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/3110126729/bohemicacom\">Geography\r\n      of Case Semantics</a><br>\r\n      </b><font color=\"#990033\">Laura\r\n      A. Janda (1993) </font>Using the dative in Czech and \r\ninstrumental in\r\n      Russian as case studies for an exploration in cognitive grammar.<small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/3110126729/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small><br>\r\n      Buy\r\n      from Amazon.com</small></b></font></a><b><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\">\r\n      / </font></b></small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/3110126729/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\"><small>\r\n      </small></font></small></b></font></a><small><small><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/3110126729/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy\r\n      from Amazon.co.uk</small></font></a></b></font></span></small></small>\r\n      <p>\r\n      <b><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/3110151545/bohemicacom0d\">Contact\r\n      Linguistics Vol 2</a></b>\r\n      <font face=\"geneva, arial, helvetica\" size=\"-1\"><br>\r\n      </font>\r\n      <font color=\"#990033\">\r\n      Hans Goebl, Peter\r\n      H. Nelde, Zdeněk Starý, Wolfgang\r\n      Wolck (Editors) (1997)</font> An important collection of papers on\r\n      different aspects of the linguistic situation in Central and Eastern\r\n      Europe. Co-edited by a Czech linguist Zdeněk Starý.<br>\r\n      <small><small><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/3110151545/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy\r\n      from Amazon.co.uk</small></font></a></b></font></span></small></small></p>\r\n      <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-top: 6.0pt; margin-bottom: 0\"><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/0903425432/bohemicacom0d\"><b>Essays in Czech and Slovak Language and Literature, SSEES\r\n      Occasional Papers</b></a><font FACE=\"Arial\" COLOR=\"#000000\"><b><i><br>\r\n      </i></b></font><font color=\"#990033\">by David Short (1996)  </font><font FACE=\"Arial\" COLOR=\"#000000\">Contains articles on a variety of interesting subjects from\r\n      grammar to literature. Important reading for Slavists.</font><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0903425432/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small><small><br>\r\n      </small></small></b></font>\r\n      </a><small><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><b><font face=\"geneva, arial, helvetica\" size=\"-1\"><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/0903425432/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy\r\n              from Amazon.co.uk</small></font></a></font></b></span></font></small> \r\n      </p>\r\n      <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-top: 6.0pt; margin-bottom: 0\"> \r\n      </p>\r\n      <p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left: 0; margin-right: 0; margin-top: 6.0pt; margin-bottom: 0\"><b><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/089357211X/bohemicacom\">Description\r\n              of Spoken Prague Czech</a></b><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/089357211X/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\" size=\"-1\"><br>\r\n      </font>\r\n      </a><font color=\"#990033\">\r\n              by Charles\r\n              E. Townsend (1990) </font>The name says it all. Important to\r\n      Slavists.<br>\r\n      <small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/089357211X/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small>Buy\r\n      from Amazon.com</small></b></font></a><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small></b></font></small><b><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\">\r\n      / </font></b></small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/089357211X/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\"><small>\r\n      </small></font></small></b></font></a><small><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small><b><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/089357211X/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy\r\n      from Amazon.co.uk</small></font></a></b></small></font></span></small>\r\n      </p>\r\n    <p><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0262200961/bohemicacom\"><b>The Magic of a Common\r\n        Language : Jakobson, Mathesius, Trubetzkoy, and the Prague Linguistic\r\n        Circle (Current Studies in Linguistics, No 26)\r\n    </b>\r\n    </a><b><br>\r\n    </b>\r\n    <font color=\"#990033\">\r\n        by Jindřich\r\n        Toman (1995) </font>A new look at the Prague Linguistic Circle by a\r\n    Czech linguist living in the US. Good to read in conjunction with some of\r\n    the books by Josef Vachek or a Czech book by Zdeněk Starý.<font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\" size=\"-1\"><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0262200961/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small><br>\r\n    Buy\r\n        from Amazon.com</small></b></font></a>\r\n        </font><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\"><b><small> <small>/ \r\n    </small><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/0262200961/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy\r\n        from Amazon.co.uk</small></font></a></small></font></span></small></b></font>\r\n    <p><b><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0674635361/bohemicacom\">On Language</a><br>\r\n    </b><font color=\"#990033\">\r\n        by Roman Jakobson, Linda\r\n        R. Waugh (Editor), Monique\r\n        Monville-Burston (Editor) (1995)  </font>Collection of linguistic\r\n    writings by arguably the greatest linguist of all time. Although Jakobson\r\n    was Russian by origin he seriously started his career in Prague in the late\r\n    1920s and is often associated with the Prague school although he moved to\r\n    the US after WWII and successfully continued his career there.<a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/0674635361/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\" size=\"-1\"><small><b><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><br>\r\n    Buy\r\n        from Amazon.com</font></b></small></font></a><font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\" size=\"-1\">\r\n    </font><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\" size=\"-1\"><b><small> <small>/ \r\n    </small><span lang=\"EN-US\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small><a href=\"http://www.amazon.co.uk/exec/obidos/ASIN/0674635361/bohemicacom0d\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><small>Buy\r\n        from Amazon.co.uk</small></font></a></small></font></span></small></b></font>\r\n    <p><b><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/902793178X/bohemicacom\">Selected\r\n                Writings</a><br>\r\n    </b><font color=\"#990033\">\r\n                by Roman\r\n                Jakobson (1982)</font>  A more complete collection of\r\n    Jakobson\'s extensive writings.<br>\r\n    <font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\" size=\"-1\"><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/902793178X/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small>Buy\r\n                from Amazon.com</small></b></font></a>\r\n                </font><p><a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1556192673/bohemicacom\"><b>The\r\n                Syntax of Sentence and Text : A Festschrift for Frantisek Dane\r\n                (Linguistic and Literary Studies in Eastern Europe, Vol 42)</b></a><font face=\"verdana,arial,helvetica\" size=\"-1\"><br>\r\n    </font><font color=\"#990033\">\r\n                by Svetla Čmejrková, Frantisek tícha (Editor) (1994) </font>Another\r\n    collection of articles from Czech linguists. This one reflects another\r\n    strand of current Czech linguistic thought which builds on the original\r\n    Prague Linguistic Circle.<br>\r\n    <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/exec/obidos/ASIN/1556192673/bohemicacom\"><font face=\"Arial\" color=\"#990000\"><b><small><small>Buy\r\n      from Amazon.com</small></small></b></font></a>\r\n', 35, 0, 1),
(32, 'Czech Keyboard', '\r\nHow to install it and use it. Plus other information about Czech and the computer. <a href=\"/index.php?m=catalog&s=78\">Available here!</a>', 3, 1, 30),
